(308,	1247,	'Mark Catoe',	'benritmato@mac.com',	'https://markcatoe.posterous.com/',	'74.235.191.174',	'2011-01-20 18:53:41',	'2011-01-21 02:53:41',	'Hey Doron, \r\n\r\nI noticed the last two podcast episodes in iTunes had no dates. So they ended up below the other episodes from your feed, and they didn\'t automatically download or refresh. Don\'t know if that\'s anything you have control over or if it\'s an issue on my computer. \r\n\r\nI\'ve been enjoying the podcasts and website so far. \r\nKeep up the good work! \r\n\r\nMark',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X 10_5_8; en-us) AppleWebKit/533.19.4 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.0.3 Safari/533.19.4',	'',	0,	0),
(309,	1247,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'98.151.2.254',	'2011-01-20 22:19:45',	'2011-01-21 06:19:45',	'Hello Mark,\r\n\r\nYou\'re right, my apologies about that. I\'m still learning the basics about podcasting, so thanks for bearing with me on this! I am excited about the podcast airing two weeks from now with Walt Weiskopf.\r\n\r\nAt any rate, thanks so much for the kind words, it\'s inspiring to hear and truly does mean a lot.\r\n\r\nAll the best,\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_5; en-US) AppleWebKit/534.10 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/8.0.552.237 Safari/534.10',	'',	308,	1),
(313,	1031,	'Evan Tate',	'evan@evantate.com',	'',	'85.176.224.10',	'2011-01-29 01:20:57',	'2011-01-29 07:20:57',	'This is an exercise that I use as well. I first learned this from Joe Allard. He also added some major extensions on this exercise over the years. The exercise also involves a technique for making the embouchure more flexible, but that can only be demonstrated per video. I hope to get around to submitting my version with video to the site.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_6; en-US) AppleWebKit/534.10 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/8.0.552.237 Safari/534.10',	'',	0,	0),
(314,	1031,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'98.151.2.254',	'2011-01-29 15:22:11',	'2011-01-29 23:22:11',	'Joe Allard\'s the MAN! And yes, I\'d love to see the exercise you\'re talking about.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_5; en-US) AppleWebKit/534.10 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/8.0.552.237 Safari/534.10',	'',	313,	1),
(316,	756,	'Back on the Sax Part 3: Practicing Overtones | Best. Saxophone. Website. Ever.',	'',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//back-on-the-sax-part-3-practicing-overtones/',	'69.89.25.172',	'2011-01-30 17:39:42',	'2011-01-31 01:39:42',	'[...] yes, I know, I&#8217;ve been droning on and on about overtones lately. But I&#8217;ve really been having a good time practicing the exercises from part 3 of the Intro to [...]',	0,	'1',	'The Incutio XML-RPC PHP Library -- WordPress/3.0.4',	'pingback',	0,	0),
(318,	1490,	'Bret Pimentel',	'bpimentel+wordpress@gmail.com',	'https://www.bretpimentel.com',	'209.147.243.180',	'2011-01-31 15:48:20',	'2011-01-31 23:48:20',	'I\'m a big fan of mouthpiece pitch exercises--I do them frequently, and require them of my saxophone students.\r\n\r\nIt\'s worth pointing out that there is some disagreement about which pitches are the \"right\" ones. I like soprano C, alto A, tenor G, and baritone D. I\'ve also often heard people recommend F-sharp for tenor. And I\'ve heard people recommend a set of pitches for \"classical\" setups, and a lower set for \"jazz.\"\r\n\r\nI think these kinds of exercises are especially vital for saxophone. For clarinet, I play at pretty much the upper limit of my voicing, and for flute and double reeds I play at pretty much the lower limit. But the saxophones need to be voiced at specific points in between, and it\'s like shooting in the dark if your mouthpiece pitch isn\'t carefully habituated.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 5.1; en-US) AppleWebKit/534.10 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/8.0.552.237 Safari/534.10',	'',	0,	0),
(319,	1490,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'98.151.2.254',	'2011-01-31 21:26:45',	'2011-02-01 05:26:45',	'That\'s a great point you bring up Bret! It does seem like there\'s some difference of opinion with regards to whether or not certain pitches are the \"right\" ones when playing on the various saxophones, but it makes sense that you practice whatever gets you the best results. These are simply helpful guidelines just to get people in the practice of aiming for a certain notes and then hitting them. \r\n\r\nThanks!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_5; en-US) AppleWebKit/534.10 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/8.0.552.237 Safari/534.10',	'',	318,	1),
(320,	423,	'Ken Ball',	'kball_uk@mac.com',	'',	'80.73.218.41',	'2011-02-01 09:10:20',	'2011-02-01 17:10:20',	'Hi Doron,\r\n\r\nI found your long tone files a great help on both alto and tenor, but was wondering if you had a midi file of the mp3 file so that I can feed it to my keyboard for playback?\r\n\r\nThanks, and I am enjoying your site from across the ocean.....',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_6; en-us) AppleWebKit/533.19.4 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.0.3 Safari/533.19.4',	'',	0,	0),
(321,	423,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'98.151.2.254',	'2011-02-01 21:56:48',	'2011-02-02 05:56:48',	'Hello Ken,\r\n\r\nA MIDI file sounds like a good idea. I went ahead and updated this post so that there\'s a MIDI download as well. \r\n\r\nGlad that you\'re enjoying the site from the other side of the world, all the best from Los Angeles!\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_5; en-US) AppleWebKit/534.10 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/8.0.552.237 Safari/534.10',	'',	320,	1),
(322,	1200,	'Jeff Rzepiela',	'scooby@scooby-sax.com',	'https://www.scooby-sax.com',	'76.245.44.254',	'2011-02-01 22:38:34',	'2011-02-02 06:38:34',	'Nice interview with a great player and educator!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 8.0; Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/4.0; GTB6.6; SLCC2; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 3.5.30729; .NET CLR 3.0.30729; Media Center PC 6.0; eMusic DLM/4; .NET4.0C)',	'',	0,	0),
