(344,	1596,	'Rick Hirsch',	'rick@hirschmusic.com',	'http://www.hirschmusic.com',	'68.232.115.161',	'2011-02-07 19:17:10',	'2011-02-08 01:17:10',	'Doron,\r\n\r\nI\'m with the don\'t-curl-lip-over-teeth school, too.\r\nHave you seen my vids about natural embouchure?\r\n\r\nsee ya!\r\n~Rick',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X 10_5_8; en-us) AppleWebKit/533.19.4 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.0.3 Safari/533.19.4',	'',	0,	0),
(345,	1596,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'98.151.2.254',	'2011-02-07 21:36:42',	'2011-02-08 05:36:42',	'Hey there Rick,\r\n\r\nI\'d love to see your videos about natural embouchure, can you please leave a comment with the URL(s)?\r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_5; en-US) AppleWebKit/534.10 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/8.0.552.237 Safari/534.10',	'',	344,	1),
(347,	1596,	'Rick Hirsch',	'rick@hirschmusic.com',	'http://www.hirschmusic.com',	'68.232.115.161',	'2011-02-08 06:45:40',	'2011-02-08 12:45:40',	'Sure. It\'s divided into three videos:\r\nNatural Embouchure Part 1: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P0IijB7gxPg\r\nNatural Embouchure Part 2: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ib9rhuk9HXs\r\nHow Much Mouthpiece: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zU5gIhwc5Qo\r\n\r\nHere\'s what Phil Barone had to say about them:\r\n\r\n\"This is a really great post and video. I\'ve been saying this for years and is what Joe Allard taught me. I\'ve also been telling all of my customers the same thing and you\'d be really surprised how many players don\'t take in enough mouthpiece. But after all, who teaches how much mouthpiece to take in your mouth? It\'s really easy to just not do it. The problem is getting past that initial period when it doesn\'t sound very good; it takes a couple of days at the most before it starts to sound normal; before that it sounds crass. I know some people don\'t agree with this. Also, check out photos of Trane and sonny Rollins playing, they eat the mouthpiece. \"\r\n\r\nThis may not work for everybody.  But, as a rule, it seems sensible that instrumentalists should always try the most physically natural and comfortable approach to playing, as our individual bodies dictate.\r\n\r\nsincerely,\r\n~ Rick',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X 10_5_8; en-us) AppleWebKit/533.19.4 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.0.3 Safari/533.19.4',	'',	0,	0),
(348,	1247,	'Jordan',	'jwosnick@gmail.com',	'',	'13.12.254.95',	'2011-02-08 07:27:42',	'2011-02-08 15:27:42',	'Quite a player! Thanks for the Youtube link and a great website.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 6.1; en-US) AppleWebKit/534.13 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/9.0.597.84 Safari/534.13',	'',	0,	0),
(349,	1247,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'38.106.61.196',	'2011-02-08 13:04:12',	'2011-02-08 21:04:12',	'Yeah, Adam is definitely a force to be reckoned with! Thanks so much for the kudos on the site, it really means a lot to me that people are getting something positive from it. \r\n\r\nBest wishes,\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; U; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_5; en-US) AppleWebKit/534.10 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/8.0.552.237 Safari/534.10',	'',	348,	1),
