(565,	2135,	'Bret Pimentel',	'bpimentel+wordpress@gmail.com',	'https://www.bretpimentel.com',	'209.147.242.1',	'2011-05-16 06:51:11',	'2011-05-16 13:51:11',	'+1 on using the Taffanel/Gaubert on saxophone. I like those especially for working out awkwardness up in the palm keys and down in the LH table.\r\n\r\nI also like to use the \"68 Exercises of Mechanism\" from the Klosé clarinet method on multiple instruments (I believe the Universal Method for saxophone has an appropriately-transposed version of these).',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1) AppleWebKit/534.24 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/11.0.696.65 Safari/534.24',	'',	0,	0),
