(973,	1797,	'Altissimo the Easy Way | Best. Saxophone. Website. Ever.',	'',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//altissimo-the-easy-way/',	'69.89.25.172',	'2011-09-06 06:02:40',	'2011-09-06 13:02:40',	'[...] 11 Tips for Improving Your Altissimo [...]',	0,	'1',	'The Incutio XML-RPC PHP Library -- WordPress/3.2.1',	'pingback',	0,	0),
(974,	1382,	'barisax1',	'refchef@gmail.com',	'',	'70.180.36.52',	'2011-09-06 06:59:47',	'2011-09-06 13:59:47',	'I\'ve been using Rico Royal #4s (on bari) for 30 years.  For the money, they\'re the best.  I always get about half a box of usable reeds and there\'s generally one or two that are really good.  Plus -- I don\'t have time to work on my reeds anymore, so Rico Royals make my playing life much easier.\r\n\r\nThey aren\'t the best reeds on Earth, but they do their job.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.7; rv:6.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/6.0.1',	'',	0,	0),
(975,	2385,	'barisax1',	'refchef@gmail.com',	'',	'70.180.36.52',	'2011-09-06 07:03:59',	'2011-09-06 14:03:59',	'Back in the day, when I was in school and playing legit, I used Vandoren #5s on alto and bari.  The cane was high quality and close grained and the #5 made a great blank to work from. The only drawback for me was that I could only get a very few practice reeds from most boxes.  The really great reed was rare -- but when I got one, it was truly great and lasted awhile as long as I took care of it.  I never found a reed brand I liked better than Vandoren.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.7; rv:6.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/6.0.1',	'',	0,	0),
