(1347,	3066,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2011-11-29 10:02:51',	'2011-11-29 18:02:51',	'Yeah, it pretty much sucked, so glad I unloaded that thing - lucky that Oleg let me do it since I bought it from him and traded in for another one of his horns.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	1343,	1),
(1349,	1278,	'james springer',	'jfs75@hotmail.co.uk',	'',	'86.150.228.115',	'2011-11-29 14:21:44',	'2011-11-29 22:21:44',	'java 2 reeds on V16 A5M mpc. ebonite. [alto sax]. rovner lig.\r\nvery good over 4 octave range. fat and lively.\r\nsoak for 2 hr , in warm water, before use.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 8.0; Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/4.0; GTB7.1; SLCC2; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 3.5.30729; .NET CLR 3.0.30729; Media Center PC 6.0; MDDC; InfoPath.2; .NET4.0C)',	'',	0,	0),
(1357,	3178,	'TenorMoxie',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'75.111.57.106',	'2011-12-01 11:41:47',	'2011-12-01 19:41:47',	'Lester Young was the daddy of ghosting using the half-tongue.  It was at the core of his classic style and he used it to swing in a way never heard before.  Lots of two or three note figures with the accents being shifted around.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows; U; Windows NT 6.0; en-US; rv:1.9.2.24) Gecko/20111103 Firefox/3.6.24 ( .NET CLR 3.5.30729; .NET4.0C)',	'',	0,	0),
(1358,	3178,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2011-12-01 11:45:01',	'2011-12-01 19:45:01',	'Yeah, I can definitely hear the half-tongue sound in his playing, really adds a lot of energy. He may very well be the father of the half-tongue! (sounds kind of funny when I put it that way).',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	1357,	1),
(1370,	270,	'Meluvsax',	'dee.ee@live.com.au',	'',	'58.170.152.148',	'2011-12-04 06:11:06',	'2011-12-04 14:11:06',	'I\'m actually doubling on alto and tenor now, they needed a second tenor for the jazz band at school.\r\n\r\nMy teacher was really happy that I was doing tenor :D\r\n\r\nI\'m also performing at our school\'s presentation ceremony tomorrow night so I\'m really excited',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	757,	0),
(1374,	270,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2011-12-04 13:01:23',	'2011-12-04 21:01:23',	'Very cool, best of luck with the performance!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	1370,	1),
(1380,	270,	'Meluvsax',	'dee.ee@live.com.au',	'',	'58.170.152.148',	'2011-12-05 06:31:04',	'2011-12-05 14:31:04',	'Thanks, and it went really great :D',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	1374,	0),
(1395,	3190,	'Jeff Rzepiela',	'scooby@scooby-sax.com',	'https://www.scooby-sax.com',	'76.232.11.109',	'2011-12-06 06:37:14',	'2011-12-06 14:37:14',	'Larry Teal\'s \"The Art of Saxophone Playing\" recommended soaking in hydrogen peroxide. I\'m not sure I\'d soak overnight like he recommends -- a couple of minutes should be sufficient, followed by a water rinse.\r\n\r\nThis wikipedia article has some additional comments about reeds, bacteria, etc. :\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wooden_reed_care',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; MSIE 9.0; Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/5.0)',	'',	0,	0),
(1396,	3190,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2011-12-06 10:05:44',	'2011-12-06 18:05:44',	'Yeah, I read about the hydrogen peroxide. Seems weird to put that stuff in your mouth even though I\'m sure it\'s totally safe if you rinse the reed off afterwards.\r\n\r\nAnyhow, thanks for the Wikipedia article - who would have though that they\'d have a wiki page on reed care? (although I guess Wikipedia has a page on just about everything).',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	1395,	1),
(1397,	3190,	'Jeff Rzepiela',	'scooby@scooby-sax.com',	'https://www.scooby-sax.com',	'166.205.137.121',	'2011-12-06 11:27:10',	'2011-12-06 19:27:10',	'Hydrogen peroxide is a common ingredient in those teeth whitening rinses, etc. so there should be no issue with putting in your mouth (especially if the reed is rinsed)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 5_0_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/534.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.1 Mobile/9A405 Safari/7534.48.3',	'',	1396,	0),
(1399,	3190,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2011-12-06 13:47:11',	'2011-12-06 21:47:11',	'Hmm, looks like someone here needs to learn a bit more about Hydrogen peroxide (hint, it\'s not you Jeff). \r\n\r\nI guess the name just sounds so toxic, but that\'s good to know, thanks for adding to the list!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	1397,	1),
(1402,	2751,	'Sarthak Therma',	'sarthak_guru@live.com',	'',	'124.41.229.51',	'2011-12-07 05:49:58',	'2011-12-07 13:49:58',	'I live in Nepal with almost no local saxophone player to look upto.Your site/articles/coverage and interviews has greatly helped me in my pursuit of learning this beautiful instrument. And this interview was really insightful sir.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	0,	0),
(1405,	2751,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2011-12-07 10:14:02',	'2011-12-07 18:14:02',	'Hello Sarthak,\r\n\r\nWow, how great it is to hear from someone in the beautiful country of Nepal! It\'s too bad to hear that there are no local players to look up to where you live. So I suppose it\'s up to you to be that player who everyone looks up to! \r\n\r\n:-)\r\n\r\nAt any rate, I am so happy to know that the site has helped you, it always means so much to get that sort of feedback. I hope that you\'ll continue to get a lot out of the site and please feel free to keep in touch via email or the comments hear to let me know what\'s new in your musical journey. \r\n\r\nAll the best,\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	1402,	1),
(1436,	507,	'Bill Plake',	'bplake@earthlink.net',	'https://billplakemusic.org',	'99.146.12.17',	'2011-12-09 13:54:30',	'2011-12-09 21:54:30',	'What a refreshing point of view! I remember the first time I heard Snoop, back in about \'92 or \'93. I was immediately struck by how distinctive he sounded, and particularly, his rhythmic trademark. A true original! The take home point here to me is to pursue our authentic self expression, whether on saxophone, or in life in general. To quote Monk, \"A man\'s a genius just for looking like himself.\" Snoop fits in well with that description. Thanks, Doron.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/534.51.22 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.1.1 Safari/534.51.22',	'',	0,	0),
(1444,	507,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2011-12-09 22:24:31',	'2011-12-10 06:24:31',	'Hey Bill, so glad you liked it! For us instrumentalists in particular, it\'s easy to let our authentic voices get lost in the quest to \"sound good,\" so this article is a little reminder to myself to, as we say in the hood (HA!), \"keep it real.\" \r\n\r\n:-)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	1436,	1),
(1477,	3205,	'Brad Carman',	'carman.music@gmail.com',	'https://bradcarmanmusic.com',	'184.60.15.186',	'2011-12-12 08:31:37',	'2011-12-12 16:31:37',	'Great article!!  \r\n\r\nI have one other suggestion which works great for punching middle D\'s (short, accented notes) or for longer sustained pitches when a brighter or louder sound is required or desired.  \r\n\r\nSimply leave your thumb off of the \"octave\" key and put down the \"high\" D key as a kind of alternate octave key. (Then adjust for pitch if necessary)\r\n\r\nI use this fingering with my Yanagisawa soprano (which tends to bark when I push or punch middle D - sounds great.) \r\n\r\nOk, I\'m off to fix my high A hiss!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0; rv:8.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/8.0',	'',	0,	0),
(1478,	3205,	'Dave Erato',	'david.erato@me.com',	'https://www.daviderato.com',	'72.135.234.73',	'2011-12-12 08:37:43',	'2011-12-12 16:37:43',	'Great article!!\r\n\r\nAnother alternate for middle D on tenor (not so much on alto) is to just use the palm D with no octave key.  It tone matches more with the lower register, so it\'s pretty good if you\'re not crossing registers.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_7_2) AppleWebKit/534.51.22 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.1.1 Safari/534.51.22',	'',	0,	0),
(1479,	3205,	'Brad Carman',	'carman.music@gmail.com',	'https://bradcarmanmusic.com',	'184.60.15.186',	'2011-12-12 08:49:37',	'2011-12-12 16:49:37',	'Readers, note: \r\n\r\nThis solution is slightly different than mine (above). One is the high D key ONLY, and the other is the regular middle D fingering with the high D key IN PLACE of the octave key. Both are good options to play around with! Try both options (and, of course those mentioned in the article) on all your different horns and see what you get.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0; rv:8.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/8.0',	'',	1478,	0),
(1480,	3205,	'Matt Stohrer',	'stohrermusic@gmail.cm',	'https://stohrermusic.com',	'174.252.153.126',	'2011-12-12 11:28:28',	'2011-12-12 19:28:28',	'Brad and Eric, thanks for reading and thank you for posting and making this article more informative with your comments!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.2; WOW64) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	0,	0),
(1657,	3205,	'TenorMoxie',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'75.111.32.122',	'2011-12-20 20:59:43',	'2011-12-21 04:59:43',	'Dave, thanks for being the guy who found the solution \"hiding in plain sight.\"  A large riser on the palm D key of a Conn 10M makes it surprisingly easy and fast to cross the octaves with that fingering (minimal knuckle motion).  Once I counteract years of muscle memory, I could see myself using the standard D2 fingering strictly as an alternate fingering.  The large riser also makes it much easier to go between D3 and front E/F without hitting the Eb key if you don\'t have large hands.  \r\n\r\nYou can make a key riser as big as you please using epoxy putty.  The practical limit on the height of the D riser is not causing difficulty with the palm Eb fingering.  Make the riser oversize and shape it to your needs with a Shur-form type wood rasp.  It\'s not the prettiest thing, but there\'s beauty in a horn that plays and sounds the best it can.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0; rv:8.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/8.0.1',	'',	1478,	0),
(1680,	3216,	'TenorMoxie',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'75.111.32.122',	'2011-12-21 15:59:53',	'2011-12-21 23:59:53',	'Do a Google search for saxophonistisches in any browser and there will be a \"translate this page\" link.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0; rv:8.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/8.0.1',	'',	0,	0),
(1694,	3216,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2011-12-22 13:59:52',	'2011-12-22 21:59:52',	'I just tried it in Safari and the translation didn\'t work, even when I was logged into my Gmail/Google account on that browser. So maybe it works on other browsers besides Chrome, but suffice it to say, there is indeed a nifty translate feature from Google that will certainly help. \r\n\r\nThanks for chiming in!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1680,	1),
(1775,	3228,	'Tobias Haecker',	'mail@saxophonistisches.de',	'http://saxophonistisches.de/',	'79.242.143.232',	'2011-12-27 11:58:16',	'2011-12-27 17:58:16',	'nice article.\r\n\r\nI for myself have littel \"ligature fetish\"\r\nhttps://saxophonistisches.de/der-grose-blattschraubenreport/\r\n\r\nYour know, that Francois Louis has also a Pure Brass Ligature. It\'s a bit different, more massiv and gives the tone more deep frequenzes and is more resonant.\r\n\r\nFurthermore there are different pressure plates for the FL. The normal, one with a rubber inlay and a heavy brass plate. The difference in sound is very notable.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	0,	0),
(1776,	3228,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'sollitt2@tcnj.edu',	'',	'174.48.220.169',	'2011-12-27 13:24:32',	'2011-12-27 21:24:32',	'I have heard of his new ligature, and do agree with you how changing the pressure plates can make a difference. I have tried the newest version of the Francois Louis ligature, and really liked it, but found it to be a bit expensive. None the less, it is a great ligature.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1775,	0),
(1778,	2732,	'Tobias Haecker',	'mail@saxophonistisches.de',	'http://saxophonistisches.de/',	'91.12.190.171',	'2011-12-27 14:06:20',	'2011-12-27 20:06:20',	'Liebman was also one of Allards pupils and in his book your personal saxophone sound shall be very influenced by allard.\r\n\r\nI got one of the rare copies of allards VHS in my hands and I put them on youtube.\r\n\r\nhttps://saxophonistisches.de/der-grose-blattschraubenreport/\r\n\r\nI would say, he says a lot of interessting things, but other things are more a personal view and others are just outdated.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	0,	0),
(1779,	2732,	'Tobias Haecker',	'mail@saxophonistisches.de',	'http://saxophonistisches.de/',	'91.12.190.171',	'2011-12-27 14:08:26',	'2011-12-27 20:08:26',	'oh, wrong link:\r\nhttps://saxophonistisches.de/joe-allard-the-master-speaks/',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1) AppleWebKit/535.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/15.0.874.121 Safari/535.2',	'',	1778,	0),
(1783,	2732,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2011-12-27 22:25:15',	'2011-12-28 06:25:15',	'Yes, Liebman\'s book is great! As for the videos, those are really cool as well, however, I\'ve heard that they do not represent Allard at his best, since he was starting to go into his Alzheimer\'s disease by the time those videos we made. \r\n\r\nThanks Tobias!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1779,	1),
(1823,	3141,	'Jason the Obscure',	'BFlat.harmonic@gmail.com',	'',	'99.27.201.173',	'2011-12-30 14:21:56',	'2011-12-30 22:21:56',	'Exit sign above the door.........I laughed out loud!\r\nGreat series of postings. Thanks.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	0,	0),
(1824,	3141,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2011-12-30 16:19:37',	'2011-12-31 00:19:37',	'Glad you enjoyed that! Hey, whatever works, right?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1823,	1),
(1825,	1130,	'Jason the Obscure',	'BFlat.harmonic@gmail.com',	'',	'99.27.201.173',	'2011-12-31 00:14:45',	'2011-12-31 08:14:45',	'Hi Doron,\r\nThanks for writing your article. I am getting around to reading more of your good site. Do you know whether the Oleg key enhancer they show for C (I never miss that key), could be flipped to the Eb next to it. My old 10M finds my finger slipping off and that just might work. Do you have one on your horn?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	0,	0),
(1827,	1130,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2011-12-31 11:40:35',	'2011-12-31 19:40:35',	'Hello Jason,\r\n\r\nI actually haven\'t had an experience with the Oleg key enhancer, but I would definitely give it a try if you are having trouble. Maybe find out if you can return it in the event that it doesn\'t work, but it seems like a great product for those horns that may not have been designed very ergonomically. \r\n\r\nWish I could be of more help, but I\'m so glad to hear that you\'re enjoying the site!\r\n\r\nAll the best,\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1825,	1),
(1828,	1130,	'Jason the Obscure',	'BFlat.harmonic@gmail.com',	'',	'99.27.201.173',	'2011-12-31 12:18:41',	'2011-12-31 20:18:41',	'Thanks. I\'ve used Oleg\'s \"highrise\" on my old Selmer SBA. I\'ve high regard for Oleg\'s work. Even have one of his mouthpieces. All of my neck straps are his too.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	0,	0),
(1907,	3247,	'Clayton',	'claytonduncan@gmail.com',	'',	'70.138.195.72',	'2012-01-05 17:06:19',	'2012-01-06 01:06:19',	'One of the exercises I use is to play High F above the staff and then a High E. Then finger High F using the Front F key and use your throat to bend the pitch down to the E you had just played. Then repeat for F to Eb. Play the interval using the real fingerings and then again using the Front F key and bending down using your throat. \r\n\r\nThis is similar to Sam\'s exercise in that you\'re bending down the pitch in increasingly larger intervals. It\'s just that instead of maintaining a single note while changing fingerings, you\'re changing notes while maintaining a single fingering.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0; rv:9.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/9.0.1',	'',	0,	0),
(1908,	3247,	'Clayton',	'claytonduncan@gmail.com',	'',	'70.138.195.72',	'2012-01-05 17:08:58',	'2012-01-06 01:08:58',	'Forgot to add that you just keep repeating the exercise, lowering the 2nd note a 1/2 step each time until you can\'t match it using the High F. For me, that\'s usually around G or F#.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0; rv:9.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/9.0.1',	'',	1907,	0),
(1909,	3247,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-05 17:29:19',	'2012-01-06 01:29:19',	'That\'s a great variation, definitely not easy by any stretch. Thanks for sharing that!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1908,	1),
(1911,	383,	'Bob',	'Bobsol3@aol.com',	'',	'74.71.206.232',	'2012-01-05 21:34:48',	'2012-01-06 05:34:48',	'I was Joe\'a first student in San Francisco, after he moved there. It was before he got onto the system as des robes here, where he taught an improvised solo. He taught some cool scale and. Boreal stuff. But he bugged with students comIng looking for licks and tricks. He was a giant soul and lonh may his music live!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 5_0_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/534.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.1 Mobile/9A405 Safari/7534.48.3',	'',	0,	0),
(1912,	383,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-05 23:04:07',	'2012-01-06 07:04:07',	'Wow, amazing that you got to study in-person with one of jazz history\'s greats! And yes, I can imagine how licks and tricks were far beneath what he had to offer students. \r\n\r\nThanks for sharing, Bob!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1911,	1),
(1913,	3247,	'Evan Tated',	'evan@evantate.com',	'http://www.evantatemusic.com',	'91.7.103.97',	'2012-01-05 23:53:04',	'2012-01-06 05:53:04',	'Hey Doron!\r\nJoe Allard , had a similar exercise. We would actually start on high A, then play G# and then go back to A. Then we\'d just finger A and bend the pitch down to G# and back to A. We\'d continue this chromatically until we\'d reach high F#. \r\nAfter that process was finished, we\'d expand the exercise to a whole step (A, G#, G, G#, A), then a minor third, major third, etc. \r\nJoe himself was able to perform this exercise to a perfect fifth! (I\'ve only managed a perfect fourth myself). \r\nThis exercise is especially great on soprano saxophone!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	0,	0),
(1915,	1490,	'Evan Tate',	'evan@evantate.com',	'http://www.evantatemusic.com',	'91.7.103.97',	'2012-01-06 00:02:15',	'2012-01-06 06:02:15',	'Hey Doron!\r\nI have a whole series of exercise like these that I got from Joe Allard. I need to rewrite them in a neat fashion. When I\"m done I\'d like to pass them on to you.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	0,	0),
(1919,	3247,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-06 08:38:45',	'2012-01-06 16:38:45',	'Sounds like a brass instrument warmup, definitely not easy. Between the article and your and Clayton\'s comments, we\'ve got an awesome pitch workout program right here on this page, thanks Evan!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1913,	1),
(1920,	1490,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-06 08:39:49',	'2012-01-06 16:39:49',	'Yes, please do, I\'d love to see them and possibly even share them on the site if that\'s OK. Thanks!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1915,	1),
(1921,	383,	'Bob',	'bobsol3@aol.com',	'',	'74.71.206.232',	'2012-01-06 09:43:27',	'2012-01-06 17:43:27',	'I must apologize for the errors in my previous post....\r\nit was late, the keyboard was small.....sorry...\r\n\r\nTo repeat, in English this time...I was Joe’s first student in San Francisco, after he moved there. It was before he got onto the system as described here, where he taught an improvised solo. He taught some cool scale and chordal stuff. But he got bugged with students coming looking for licks and tricks. He was a giant soul and long may his music live!\r\nIt was always a great hang with Joe, he asked me to help him with several projects that were amazing to be a part of.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 8.0; AOL 9.6; AOLBuild 4340.168; Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/4.0; SLCC2; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 3.5.30729; .NET CLR 3.0.30729; Media Center PC 6.0; HPNTDF; .NET4.0C)',	'',	0,	0),
(1922,	383,	'Bob',	'bobsol3@aol.com',	'',	'74.71.206.232',	'2012-01-06 09:43:57',	'2012-01-06 17:43:57',	'I must apologize for the errors in my previous post....\r\nit was late, the keyboard was small, it was late.....sorry...\r\n\r\nTo repeat, in English this time...I was Joe’s first student in San Francisco, after he moved there. It was before he got onto the system as described here, where he taught an improvised solo. He taught some cool scale and chordal stuff. But he got bugged with students coming looking for licks and tricks. He was a giant soul and long may his music live!\r\nIt was always a great hang with Joe, he asked me to help him with several projects that were amazing to be a part of.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 8.0; AOL 9.6; AOLBuild 4340.168; Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/4.0; SLCC2; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 3.5.30729; .NET CLR 3.0.30729; Media Center PC 6.0; HPNTDF; .NET4.0C)',	'',	0,	0),
(1923,	1712,	'Adam',	'adamrlee@gmail.com',	'',	'71.167.193.154',	'2012-01-06 10:20:41',	'2012-01-06 18:20:41',	'Your comment on the \"footballs\" in big band playing is not a characteristic of the music, it is a characteristic of lazy arrangers in a Sammy Nestico-ized arrangement world.  The bari in the Big Band era frequently mirrors the lead alto down the octave.  That means the bari\'s are playing the main theme!  Nothing boring or footballish about that.  Don\'t blame the music, blame the lazy arrangers.\r\n\r\nAdam\r\nBig Band Bari Player/Bandleader and loving it.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	0,	0),
(1927,	383,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-06 19:49:16',	'2012-01-07 03:49:16',	'Haha, I figured there was some auto-correct issue going on, but I got the basic gist of what you were saying.  Seems like he had his students on a pretty intense regiment with all of that heavy-duty ear training stuff.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1922,	1),
(1935,	2135,	'Chris Hubbard',	'jazzhubbard@gmail.com',	'',	'69.179.152.117',	'2012-01-09 15:28:03',	'2012-01-09 23:28:03',	'Reading this reminded me that I read how Branford Marsalis did this as well.  I may have to check this out.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:8.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/8.0.1',	'',	0,	0),
(1942,	2553,	'Evan Tate',	'evan@evantate.com',	'http://www.evantatemusic.com',	'78.51.135.253',	'2012-01-11 09:29:37',	'2012-01-11 15:29:37',	'Hey Doron! \r\n\r\nI bought the tuning CD via itunes and tried it out last night. Man, are those drones penetrant! After about 20 minutes I got stars before my eyes and a headache! But I will say that it\'s a good tool to use in concert with a tuning device, a piano and of course playing with musicians.\r\n\r\nPeace!\r\n\r\nEvan',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	0,	0),
(1943,	2553,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-11 09:49:18',	'2012-01-11 17:49:18',	'Hey there Evan!\r\n\r\nCool that you can get the CD on iTunes. I gotta get that thing myself, sounds like it really does the trick. \r\n\r\nThanks for sharing that!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1942,	1),
(1947,	805,	'predstave.net',	'',	'',	'208.43.239.39',	'2012-01-12 08:19:01',	'2012-01-12 14:19:01',	'<strong>A Ladies Guideline to Composing an Excellent Profile...</strong>\r\n\r\nOK…time has come. You have registered an internet relationship services or two. Now you must create that all-important profile… the one that will appeal to interest and fishing catch the man of your dreams… but where to start? Maybe writing is certainl...',	0,	'1',	'WordPress/3.2.1; https://predstave.net',	'trackback',	0,	0),
(1950,	85,	'Socrates De Jesus',	'socratesdejesusinc@yahoo.com',	'',	'74.88.255.236',	'2012-01-12 11:26:31',	'2012-01-12 19:26:31',	'Hey Doron,I\'ve playing house and soul music for a while i\'m based in New York city,if you need a sax player email me.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0; rv:9.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/9.0.1',	'',	0,	0),
(1951,	85,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-12 16:29:26',	'2012-01-13 00:29:26',	'Hello Socrates,\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, being that I\'m a sax player in Los Angeles and not a club promoter, I don\'t think that I\'d be of much help to you. If you can go out to some of those clubs and network with the promoters and DJs, or maybe just do it on Facebook and MySpace, then you have a decent shot at getting some of these gigs. \r\n\r\nBest of luck with it!\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1950,	1),
(1957,	1712,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-17 14:35:31',	'2012-01-17 22:35:31',	'I didn\'t write this article myself, but you bring up an interesting point. I think that there are a lot of cool ways to employ the bari in a big band setting, and sometimes those \"footballs\" sound really cool. In my opinion, it\'s about what\'s best for the music, not for the individual player. That said, I think it\'s important for arrangers to be creative in how they write their bari parts and not resort to the same old tired effects on every arrangement. \r\n\r\nThanks for chiming in Adam!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	1923,	1),
(1958,	1490,	'Autumn Towne',	'dazzlingglass@yahoo.com',	'',	'98.17.97.70',	'2012-01-18 19:37:38',	'2012-01-19 03:37:38',	'I am one of the few that can\'t whistle. Is there another analogy or image for positioning the tongue to change the pitch? Thanks.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1; rv:9.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/9.0.1',	'',	0,	0),
(1959,	1490,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-18 21:16:25',	'2012-01-19 05:16:25',	'Hello Autumn, \r\n\r\nThanks for your question! You don\'t actually have to be able to whistle to do this. In fact, I myself can\'t whistle. Unfortunately, there is no way (that I know of, at least) to describe the exact adjustments one must make in the inner mouth. I would start by experimenting with different placements of the tongue in relationship to the soft palate. You might also think of it in terms of vowel sounds such as \"eee\" or \"eww.\" Remember, this is not easy stuff and will definitely take some practice, so it\'s important to be patient with yourself here. But the rewards will be great if you persevere! \r\n\r\nI hope that helps,\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	1958,	1),
(1960,	1490,	'Evan Tate',	'evan@evantate.com',	'http://www.evantatemusic.com',	'78.51.173.103',	'2012-01-19 00:04:52',	'2012-01-19 06:04:52',	'As far as tongue position goes, I have my students just say the letter \"A\". This puts the tongue in a raise position in your mouth. You can then compare that to saxying \"Ahhh\" pr the word \"Law\". Notice your tongue position with those words. Try the words \"Low\", \"Lord\", \"Lee\", etc. \r\n\r\nIf you can\'t whistle this may be an alternative.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	0,	0),
(1961,	1490,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-19 08:31:23',	'2012-01-19 16:31:23',	'What you\'re proposing sounds great Evan. In the end, I think it just comes down to hearing the notes loud and clear in your mind and then letting the body find its way towards getting the notes to come out of the mouthpiece, and the tools you\'re offering help to facilitate that.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	1960,	1),
(1962,	928,	'andrew Fawcett',	'a.fawcett616@btinternet.com',	'',	'86.138.241.167',	'2012-01-19 09:31:31',	'2012-01-19 15:31:31',	'I vote for Sonny Side Up.  I have been listening to this on and off for about 50 years, and it never ceases to inspire me.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_5_8) AppleWebKit/534.50.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.0.6 Safari/533.22.3',	'',	0,	0),
(1963,	1490,	'Bret Pimentel',	'bpimentel+wordpress@gmail.com',	'https://bretpimentel.com/',	'209.147.246.68',	'2012-01-19 10:27:58',	'2012-01-19 18:27:58',	'I list a few alternative analogies here: https://bretpimentel.com/what-is-voicing/\r\n\r\nOne of my favorites is the idea of warm vs. cold air. I hope that helps.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.63 Safari/535.7',	'',	1958,	0),
(1965,	928,	'o',	'johncoltraneonline@googlemail.com',	'',	'87.78.138.176',	'2012-01-20 01:26:03',	'2012-01-20 09:26:03',	'how about this one with trane and mobley:\r\n\r\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Two_Tenors',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_7_2) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	0,	0),
(1966,	928,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-20 07:23:35',	'2012-01-20 15:23:35',	'Great album - but doesn\'t the trumpet not make it quite a \"saxophone blowing session?\" I mean we can\'t have trumpets coming in and mucking up the sonic landscape can we? ;)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	1962,	1),
(1967,	928,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-20 07:25:47',	'2012-01-20 15:25:47',	'Of course, you can never go wrong with those two! Pretty darn different playing styles between Trane and Mobley which makes it all the more rich of a listening experience.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	1965,	1),
(1968,	928,	'andrew Fawcett',	'a.fawcett616@btinternet.com',	'',	'86.138.241.167',	'2012-01-20 07:30:58',	'2012-01-20 13:30:58',	'ah, yes, but Dizzy doesn\'t start until after a dozen individual sax choruses plus I don\'t remember how many of fours and eights.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_5_8) AppleWebKit/534.50.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.0.6 Safari/533.22.3',	'',	1966,	0),
(1969,	928,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-20 07:57:14',	'2012-01-20 15:57:14',	'Well, someone here hasn\'t heard the album yet, have they...? OK, guilty as charged, will add it to my \"to check out\" list. :)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	1968,	1),
(1971,	928,	'andrew Fawcett',	'a.fawcett616@btinternet.com',	'',	'86.138.241.167',	'2012-01-20 09:59:47',	'2012-01-20 15:59:47',	'well, you MUST.  And there is a transcription of the tenor solos (Rollins and Stitt), (but not the trades).',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_5_8) AppleWebKit/534.50.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.0.6 Safari/533.22.3',	'',	1969,	0),
(1972,	928,	'andrew Fawcett',	'a.fawcett616@btinternet.com',	'',	'86.138.241.167',	'2012-01-20 10:00:55',	'2012-01-20 16:00:55',	'Sorry, I should have said, the tune is The Eternal Triangle, I got rhythm with an altered bridge....',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_5_8) AppleWebKit/534.50.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.0.6 Safari/533.22.3',	'',	1969,	0),
(1973,	928,	'Theotis',	'tedgomulka@hotmail.com',	'',	'192.172.14.99',	'2012-01-20 11:57:49',	'2012-01-20 19:57:49',	'\"Very Saxy\", an LP recorded in \'59. 4 tenors: Jaws/Buddy Tate/Coleman Hawkins/Arnett Cobb\r\nAlso Shirley Scott on B3!\r\nClassic wailin what really do belong on this list!\r\nPrestige 7167',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 7.0; Windows NT 6.0; SLCC1; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; InfoPath.2; MS-RTC LM 8; .NET CLR 3.5.30729; .NET CLR 3.0.30729)',	'',	0,	0),
(1974,	1763,	'Ray Beatty',	'sailing@hawaii.rr.com',	'',	'76.93.207.213',	'2012-01-20 18:11:42',	'2012-01-21 02:11:42',	'I also feel very fortunate to have had a lesson with Bob a few years ago while in LA.\r\nHeard him at the LA Jazz Institutes concert at the airport Marriot last Oct.\r\nHe has such a tasty touch.\r\ni really enjoy your website--keep em coming.\r\nRay',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/534.52.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.1.2 Safari/534.52.7',	'',	0,	0),
