(1988,	2589,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-23 08:09:36',	'2012-01-23 16:09:36',	'Yeah, I actually got to try some pro model P. Mauriat\'s at NAMM this past weekend. Great horns, and I imagine that Mauriat\'s high level of quality extends down into the more inexpensive instruments as well. \r\n\r\nThanks for sharing that!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	1986,	1),
(1993,	1031,	'Mark Ewert',	'funeralcounseling@gmail.com',	'',	'74.118.167.9',	'2012-01-24 13:27:54',	'2012-01-24 21:27:54',	'This is exciting- I have just started playing the Sax. Is this something I should practice now or should I wait?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; MSIE 9.0; Windows NT 6.1; Trident/5.0; BOIE9;ENUSMSNIP)',	'',	0,	0),
(1994,	196,	'David',	'dazadi_mx@yahoo.com.mx',	'',	'201.147.155.204',	'2012-01-24 13:40:31',	'2012-01-24 21:40:31',	'Hello. What about the 61 series? I have read this series is better than 62 series. Specially tenor 61 saxes are good valued. By the way, theres is so little information about 61s.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; rv:9.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/9.0.1',	'',	0,	0),
(1995,	1031,	'Evan Tate',	'evan@evantate.com',	'http://www.evantatemusic.com',	'92.227.27.120',	'2012-01-24 14:06:53',	'2012-01-24 20:06:53',	'Well, of course you\'d have to ask you teacher about this (you do have one, don\'t you?). If you don\'t have a teacher, I\'d advise you get one before attempting to do these exercises on your own. You can develop bad habits with the embouchure if you\'re not properly instructed. \r\n\r\nIn my opinion, it\'s (almost) never too early to start the practice of overtones. You must first have a good understanding about what they are first and why you practice them.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	1993,	0),
(1997,	196,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-24 20:06:41',	'2012-01-25 04:06:41',	'Hello David,\r\n\r\nTo be perfectly honest, I haven\'t tried the 61 series, so I can\'t really speak intelligently about those. I was just at NAMM, but the Yamaha horns were on a different floor than the rest of the horns and I never made my way up to that booth. \r\n\r\nHopefully someone else can chime in here. Sorry!\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	1994,	1),
(1998,	1031,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-24 20:09:07',	'2012-01-25 04:09:07',	'I totally agree with Evan. Properly learning to control the muscles involved in getting those overtones to sound will build up your sound tremendously and teach you how to get around the horn without depending on inaccurately moving your jaw all over the place when you\'re moving throughout the horn\'s range.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	1995,	1),
(2000,	2732,	'Matheus',	'sparks.220@hotmail.com',	'',	'187.35.191.202',	'2012-01-25 02:50:10',	'2012-01-25 10:50:10',	'Guy... thank you. I am a singer and one of the things that I have been studying actually is that we are supposed to work on developing an \"open throat\" to sing. If we don\'t do it we will supposed to sound weak and thin, and strained too. I didn\'t believe too much about that, simply because it didn\'t make too much sense to me and trying to sing like that was no something natural to me. I\'ve been studying things from various vocal coaches and hardly I found something that really convinced me. Then I found your this page and WOW, now yes, convinced me. There are lots of misunderstandings about lots of things, in singing too: \"singing with a high larynx is bad and bla bla bla, you will sound forced if you do it and bla bla bla...\" The position of the larynx while singing was one of the myths I luckily could discover the truth. Well... thanks for showing us that. I don\'t play saxophone but you made me a better singer, thank you ^^.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1) AppleWebKit/535.11 (KHTML, like Gecko) Comodo_Dragon/17.1.0.0 Chrome/17.0.963.38 Safari/535.11',	'',	0,	0),
(2002,	196,	'Bruce',	'bwilliams@logic.bm',	'',	'69.17.215.194',	'2012-01-25 05:16:08',	'2012-01-25 13:16:08',	'Hello,\r\n\r\nI understand that the Yamaha soprano 82Z is pretty new on the market, but why is there so little critical review to be found posted? Is it because of the high price in this lousy economy, is it failing to meet expectations of those who\'ve tried it or is it just too soon?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1; rv:2.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/4.0',	'',	0,	0),
(2003,	2732,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-25 10:12:13',	'2012-01-25 18:12:13',	'Wow, that\'s very cool that you\'ve found this article helpful! I would imagine that a powerful and focused airstream is a good thing to have whether you play sax or sing, so I can see the similarity. \r\n\r\nI am curious how you came across this site, however(?).\r\n\r\nAt any rate, thanks so much for chiming in!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	2000,	1),
(2004,	196,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-25 10:15:54',	'2012-01-25 18:15:54',	'I think that saxophone reviews in general are pretty rare because very, very few saxophonists have access to instruments other than their own, and out of that small population - which is probably made up mostly of successful full-time professionals - how many of them will take the time to write a review and see that it gets published? \r\n\r\nHopefully I\'ll be able to add some horn reviews here in the near future, but in the meantime, I suppose thing to do is to go try out the horns yourself at a local music store.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	2002,	1),
(2006,	2732,	'Matheus',	'sparks.220@hotmail.com',	'',	'200.148.49.185',	'2012-01-25 20:37:10',	'2012-01-26 04:37:10',	'I was doing one of my Google researches and then I  found your site. I started to read and then when you \'said\' that the throat cannot move I felt like \'BINGO\'! THAT makes sense, and when you do exercises to get rid of tension in your tongue, neck, jaw or even in the muscles near the throat you feel like you have an \'open throat\' - not because it was closed but yes because you were under bad tension (yes, there\'s a good tension; a good tension that you put on your vocal folds to change the way your voice sounds. If well done it\'ll not damage them.), what can hamper your singing and even when you play an instrument where a \'free\' throat is need, like a saxophone. Thanks again.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1) AppleWebKit/535.11 (KHTML, like Gecko) Comodo_Dragon/17.1.0.0 Chrome/17.0.963.38 Safari/535.11',	'',	2003,	0),
(2007,	2732,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-25 20:45:48',	'2012-01-26 04:45:48',	'A \"free throat\" - that\'s a good way of thinking about it!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	2006,	1),
(2008,	2732,	'Matheus',	'sparks.220@hotmail.com',	'',	'200.148.49.185',	'2012-01-26 07:22:19',	'2012-01-26 15:22:19',	'A \"free throat\" - sure!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1) AppleWebKit/535.11 (KHTML, like Gecko) Comodo_Dragon/17.1.0.0 Chrome/17.0.963.38 Safari/535.11',	'',	2007,	0),
(2009,	383,	'Nemoy',	'Nemoynsw@gmail.com',	'',	'124.149.43.96',	'2012-01-26 15:26:17',	'2012-01-26 23:26:17',	'That was the best article ever.  I had a listen to the recordings as well.  Can\'t wait to grab the horn.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 8.0; Windows NT 5.1; Trident/4.0; EasyBits GO v1.0; .NET CLR 1.1.4322; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 3.0.4506.2152; .NET CLR 3.5.30729; AskTbDVS2/5.14.1.20007)',	'',	0,	0),
(2011,	2589,	'fabion',	'fvicks@hotmail.com',	'',	'98.80.189.159',	'2012-01-26 18:21:13',	'2012-01-27 02:21:13',	'have you had an opportunity to play a cannonball sax yet. I am thinking about purchasing the raven model.I have been playing for over 22 years and play each sunday during service and some outside gigs.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1; rv:9.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/9.0.1',	'',	0,	0),
(2012,	928,	'TenorMoxie',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'75.111.32.122',	'2012-01-26 19:52:41',	'2012-01-27 03:52:41',	'Nighthawk, 1960 session with Coleman Hawkins and Lockjaw.  A nice conversation between those two gentlemen.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0; rv:9.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/9.0.1',	'',	0,	0),
(2013,	2589,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-26 21:09:35',	'2012-01-27 05:09:35',	'I did actually try a Cannonball and really likeed it a lot, definitely worth checking out. I was also pleasantly surprised by the Chateau horns, so you may want to give those a try as well. You can hear me trying a bunch of horns back to back at NAMM in this video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2XYErnWlKRg.\r\n\r\nI hope that helps!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	2011,	1),
(2014,	383,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-26 21:42:31',	'2012-01-27 05:42:31',	'Very coo Nemoy, so glad you found it helpful and inspiring!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.75 Safari/535.7',	'',	2009,	1),
(2020,	756,	'SaxGuy214',	'jaredsharp16@gmail.com',	'',	'71.193.132.120',	'2012-01-29 21:06:17',	'2012-01-30 05:06:17',	'What song is that in the audio clip of David Sanborn?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	0,	0),
(2021,	756,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-29 21:49:26',	'2012-01-30 05:49:26',	'It\'s the song, Hideaway taken from the live album \"Straight to the Heart.\" https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Heart-David-Sanborn/dp/B000002L6N\r\n\r\nSome people might call his music smooth-ish jazz, but regardless, Sanborn is without a doubt one of the most gifted and soulful players ever to play the sax (in my humble opinion).',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	2020,	1),
(2022,	756,	'SaxGuy214',	'jaredsharp16@gmail.com',	'',	'71.193.132.120',	'2012-01-29 22:23:31',	'2012-01-30 06:23:31',	'I agree, his sound would fit into a multitude of jazz settings, including the really elaborate big band charts. This is the (not exact) kind of sound I still am striving to achieve on my alto, which I most commonly play in a big band setting.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	2021,	0),
(2023,	756,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-01-29 22:32:00',	'2012-01-30 06:32:00',	'Yeah, Sanborn\'s normal sound would be hard to contain in a big band setting, but he\'s such a badass that I bet he could make it work, no problem.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	2022,	1),
(2028,	3310,	'David O',	'tavita@ipacific.com',	'',	'68.116.51.131',	'2012-01-30 15:09:34',	'2012-01-30 21:09:34',	'Nice report, Zach. I\'ll have try one of those bamboo-infiltrated Forestones!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1; rv:6.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/6.0',	'',	0,	0),
(2029,	3310,	'Zach',	'sollitt2@tcnj.edu',	'',	'99.156.127.214',	'2012-01-30 16:20:57',	'2012-01-31 00:20:57',	'Hey Dave,\r\n\r\nThanks for the compliment. The forestone reed is a great alternative to cane as well as a great back up reed.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	2028,	0),
(2071,	3337,	'Gary',	'graykopp@yahoo.com',	'',	'74.40.39.118',	'2012-02-06 10:00:40',	'2012-02-06 18:00:40',	'One of the best tools for keeping your fingers limber is the Finger Excercise in the Rubank Advanced Method, Book 1.  These are designed to exploit weaknesses in fingers.  Mine is the pinky on my left hand.  I use a few select exercises during warm-up to keep this in check.  The real trick is to play them slowly, about 60 BPM. It takes discipline to play that slow and precise and really helps play evenly.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 8.0; Windows NT 5.1; Trident/4.0; BTRS27183; .NET CLR 1.1.4322; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 3.0.4506.2152; .NET CLR 3.5.30729)',	'',	0,	0),
(2072,	3337,	'Bret Pimentel',	'bpimentel+wordpress@gmail.com',	'https://bretpimentel.com/',	'209.147.246.68',	'2012-02-06 10:49:16',	'2012-02-06 18:49:16',	'I like the \"Sixty Exercises of Mechanism\" from the Universal Method for this same type of very slow, very precise work. I\'ve had my saxophone students doing these recently (and my clarinet students doing the corresponding Klose exercises) with great success: even, controlled, relaxed technique, with even, consistent tone from note to note.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	2071,	0),
(2078,	3337,	'Stroobia',	'arundo.donax@stroobia.com',	'http://www.stroobia.com/',	'91.75.44.196',	'2012-02-06 20:58:36',	'2012-02-07 02:58:36',	'I play Bach\'s Six Suites for cello (by Trent Kynaston) on and on (well, not all of them). With different articulations, and sometime, sacrilege, I swing them.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 7.0; Windows NT 6.1; Trident/5.0; SLCC2; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 3.5.30729; .NET CLR 3.0.30729; Media Center PC 6.0; InfoPath.3)',	'',	0,	0),
(2079,	3337,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-02-06 21:00:15',	'2012-02-07 05:00:15',	'I remember playing along with the Rubank Books, very good stuff indeed. Yeah, playing really slow is the ultimate challenge. In fact, I should have mentioned that since it\'s such an important piece of the technical puzzle. Thanks Gary!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	2071,	1),
(2080,	3337,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-02-06 21:03:21',	'2012-02-07 05:03:21',	'Hey Bret! It\'s been a long time since I\'ve broken out the Universal Method. The Klose is a book that I would love to get familiar with (if only I didn\'t spend so much time on the dang website!).  It seems like you have a holistic approach to technique the goes beyond simply moving fingers quickly. Lucky students!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	2072,	1),
(2081,	3337,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-02-06 21:04:49',	'2012-02-07 05:04:49',	'Swinging Bach! Oh my virgin ears - how dare you! But seriously, I think that\'s great practice. Baroque music in general is great practice since it really keeps your fingers moving with a focus on clarity and evenness. Thanks for the great suggestion!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	2078,	1),
(2082,	3337,	'Stroobia',	'arundo.donax@stroobia.com',	'http://www.stroobia.com/',	'91.75.44.196',	'2012-02-06 21:12:09',	'2012-02-07 03:12:09',	'Yeah... I know, swinging Bach is bad :) but i can\'t resist it ;) only sometimes...',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 7.0; Windows NT 6.1; Trident/5.0; SLCC2; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 3.5.30729; .NET CLR 3.0.30729; Media Center PC 6.0; InfoPath.3)',	'',	2081,	0),
(2100,	1712,	'rodney',	'rodneydeery@hotmail.com',	'',	'82.132.210.189',	'2012-02-08 12:42:43',	'2012-02-08 20:42:43',	'baritone saxophone can be and to me is one of the most melodic instrument\'s ,i play alto/tenor/clarinete / and of course baritone. like anything you do in music it deserves practice and attention, and perhaps a slightly more focused umbersure ,iv\'e done big-band recording\'s at my home studio\' of classics such as the very old saxophobia as a cha cha and the bari stand\'s out and take\'s a bow when he\'s finished, of course it\'s imperative that arrangements are good;\r\nthanks. rod deery.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	0,	0),
(2101,	1712,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-02-08 13:48:33',	'2012-02-08 21:48:33',	'Hey Rodney! I\'ve never really thought about the embouchure differences for baritone, but I could see that perhaps the bigger mouthpiece means that you have more to control in terms of focusing the air into the horn in the most efficient way. Feel free to elaborate if you wish. Thanks for chiming in!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	2100,	1),
(2107,	1712,	'rodney',	'rodneydeery@hotmail.com',	'',	'82.132.211.9',	'2012-02-09 10:55:27',	'2012-02-09 18:55:27',	'hello doron,\r\nagain that work\'s for me but i can remember year\'s ago when i started on saxophone this is very important, load\'s of player\'s spend an inundated fortune on sax mouth-peaces and 7 times out of ten   the one there useing would be fine with perseverance, i use a very old ottolink 7star on the bari, it\'s fine top and bottom a, even altissmo , if needed and i keep my ligature fairly slack it\'s important as you well no to give the reed vibrating scope hope this info is of use.\r\nkind regard\'s rod.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1) AppleWebKit/535.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/16.0.912.77 Safari/535.7',	'',	2101,	0),
(2132,	3345,	'Andrew Smith',	'andrew@flicflac.co.uk',	'http://www.flicflac.co.uk',	'188.223.141.193',	'2012-02-13 09:03:01',	'2012-02-13 15:03:01',	'Are these available on other platforms too (I\'m on Android and Windows Phone)?\r\n\r\nWhile I\'m here, I should also give an honorable mention to iRealB. It\'s an open-format fakebook platform, where you can download chord charts submitted by other community members, or write your own. The software can then transpose them to any key, and play a backing track at any tempo in any of about 15 styles. Great for practising improvising...',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; rv:10.0.1) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/10.0.1',	'',	0,	0),
(2134,	3345,	'Tobias Haecker',	'mail@saxophonistisches.de',	'http://saxophonistisches.de/',	'92.228.250.136',	'2012-02-13 09:51:45',	'2012-02-13 15:51:45',	'Do you know already iRealB ?\r\n\r\nhttps://www.irealb.com/ \r\n\r\n(the only reason for me to purchase an iphone)\r\n\r\nhere I also collected some other good apps:\r\nhttps://saxophonistisches.de/ijazz-apps-fur-musik/',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/535.11 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/17.0.963.46 Safari/535.11',	'',	0,	0),
(2137,	3345,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-02-13 20:52:10',	'2012-02-14 04:52:10',	'Hello Andrew,\r\n\r\nUnfortunately at this time these apps are only available for iPhone. But that real book app sounds amazing - will have to try it soon, since I really have only a few play along albums that I enjoy playing with. \r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.11 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/17.0.963.46 Safari/535.11',	'',	2132,	1),
(2138,	3345,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.52.64',	'2012-02-13 20:56:35',	'2012-02-14 04:56:35',	'Hey Tobias!\r\n\r\nYeah, Andrew in the comment before you actually brought up iRealB. Sounds like a great app, will probably download it soon. But I love the list of apps you have on your site, especially the one for slowing down audio. It\'s amazing how conveniently and inexpensively we can get access to tools and information that would have been so difficult to get just 5 years ago. \r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/535.11 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/17.0.963.46 Safari/535.11',	'',	2134,	1),
