(6153,	3708,	'pavel',	'garisonsax@mail.ru',	'',	'31.31.21.69',	'2013-07-07 11:09:10',	'2013-07-07 18:09:10',	'I HAVE A PROBLEM ON MY MARK 6 NUMBER 183 *** PROBLEM low note С# ..C H B ...SAX SHUT adjusted at the bottom notes are taken BAD plays\r\nWhen the game is like gurgling, OR THAT IT WILL NOT CLOSE....Sax was being renovated master does not know what to do..\r\n-- I LIVE HERE IN MOLDOVA AND NONE OF THIS WHO UNDERSTANDS .this decision may?https://www.youtube.com/watch?feature=player_embedded&amp;v=q7efNh7qJlc  IS THERE SUCH WAY TO SOLVE THIS PROBLEM.? CAN YOU KNOW HOW TO HELP ME I JUST I am suffering when the game and would be grateful to',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/27.0.1453.116 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(6160,	4539,	'Steve B',	'seboney@comcast.net',	'',	'98.244.129.193',	'2013-07-08 05:16:50',	'2013-07-08 12:16:50',	'Hi...Where is arpeggio exercise?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/27.0.1453.116 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(6161,	4539,	'Zach Sollitto',	'zach@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'',	'139.76.64.65',	'2013-07-08 05:30:29',	'2013-07-08 12:30:29',	'Hey Steve,\r\n\r\nIt\'s not a pdf exercise. \r\n\r\nBased on Chad\'s advice, you can make up your own exercise based on voicing any type of scale by 1,4,5,7,10,13 instead of 1,3,5,7,9. This is another way to hear different chord tones and see how you can apply theses sounds throughout your solos.\r\n\r\nI hope this helps.\r\n\r\nRead below for Chad\'s description.\r\n\r\n\r\n Technically, I’m focused on using more rhythmic concepts and using triads in every possible way. This thought process comes from George Garzone which teaches you to play every variation of a triad and connecting it to different triads as a way to create tension. I also practice what I like to call diatonic intervallic stacking. For example instead of playing the scale degrees 1,3,5,7,9, I’ll play 1,4,5,7,10,13 and play them as if I was playing any other arpeggio exercise, which I think opens up your ears to different sounds. I’ve found this to be a great way to practice your altissimo range and playing more fluidly in that range instead of hitting a really high note and then jumping back down to the standard fingerings.\r\n\r\nZach',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 8.0; Windows NT 6.1; Trident/4.0; SLCC2; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 3.5.30729; .NET CLR 3.0.30729; Media Center PC 6.0; .NET CLR 1.1.4322; .NET4.0C; .NET4.0E; ATT)',	'',	6160,	0),
(6168,	337,	'Timi',	'funtyke@gmail.com',	'',	'151.183.0.36',	'2013-07-09 02:41:59',	'2013-07-09 09:41:59',	'Could you please tell me where to purchase a professional selmer tenor and alto saxophone (green and white color).\r\n\r\nThanks',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/27.0.1453.116 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(6173,	3827,	'Bopsmom',	'suited1@verizon.net',	'',	'72.81.226.56',	'2013-07-09 19:49:25',	'2013-07-10 02:49:25',	'I am not sure what happened with Chuck Levin\'s and Wildabeast. We purchased a Soprano sax for my daughter there recently. They took us back into the office/storage area---which is quite large and absolutely FULL of instruments. I can not speak to the used options there. We did have an \"appointment\" so to speak.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; MSIE 10.0; Windows NT 6.2; WOW64; Trident/6.0)',	'',	5254,	0),
(6222,	3667,	'jake',	'jeopeo@hotmail.com',	'',	'83.189.184.119',	'2013-07-12 13:09:23',	'2013-07-12 20:09:23',	'Thx daniel, I really like that one. You can even adjust \"swingrate\". Im a bassplayer and play a lot of jazz, and its really awesome to practise to the swingride in different tempos when u can adjust the swing.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.71 Safari/537.36',	'',	6115,	0),
(6224,	3667,	'John Nastos',	'john@johnnastos.com',	'https://johnnastos.com',	'98.246.77.53',	'2013-07-12 13:58:56',	'2013-07-12 20:58:56',	'Metronomics for Android is now available, too.  It has all of the regular Metronomics features, including the adjustable swing rate one of the other commenters mentioned.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_3) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/27.0.1453.116 Safari/537.36',	'',	2611,	0),
(6226,	3667,	'jake',	'jeopeo@hotmail.com',	'',	'83.189.184.119',	'2013-07-12 17:46:38',	'2013-07-13 00:46:38',	'Cool app, random rythms can sound good. \r\n\r\nI like how easy it is in JEOS metronome to play uneven timesignatures and that u get allready preset grooves. Its easier. \r\n\r\nLike if u wanna practice samba there\'s a sambagroove ready for u and it plays it in 7/8 or whatever. Very neat. \r\n\r\nBut I like the random feature of your app, I bought both. \r\n\r\n:)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 4.1.1; HTC One X+ Build/JRO03C) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.64 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	6224,	0),
(6234,	3827,	'Dennis',	'piperofhamlin@yahoo.com',	'',	'24.247.148.224',	'2013-07-13 09:56:15',	'2013-07-13 16:56:15',	'Did you just download a list of Selmer dealers in the U.S?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(6240,	3527,	'Zach',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'99.156.125.176',	'2013-07-13 16:49:37',	'2013-07-13 23:49:37',	'Sure. Send me an email at bellsouth.net when you would like to talk.\r\n\r\nZach',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.72 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(6241,	3827,	'Zach',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'99.156.125.176',	'2013-07-13 16:52:33',	'2013-07-13 23:52:33',	'Hey Dennis,\r\n\r\nNo. It might seem like that because most to all of these dealers carry Selmer but these are shops I have visited or have talked to multiple players who highly enjoyed visiting these shops. Actually, most of these shops carry much more then just Selmer (Keilwerth, Yanagisawa, MacSax, R.S. Berkley, Viking, Yamaha, P Mauriat, Cannonball, etc.)\r\n\r\nIs their a horn you are looking for in particular? \r\n\r\nZach',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.72 Safari/537.36',	'',	6234,	0),
(6262,	922,	'Norman',	'norrmanndo@yahoo.com',	'',	'173.79.122.208',	'2013-07-14 18:32:21',	'2013-07-15 01:32:21',	'Thanks for all this information. I played in highschool and none of this was covered even though one band teacher specialized sax. That was 33 years ago. Im finally getting back into it. I really appreciate it.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; U; Android 4.1.2; en-us; SCH-I605 Build/JZO54K) AppleWebKit/534.30 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4.0 Mobile Safari/534.30',	'',	0,	0),
(6271,	922,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.168.48.206',	'2013-07-14 23:28:23',	'2013-07-15 06:28:23',	'So glad to help, congrats on getting back in the sax game!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.71 Safari/537.36',	'',	6262,	1),
(6403,	1254,	'Top Tips For Cleaning Your Saxophone - Hooppler',	'',	'',	'80.77.157.4',	'2013-07-18 14:21:48',	'2013-07-18 20:21:48',	'[...] to keep your saxophone clean is to make sure you play your instrument with clean hands as well as brushing your teeth before playing. Moisture always gets inside your saxophone while you play and you shouldn’t put your saxophone [...]',	0,	'1',	'The Incutio XML-RPC PHP Library -- WordPress/3.5.2',	'pingback',	0,	0),
(6411,	624,	'Ken',	'kfrankgm@gmail.com',	'',	'74.203.58.99',	'2013-07-18 17:15:48',	'2013-07-19 00:15:48',	'I just got the book and it is a duet book but different from the one for oboe. Bit disappointing really unless you have someone to practice them with.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(6422,	337,	'Thea',	'thea_levesque@telus.net',	'',	'173.183.68.149',	'2013-07-18 21:48:24',	'2013-07-19 04:48:24',	'Can you tell me anything about the Selmer AS32 and AS42 saxophones.  I cannot seem to find any reviews of them on the web.  Thank you very much.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(6473,	4553,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.43.183',	'2013-07-22 17:38:46',	'2013-07-23 00:38:46',	'Zach: I e-mailed them to see if they would send me some sample reeds. They asked for my address which I gave them but so far I haven\'t received any reed samples.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(6474,	4575,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.43.183',	'2013-07-22 17:45:09',	'2013-07-23 00:45:09',	'Doron:\r\n\r\nGood stuff, I totally agree.\r\n\r\nLarry W',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(6475,	4575,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'4.31.55.178',	'2013-07-22 17:56:25',	'2013-07-23 00:56:25',	'Thanks, Larry!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.71 Safari/537.36',	'',	6474,	1),
(6476,	270,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.43.183',	'2013-07-22 18:07:14',	'2013-07-23 01:07:14',	'Doron:\r\n\r\nThese days I\'m playing a lot more tenor than clarinet. BUT, I have done shows where I had to play both tenor and clarinet and it was important to sound good on both instruments. \r\n\r\nIf I had my \'druthers I would just play tenor in a jazz combo all the time. However being able to play clarinet well has gotten me gigs, especially shows. It also helped to get me into the Navy Band Program. Believe it or not I also played clarinet when I did the Four Tops Show. Also a lot of big band charts do require sax players to play either flute, clarinet or bass clarinet. That\'s 1 thing I really liked about playing in Navy Bands, I got a chance to play bari, bass clarinet, clarinet and my tenor. I was given a chance to be featured on tenor, bari and clarinet. We did Artie Shaw\'s \"Concerto For Clarinet\" and I was Shaw. \r\n\r\nBesides playing tenor and clarinet I also teach both. It all adds up to being part of your income earning bag of tricks. Btw - I also play piano.Not good enough to be in a Jazz Combo but good enough to help w/arranging, showing students how to comp etc. \r\n\r\nWell that\'s my 2 cents. Check out Dan Higgins, Gene Ciprano, Gary Foster, Sal Lozano and other LA Studio cats to see how they double/triple etc.\r\n\r\nLater,\r\n\r\nLarry',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(6477,	770,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.43.183',	'2013-07-22 18:17:37',	'2013-07-23 01:17:37',	'Jeff: Very cool arrangement, and great overdubbing on all the parts. Every sax you play sounds great giving a nice full sax section sound. Did you write the chart too in your spare time between gigs and on set breaks?\r\n\r\nTake care,\r\n\r\nLarry W',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(6481,	270,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.175.195.148',	'2013-07-22 22:24:43',	'2013-07-23 05:24:43',	'Yep, there\'s no doubt that being a doubler increases your income as a sax player, in many cases exponentially so. Not doubling definitely makes playing sax professionally an even more risky venture. But then again, if you have a very specific vision for what you want to do musically, and you\'re very passionate about that vision, and it doesn\'t involve playing doubles, then it might be worth the added risk.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.71 Safari/537.36',	'',	6476,	1),
(6482,	3411,	'Jerome',	'jeromerider@web.de',	'',	'173.234.196.249',	'2013-07-23 01:31:41',	'2013-07-23 07:31:41',	'However, it is notable that Phentermine can indeed help you \r\nwhen dieting 5 days a week and physical exercises fail to yield desired weight loss results \r\nare far more accessible to the public.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 8.0; Windows NT 6.0; Trident/4.0; Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1) ; .NET CLR 3.5.30729)',	'',	0,	0),
(6483,	270,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.43.183',	'2013-07-23 07:25:59',	'2013-07-23 14:25:59',	'Doron:\r\n\r\nWell yes it all depends on what you want to do or are able to do and get the calls for. Some really great non doubler\'s today are guys like Eric Alexander, Scott Hamilton and Harry Allen. Actually Harry does play clarinet but he has said that it would take up to much of his time to keep it to the level he would need it to be at to play gigs on it. Those guys are into the more creative aspect of music than the commercial/teaching part of it.\r\n\r\nPersonally I am really into that myself these days. I keep my clarinet chops up to the point where I can teach it and play 1 or 2 tunes a night on clarinet on my jazz gigs. Because I started on clarinet it might be a bit easier for me to put my chops back together after a layoff than other guys who started on sax.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(6485,	770,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.43.183',	'2013-07-23 10:05:11',	'2013-07-23 17:05:11',	'Really nice interview with Jeff Driskill. I liked his comment about that if you really want to do something than do it.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(6487,	2933,	'wilson leather bags',	'lanny_hatchett@zoho.com',	'',	'188.40.244.46',	'2013-07-23 12:51:40',	'2013-07-23 18:51:40',	'Hi, I think your site might be having browser compatibility issues.\r\n\r\nWhen I look at your blog in Opera, it looks \r\nfine but when opening in Internet Explorer, it has some overlapping.\r\nI just wanted to give you a quick heads up! Other then that, excellent blog!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 7.0; Windows NT 5.1; Trident/4.0; .NET CLR 1.1.4322)',	'',	0,	0),
(6488,	4363,	'Obagi',	'cassiebourque@gmx.de',	'',	'142.234.62.213',	'2013-07-23 13:28:01',	'2013-07-23 19:28:01',	'Amazing things here. I\'m very glad to look your article. Thanks a lot and I am taking a look forward to touch you. Will you kindly drop me a e-mail?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 6.0; Windows NT 5.1; SV1; MRA 5.8 (build 4157); .NET CLR 2.0.50727; AskTbPTV/5.11.3.15590)',	'',	0,	0),
(6493,	4553,	'Tibbs',	'jtibbs06@gmail.com',	'',	'70.61.235.69',	'2013-07-24 12:57:58',	'2013-07-24 19:57:58',	'I also emailed them about some sample reeds and never got a response back from them. Strange most companies would want people to try their product.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; MSIE 10.0; Windows NT 6.1; Trident/6.0)',	'',	0,	0),
(6494,	4553,	'Zach Sollitto',	'zach@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'',	'139.76.64.65',	'2013-07-24 13:12:11',	'2013-07-24 20:12:11',	'Hey Larry &amp; Tibbs\r\n\r\nI will see what I can do.\r\n\r\nI have some sample reed packs so if you let me know what you want to try I will do my best to get you some samples.\r\n\r\nIn addition. Most companies will send samples to potential endorsing artists or current endorsing artists.\r\n\r\nEven as a product reviewer, not all companies will send me sample products unless I meet them in person or have a strong reference.\r\n\r\nZach',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 8.0; Windows NT 6.1; Trident/4.0; SLCC2; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 3.5.30729; .NET CLR 3.0.30729; Media Center PC 6.0; .NET CLR 1.1.4322; .NET4.0C; .NET4.0E; ATT)',	'',	0,	0),
(6495,	4575,	'TenorMoxie',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'75.111.3.29',	'2013-07-24 13:53:30',	'2013-07-24 20:53:30',	'Definitely agree that a lot of players put way too much emphasis on gear and for the wrong reasons.  Launching a quest for Florida Link or magic VI is not going to transform anybody\'s playing.  \r\n\r\nThe most important criterion for good equipment isn\'t what it does, but what it doesn\'t do, i.e. impede the development of your sound. We\'re all familiar with players who mold their style excessively around limitations of their technique.  But sometimes technique runs up against limitations in equipment, and that can also be limiting to a player\'s style.  Figuring what\'s going on when a technical wall is encountered can be kind of tricky.  Sometimes shortcomings in equipment remain latent until a player is pushing their tone and technique.  If the player is lucky, it\'s a minor issue with condition or adjustment.  But sometimes it really is an inherent limitation based on design or quality.  \r\n\r\nMy experience runs the whole gamut - most of the time the solution was practice, practice, practice; less commonly (but too often) it was a repair or adjustment issue that went unrecognized; and on a few occasions a piece of equipment was simply unsuited for what I was trying to achieve.  Most recently, a more rigorous and exacting practice routine exposed a response problem. The solution was a simple procedure on the mouthpiece performed with hardware store supplies.  Got off cheap!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; MSIE 10.0; Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/6.0)',	'',	0,	0),
(6499,	4553,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.43.183',	'2013-07-24 16:40:54',	'2013-07-24 23:40:54',	'Zach: Thanks for the offer. I play Orange box Rico 2.5 on tenor and sometimes a Plasticover # 3 for outdoors gigs. On alto which I use for teaching, I play a LaVoz Hard. So I would need something comparable to that. \r\n\r\nThis guy from the company did say he would try to send me some but so far nothing. Who sells them in the States? I told the guy I teach at 2 colleges (Old Dominion University and Tidewater Comm College and I was retired from a Navy Band). So I am not some beginner or college student in my 20\'s.\r\n\r\nAnyway send me a private e-mail to Lweintraub1@cox.net and I\'ll send you my address.\r\n\r\nThanks Zach,\r\n\r\nLarry W',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(6503,	3827,	'Kenny',	'Contact@saxophonebackingtracks.com',	'https://Saxophonebackingtracks.com',	'119.56.120.194',	'2013-07-25 04:06:19',	'2013-07-25 11:06:19',	'These are famous sax shop in the states? Thanks ! I think joe is good',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 6_1_4 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/536.26 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/6.0 Mobile/10B350 Safari/8536.25',	'',	0,	0),
(6511,	4553,	'Tibbs',	'Jtibbs06@gmail.com',	'',	'99.155.214.60',	'2013-07-25 07:49:53',	'2013-07-25 14:49:53',	'How are the reed sizes compared to Vandorens?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_6_8) AppleWebKit/534.59.8 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/5.1.9 Safari/534.59.8',	'',	6494,	0),
(6512,	4599,	'Bret Pimentel',	'bpimentel+wordpress@gmail.com',	'https://bretpimentel.com',	'209.147.242.196',	'2013-07-25 08:09:06',	'2013-07-25 15:09:06',	'I tried some Eastman prototypes a couple of years ago. From your review, it seems that maybe they have made some improvements since then.\r\n\r\nOne thing that struck me as add about them was that they used a lot of hex/Allen screws instead of the usual slotted screws (I don\'t recall the ones I played having the adjustable palm keys). The Eastman rep I spoke with had no explanation for this. Did the ones you played have hex screws, besides the palm keys?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.71 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(6516,	4599,	'Zach Sollitto',	'zach@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'',	'139.76.224.65',	'2013-07-25 09:46:00',	'2013-07-25 16:46:00',	'Hey Bret,\r\n\r\nTo be honest I only believe the palm keys had the hex screws but I do believe you could adjust other parts of tenor and alto and they might also have hex screws.\r\n\r\nI know alot of horns come with slotted screws as you mentioned.\r\n\r\nWhat is your current setup?\r\n\r\nZach',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/4.0 (compatible; MSIE 8.0; Windows NT 6.1; Trident/4.0; SLCC2; .NET CLR 2.0.50727; .NET CLR 3.5.30729; .NET CLR 3.0.30729; Media Center PC 6.0; .NET CLR 1.1.4322; .NET4.0C; .NET4.0E; ATT)',	'',	0,	0),
(6522,	4599,	'andrew fawcett',	'a.fawcett616@btinternet.com',	'',	'86.144.132.88',	'2013-07-25 12:01:34',	'2013-07-25 19:01:34',	'I actually like the sound of the 52 tenor better than the MK VI.    On the alto, I wasn\'t so sure.  Thought you were very comfortable with the Mk VI alto.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_7_5) AppleWebKit/536.30.1 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/6.0.5 Safari/536.30.1',	'',	0,	0),
(6528,	4575,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.175.195.148',	'2013-07-25 15:26:10',	'2013-07-25 22:26:10',	'Awesome insights! I do think that it\'s good to have at least decent equipment in good working order so that we\'re not developing bad habits to compensate for the equipment\'s shortcomings. But I still think it\'s good from time to time to try some different gear out just in case something jumps out that gets you to where you want to be much faster than if you tried getting there with practice alone. As long as new gear isn\'t a crutch, then we\'re all entitled to something shiny and new from time to time, no?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.71 Safari/537.36',	'',	6495,	1),
(6554,	4575,	'TenorMoxie',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'75.111.3.29',	'2013-07-26 13:36:49',	'2013-07-26 20:36:49',	'Well.... playing something that looks like a sewer pipe is my comfort zone.  Purchases driven by testing against a performance objective seem justified.  But sometimes there\'s the pressure to seek validation through gear, and that\'s where players fall into a trap.  Peer pressure, teacher pressure, razzle dazzle pressure.... There\'s a guy who fulfilled his dream of owning a Selmer with a Reference 54.  He found out that he preferred the horn he\'d had for 30 years.  Ouch!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; MSIE 10.0; Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/6.0)',	'',	6528,	0),
(6641,	4599,	'Zach',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'99.156.125.176',	'2013-07-30 18:31:59',	'2013-07-31 01:31:59',	'Hey Andrew,\r\n\r\nI am used to playing my Selmer Mark VI tenor but thought the 52nd street tenor played great. \r\n\r\nOn alto, I felt more comfortable on my SBA than the 52nd street alto but I did like some the features on the 52nd street alto that I wish my SBA had.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.72 Safari/537.36',	'',	6522,	0),
(6650,	3733,	'Molly Ruggles',	'molly_d_ruggles@yahoo.com',	'https://mollyruggles.com',	'71.232.15.190',	'2013-07-31 05:12:24',	'2013-07-31 12:12:24',	'Great site! Great suggestions! May I add Coleman Hawkins to the list? His solo on \'You\'d be so Nice to Come Home to\' is harmonically rich and very rewarding to study and get to know.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_7_5) AppleWebKit/536.29.13 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/6.0.4 Safari/536.29.13',	'',	0,	0),
(6664,	3733,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.175.195.148',	'2013-07-31 13:48:09',	'2013-07-31 20:48:09',	'A great suggestion indeed, there\'s a lot of vocabulary we get could get from Coleman that we wouldn\'t come across in the world of bop and \"modern jazz\" that so many of us focus on.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.95 Safari/537.36',	'',	6650,	1),
(6688,	4419,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.43.183',	'2013-08-01 13:39:31',	'2013-08-01 20:39:31',	'Has anyone ever done a playing comparison between an FL Otto Link Metal STM and a metal Hollywood Dukoff from the 40\'s-50\'s like the one Dexter played? If so have you made a youtube of the comparison. \r\n\r\nAlso how about a comparison between a Slant Sig HR Link and a Dukoff HR Fluted chamber mpc. Both of these comparisons would be interesting to hear. \r\n\r\nOf course 1st we have to find someone who either owns those mpcs or else has access to them.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(6771,	1596,	'iain duncan',	'iainctduncan@gmail.com',	'http://www.iainduncan.com',	'96.49.209.182',	'2013-08-04 09:55:38',	'2013-08-04 15:55:38',	'Just wanted to chime in for those wondering whether to take the plunge and retrain the emboucer. I did it about a year ago. I purchased a way smaller tip opening to work out on for the process ( 6 down from 7* on a metal link ).  It feels freaking impossible at first and you sound like crap and can\'t play for long at all. It took a few months before playing was real. Now a year later, I can play longer, way bigger tone, and ZERO lower lip pain. I used to get really bad pain from a sharp crooked lower tooth protrusion, and now it doesn\'t bother me ever. In other words, TOTALLY WORTH IT. Just be patient, expect it to take a while and I highly recommend dropping down a few levels on your reed and mouthpiece combo while you work on it. Rick\'s videos were very helpful.\r\n\r\nmy two cents.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.71 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(6774,	1596,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.175.195.148',	'2013-08-04 10:11:36',	'2013-08-04 17:11:36',	'That\'s awesome to hear, and very much in line with my experience as well. I had to drop a reed strength, since I was exerting much less pressure from my lip. Thanks for sharing!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.95 Safari/537.36',	'',	6771,	1),
(6793,	3178,	'molly',	'mmoorehead360@gmail.com',	'',	'108.220.138.52',	'2013-08-05 10:22:39',	'2013-08-05 17:22:39',	'Doron,\r\n\r\nHey, nice sound but you may have a little \"slap-tongue\" going on. Could be your mic. but if you listen to your ghost notes, you can hear it.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; MSIE 10.0; Windows NT 6.2; WOW64; Trident/6.0)',	'',	0,	0),
(6803,	3178,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.175.195.148',	'2013-08-05 21:32:36',	'2013-08-06 04:32:36',	'Well, I don\'t think it could be slap tonguing because that\'s a technique I don\'t yet know. Unfortunately the camera I used for this video was pretty crappy, so perhaps there was some distortion that made my attacks sound a bit harsher, like slap tonguing, but I can assure you that that was not what I was doing.\r\n\r\nI\'m just glad that I now have a better camera to use for future videos! :)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/28.0.1500.95 Safari/537.36',	'',	6793,	1),
(6855,	4553,	'roberto upazzoli',	'upazzoli@phaselus.com',	'https://www.phaselus.com',	'46.14.104.194',	'2013-08-09 03:27:06',	'2013-08-09 10:27:06',	'Hi people, I\'m the President of Phaselus, which is the owner of Lupifaro brands. Wich adress have you tried?\r\nWe dont have recieved your mail.\r\nPlease keep direct in toch with me at upazzoli@phaselus.com and I\'ll obviously send some samples.\r\nthank you\r\nRoberto Upazzoli',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.0; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	6473,	0),
