(7670,	2732,	'Saxophone Lessons',	'rocking.san2010@yahoo.com',	'http://saxophonehub.com/saxophone-lessons',	'180.234.54.12',	'2013-09-29 00:19:06',	'2013-09-29 06:19:06',	'Best site ever about sax player. Thanks.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; rv:24.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/24.0',	'',	0,	0),
(7680,	1031,	'Rob Zantay',	'robzantay@gmail.com',	'',	'172.254.41.114',	'2013-09-29 16:42:19',	'2013-09-29 23:42:19',	'I also studied with Joe Allard, I have developed an exercise for flutes that involves playing bugel calls on the low C, C#, and D fingerings.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/29.0.1547.76 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(7683,	1031,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.175.195.148',	'2013-09-29 20:23:12',	'2013-09-30 03:23:12',	'Hey Rob,\r\n\r\nThat\'s awesome that you got to study with Joe! I\'d love to feature your exercise in an article on this website. If you wanted to do a quick write up or maybe get the exercise to me in notated format, that would be super-cool. I\'d be happy to give you full credit and link to anything you\'d want me to link to or put a little feature box where you could promote whatever you like. \r\n\r\nIf you\'re interested, hit me up via my Contact page and we\'ll make it happen. \r\n\r\nThanks!\r\n\r\nDoron',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_5) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/29.0.1547.76 Safari/537.36',	'',	7680,	1),
(7693,	4575,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.43.183',	'2013-09-30 18:02:37',	'2013-10-01 01:02:37',	'Zoot too only used 2 mpcs his whole career. Both were HR Brilharts. I believe the 2nd mpc was a Great Neck, Long Island HR Brilhart. Tommy Newsom played the same mpc on tenor.\r\n\r\nAlso Zoot said in an interview that he only owned 2 horns. While with Woody Herman he bought his 2nd horn a Selmer Super Balanced Action. Zoot said he bought it used, I believe off a college student.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:23.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/23.0',	'',	0,	0),
(7695,	2732,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.175.195.148',	'2013-09-30 19:24:27',	'2013-10-01 02:24:27',	'Thanks man, glad you found it helpful!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_5) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/29.0.1547.76 Safari/537.36',	'',	7669,	1),
(7696,	2161,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'76.175.195.148',	'2013-09-30 19:26:38',	'2013-10-01 02:26:38',	'Yeah, 4 good reeds in a box is pretty nice! As for the strength of the reed, if it sounds good and is letting the air flow naturally, then I don\'t see a problem. \r\n\r\nMaybe the 1.5 Vandoren is working for you since you have a very big tip opening on your Rico Metalite?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_8_5) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/29.0.1547.76 Safari/537.36',	'',	7648,	1),
