(101128,	1180,	'paul',	'jemiseyeholaiya@yahoo.com',	'',	'82.145.223.34',	'2015-05-30 02:01:52',	'2015-05-30 09:01:52',	'I want to know how to run scale on all the 12 keys on saxophone',	0,	'1',	'Opera/9.80 (BlackBerry; Opera Mini/8.0.35667/36.2168; U; en) Presto/2.12.423 Version/12.16',	'',	0,	0),
(101236,	4843,	'Ben Weiss Levi',	'benweisslevi@ziggo.nl',	'',	'83.84.137.102',	'2015-05-30 09:56:43',	'2015-05-30 16:56:43',	'The best way to approach chromatic passing tones is the way Barry Harris teachs. it\'s sounds elementary but if you start to dig it you\'ll become aware of the huge possibility this way offer sintetically you can concentrate the all thing in few words: ON THE DOWNBEAT PLAY ONLY NOTES OF THE CHORD/TONALITY, ON THE OFFBEAT PLAY WHATEVER YOU WANT.\r\nBe aware of the fact that between 3rd en 4th and 7th en 1st in maj and between 2nd en 3rd and 7th and 1st in min mel. (min harm. is even moore triky) there is an halfstep interval which made the all thing quite complex. best regards. Ben Weiss Levi',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_10_3) AppleWebKit/600.6.3 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/8.0.6 Safari/600.6.3',	'',	0,	0),
(102121,	3813,	'Cesar Nunez',	'cesar.nunez16@hotmail.com',	'',	'172.9.14.16',	'2015-06-02 02:50:15',	'2015-06-02 09:50:15',	'I have only been playing sax (mostly alto) for about seven years, but here\'s what I think. NOT ABOUT DIFFERENCE IN SOUND.\r\n\r\nI myself believe people should use what is most comfortable for them, meaning what works best. I have always been the one in my group of musician friends who always try new gear, and neck straps have only resently been one of those things. As of right now I own a Neotech neck strap, a Neotech body harness (even though I play alto), and a Jazzlab harness. I find that each three affect my playing greatly. The Neotech strap lets me move more freely while playing, but, I find, limits how fast my fingers can move (my sax moves too). The Neotech harness makes me feel more connected to my sax (because I am) and allows me to have more control in the movement of my fingers as well as tone. I prefer to use it for classical playing. Now the Jazzlab harness, I love. Between the three it is my favorite. It lets me move as much as I want, which I do a lot of, while having control over my sax. Although, of the three, it makes me feel like my sax is a separate object from my body (which it is). It is great for jazz playing though.\r\n\r\nI also recently got a new alto and find that the Neotech harness is helping me gets use to my sax. As I said, it gives me better control in the movement of my sax while playing fast licks. Personally, I like to use different gear for different settings and I think it is good to experiment with things other musicians take for granted, like a neck strap (or harness). \r\n\r\nUntil I feel more comfortable with my new sax, I think I\'ll keep using the Neotech harness, but come back to the other two to see what I perfer. Thanks for the article; interesting read.\r\n                                               -Cesar Sabino Nunez',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; U; Android 4.3; en-us; SCH-I535 Build/JSS15J) AppleWebKit/534.30 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4.0 Mobile Safari/534.30',	'',	0,	0),
(102318,	3813,	'james frankie [alto sax]',	'jfs75@hotmail.co.uk',	'',	'86.156.102.100',	'2015-06-02 16:27:42',	'2015-06-02 23:27:42',	'cesar n\r\ngood stuff. enjoyable. write more.\r\nneck s is more convenient, looks better. And one can lift the sax in the air higher and better, and swifter.\r\nHarness more  bulk, more confused to put on, more cost, more mass etc. Some ways of dressing don`t look nice with the H.     Nice having it discretely under a coat or jacket. . `\r\nI can do similar things with both.\r\nBUT I do not tire with my harness. I can play a whole day. I tire within the hr on a neck strap. The feeling of the H on my 2 shoulders is sweet. I feel like playing.           I have personally attached 2 large pads on the shoulder contact points.   jfs [sax, trpt, org, bass g, &amp; org]',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/43.0.2357.81 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(102900,	2161,	'Jeff Ayers',	'jsayers2004@yahoo.com',	'',	'68.119.199.8',	'2015-06-04 07:11:31',	'2015-06-04 14:11:31',	'I have recently fell in love with the \"out of box\" playability of the synthetic reed, maybe its just the convenience factor or Im getting a little older and less patient! Anyway, the only real issue I have had is using them with a Jody Jazz HR piece they tend to quickly build up moisture on the bottom of the reed and give a \"spitty\" sound which drives me a little nuts.     I assume cane does a better job with absorption so you dont get this caveat as much.  Sound wise I have not noticed much loss aside from the wet sound.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_10) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/8.0 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(104476,	3264,	'Jeffrey L. Roche',	'whiskey34me@gmail.com',	'https://thejrdesigns.com',	'107.209.169.86',	'2015-06-08 14:49:26',	'2015-06-08 21:49:26',	'I\'ve played metal Tenor Otto link #6 for 42 years.I believe it was $67 back in 74. Looking for a replacement for Alto. I\'ve played Bundy since 1989. It came with my Buescher. It needs resurfacing. After reading this enlightenment, a replacement sounds exciting.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; U; Android 2.3.6; en-us; Huawei-U8665 Build/HuaweiU8665B037) AppleWebKit/533.1 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4.0 Mobile Safari/533.1',	'',	0,	0),
