(170122,	3630,	'Sarah Y.',	'syork1993@gmail.com',	'',	'50.184.180.49',	'2016-01-06 19:26:04',	'2016-01-07 03:26:04',	'I just got a saxophone from eBay. A Vito Alto Saxophone by Yamaha. The neck piece was NOT as described and is in poor condition. How much would it cost, do you think, to replace the cork on it?\r\nAlso, one of the keys is warped and should be nice and pearly looking, smooth to the touch. Is there a way to smooth that out? Cost?\r\nThirdly and lastly, a couple of the little pads are missing as well as one key does not go down all the way when I play an F. How much would it cost to fix those things?\r\n\r\nThank you!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/47.0.2526.106 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(171491,	4921,	'Daniel',	'Daniel.kr88@gmail.com',	'',	'212.11.105.250',	'2016-01-13 10:22:19',	'2016-01-13 18:22:19',	'Jungleland best sax solo ever by Clarence Big Man Clemons',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/47.0.2526.106 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(171676,	1254,	'Andrew G',	'5450andrew@gmail.com',	'',	'219.89.25.89',	'2016-01-14 11:46:45',	'2016-01-14 19:46:45',	'Great site. I\'m mildly devastated because my 18month old sax needs repadding, costing nearly as much as the sax itself. I use a swab and pad saver every time and brush my teeth before every practise session.  \r\n\r\nI\'m going to use my \"old\" sax as a fingering practise tool, and move to a tenor. BUT I want to ensure the same thing doesn\'t happen again!  \r\n\r\nFrom my bagpipe playing days, I know I\'m a \"wet\" blower.  Bagpipe technicians designed a moisture box which reduced the moisture before the air got to the reeds. I wonder if a similar concept could be used on the sax (replace reeds with pads obviously). Some kind of filter after the mouthpiece? Probably interfere with the air flow too much I suspect.\r\n\r\nIn the interim, I\'ll continue with my regime of swabbing etc. But I was wondering about running a hair dryer (cold setting) over the sax and even using a fan to help dry out the sax?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	0,	0),
(171824,	4982,	'Vasilis',	'vasilistzev@gmail.com',	'',	'2.85.185.63',	'2016-01-15 13:22:53',	'2016-01-15 21:22:53',	'Seems a great app! But is there any way to install it on an Android tablet/phone? :-)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Android 4.4.2; Tablet; rv:43.0) Gecko/43.0 Firefox/43.0',	'',	0,	0),
(171925,	3205,	'Sir Royston',	'roycrosland@hotmail.com',	'',	'94.14.211.135',	'2016-01-16 08:05:09',	'2016-01-16 16:05:09',	'An excellent article. A problem I continually struggle with is when going from octave D (D2, I think) to open C#.  \r\nA song I play regularly goes from low A to Octave D, followed by C#. Transitioning to the D note sounds flat and causes me to struggle to maintain my air support and embouchure. Then when I drop a semi to C#, my adjusted air and embouchure create a horrible sound. Is this common to other people or is it just me? \r\nAnyway, armed with the knowledge picked up from here I can at least start to understand the problem. Who knows? maybe I can even solve it!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/47.0.2526.111 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
