(179844,	3863,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'24.55.15.242',	'2016-04-13 17:48:23',	'2016-04-14 00:48:23',	'Haha, yeah, that is probably the worst troll I\'ve had to deal with on the site, which isn\'t too terrible, so I consider myself very lucky to have such a cool bunch of supportive folks such as yourself checking out that site. So glad you found it helpful!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_3) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/49.0.2623.112 Safari/537.36',	'',	179836,	1),
(179988,	5452,	'Paul van Dun',	'paulvandun@gmail.com',	'',	'84.24.139.239',	'2016-04-15 10:01:22',	'2016-04-15 17:01:22',	'Please don\'t believe this nonsense. It\'s just business and won\'t improve your sound.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_10_5) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/49.0.2623.112 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(179995,	5452,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'206.169.91.210',	'2016-04-15 10:59:07',	'2016-04-15 17:59:07',	'Hello Paul,\r\n\r\nIs this the experience you had when you tried the Klangbogen on your saxophone?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/49.0.2623.112 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(180420,	2161,	'Greg Perry Sr',	'gb4real2@gmail.com',	'',	'192.154.122.250',	'2016-04-20 05:49:50',	'2016-04-20 12:49:50',	'I agree Totally, been playing on them for the past year. The projecting of the sound is unmatched. They have truly been a blessing in disguise for me..',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/49.0.2623.112 Safari/537.36',	'',	1317,	0),
(180581,	4575,	'ANP',	'dark_lord_of_the_sith@hotmail.com',	'',	'73.228.91.79',	'2016-04-21 15:43:19',	'2016-04-21 22:43:19',	'This is really helpful! I\'m really glad I came across this, because I\'ve been needing it recently... I\'ve noticed my sound quality drop like crazy and I have no idea why. So hopefully these will help with that.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; CrOS armv7l 7834.70.0) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/49.0.2623.112 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(180621,	5240,	'Steve',	'bullhead50@yahoo.com',	'',	'173.85.4.16',	'2016-04-22 06:10:26',	'2016-04-22 13:10:26',	'Richer today for having read your interview with Lucas Pino, and listening to his groove. Best, -steve',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 4.3; HUAWEI Y336-A1 Build/HuaweiY336-A1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/46.0.2490.76 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(180635,	5452,	'Leon Zunec',	'leo_zingy@hotmail.com',	'',	'89.142.191.214',	'2016-04-22 11:43:52',	'2016-04-22 18:43:52',	'Will this fit a Yanagisawa A-WO1, which has a completely different position of the lyre holder (lower down, at the side)? How long is the Klangbogen bar - in cm or inches please, \"it\'s quite long\" doesn\'t help :) :) :)  Any info would be greatly appreciated!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.3; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/50.0.2661.87 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(180850,	5452,	'harold pizer',	'haroldpizer@yahoo.com',	'https://haroldpizer@yahoo.com',	'32.214.170.80',	'2016-04-25 13:29:32',	'2016-04-25 20:29:32',	'I\'m not sure this would fit on an old vintage horn such as my Martin Committee Lion &amp; Crown  tenor',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_7_5) AppleWebKit/537.78.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/6.1.6 Safari/537.78.2',	'',	0,	0),
(180852,	1130,	'harold pizer',	'haroldpizer@yahoo.com',	'https://haroldpizer@yahoo.com',	'32.214.170.80',	'2016-04-25 14:28:05',	'2016-04-25 21:28:05',	'Hi Doron and friends. I play on an old Martin Committee tenor, the lion &amp; crown model. Beautiful sounding horn but not ergonomically friendly and the palm keys are hard to play cleanly and precisely even at slow speeds.\r\n       Here\'s what I\'ve been practicing lately in an attempt to bypass as much as possible those left hand palm keys: If I play G, with or without the octave key, it doesn\'t matter, I can produce high D. If I play Ab, again with or w/o the octave key, I can produce high Eb. Playing A will produce high E, Bb will produce high F, and B will produce high F#. \r\n        Using these overtones, I\'ve actually been able to build up speed and for the most part I\'ve been able to avoid playing those left hand palm keys. One thing I haven\'t been able to do however, is to hit altissimo G by playing  the C key. Doron I was just wondering if you or any of your readers have ever experimented with this method ?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_7_5) AppleWebKit/537.78.2 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/6.1.6 Safari/537.78.2',	'',	0,	0),
(180857,	4224,	'Peter Petersburg',	'ott_michael@me.com',	'',	'141.84.69.20',	'2016-04-25 15:42:17',	'2016-04-25 22:42:17',	'These look a lot like the daily exercises by H. Klosé. I will stay with the latter, since they are specifically for saxophone, so I don\'t have to struggle with notes out of my flagolett range.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/50.0.2661.75 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(180883,	5452,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'206.169.91.210',	'2016-04-26 14:09:29',	'2016-04-26 21:09:29',	'Do you have a picture of your tenor since the lyre holder insert seems to be a bit different on each horn.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/49.0.2623.112 Safari/537.36',	'',	180850,	0),
(180884,	5452,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'206.169.91.210',	'2016-04-26 14:10:45',	'2016-04-26 21:10:45',	'The Klangbogen fit my Yanagisawa 991 tenor fine. I will let you know when I hear back from Mauro with his feedback.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/49.0.2623.112 Safari/537.36',	'',	180635,	0),
(180908,	337,	'prince',	'princeston.sean@gmail.com',	'',	'197.251.163.204',	'2016-04-27 05:23:57',	'2016-04-27 11:23:57',	'i really want a professional selmer tenor saxophone who can buy me one am in africa',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; WOW64; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0',	'',	0,	0),
(181294,	1797,	'Vassilis',	'vasilistzev@gmail.com',	'',	'2.85.179.196',	'2016-05-04 04:53:31',	'2016-05-04 11:53:31',	'Hello Doron, thank you for that useful article! \r\n\r\nDo you have any advice about how to play in tune in the altissimo register? I can play the 3 first notes of altissimo. G sounds great, but G#  and A sound really sharp. Should I search for another fingering?\r\n\r\nVassilis',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 4.4.2; Lenovo B6000-F Build/KOT49H) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4.0 Chrome/30.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(181584,	4267,	'Michael John Alexander',	'vantagemusic1@gmail.com',	'',	'41.145.153.198',	'2016-05-08 11:28:46',	'2016-05-08 17:28:46',	'Thank you for generously sharing this information. A great resource which both my students and myself appreciate.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/50.0.2661.94 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(182272,	1937,	'Autumn',	'daunlessresa82@gmail.com',	'',	'12.23.76.3',	'2016-05-19 15:30:24',	'2016-05-19 22:30:24',	'So to growl is kinda like purring into my mouthpiece?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_9_5) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/50.0.2661.102 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(182315,	1797,	'Ronaldo',	'ronaldopetoral@aol.com',	'',	'69.114.21.146',	'2016-05-20 06:10:41',	'2016-05-20 13:10:41',	'I was challenged to pick up sax again recently because of the altissimos. I gave up multiple times playing high registers. But this time since there are so many info on the internet, and of course persistent practice, I finally able to play comfortably up to D. That\'s exactly 3 weeks after picking up the saxophone back again.  Now, I started practicing sax everyday and very slowly improving my overall playing. This site gave me lots of info about sax playing. Long overtones is the key. Thanks Doron... Btw, I\'m a pro guitar player not sax. :)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_10_3) AppleWebKit/600.5.17 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/8.0.5 Safari/600.5.17',	'',	0,	0),
(182434,	337,	'onowu ifeanyi',	'sammyo2000@yahoo.com',	'',	'8.37.230.149',	'2016-05-23 02:22:28',	'2016-05-23 09:22:28',	'Please I don\'t know d difference bw saxophones...how d u note a selmer saxophone',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; U; Android 5.1; en-US; INFINIX-X551 Build/LMY47I) AppleWebKit/534.30 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4.0 UCBrowser/10.9.0.731 U3/0.8.0 Mobile Safari/534.30',	'',	0,	0),
(182517,	1797,	'James f',	'Jfs75@hotmail.co.uk',	'',	'86.131.67.60',	'2016-05-24 14:03:19',	'2016-05-24 21:03:19',	'For me, the employment of diaphragm , it\'s awareness , breathing powerfully from it, like panting,is the topmost thing to grasp.\r\nThen after is how to do careful research in very organised and scientific manner. Get many blank charts for entering fingerings . Get all , many of the Internet fingerings. Try all, all. Go not with a loaded belly. Speed great r and d in the woodshed. Keep water for throat.\r\nSuck in your belly to pressure the air, and give it speed.\r\nSomething must happen. Guaranteed .',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 9_0_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.0 Mobile/13A452 Safari/601.1',	'',	0,	0),
(182518,	1797,	'James f',	'Jfs75@hotmail.co.uk',	'',	'86.131.67.60',	'2016-05-24 14:10:17',	'2016-05-24 21:10:17',	'S. Series 3. Alto\r\nVandoren mpc V16 A7M\r\nVandoren leather ligature.\r\nReeds: Vandoren Java 2 , green box\r\nRange: 4 octaves and a few.\r\nGenre: hymns and anthems to God.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 9_0_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.0 Mobile/13A452 Safari/601.1',	'',	0,	0),
(182519,	1937,	'James f',	'Jfs75@hotmail.co.uk',	'',	'86.131.67.60',	'2016-05-24 14:16:35',	'2016-05-24 21:16:35',	'Sure bet he is right,\r\nBalding.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 9_0_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.0 Mobile/13A452 Safari/601.1',	'',	0,	0),
(182861,	4854,	'Mark Taylor',	'mark@taylormademusic.com.au',	'https://marktaylor.com.au',	'121.209.235.115',	'2016-05-31 06:04:52',	'2016-05-31 12:04:52',	'Great article Zach, thanks!\r\nAlso great to read the comments with those additional names mentioned. \r\n\r\nI concur about John Reilly in Los Angeles.\r\nHe has done some excellent refacing and customising for me on several pieces. \r\nJohn has a website: https://www.jrmpcdr.com/\r\n\r\nAlso in LA, studio woodwind player John Yoakum is highly respected for his mouthpiece refacing work. \r\n\r\nAnother guy in New York who comes extremely highly recommended and is very highly regarded by many of the top Broadway, studio and jazz players there is Scott Shachter.\r\n[Sorry(!), but this web page has disappeared since the original publication of this article]\r\n\r\nAmongst many great players, he was working on some of Michael Brecker\'s mouthpieces prior to Mike\'s illness and passing. \r\n\r\nHere in Australia, Gabriel Vatavu is outstanding!.\r\ngabrielvatavurepairs.com/mouthpiece.php',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 9_3_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.0 Mobile/13F69 Safari/601.1',	'',	0,	0),
(183028,	337,	'Tatiana',	'tatiana.oszczypok@gmail.com',	'',	'139.216.173.17',	'2016-06-02 20:56:42',	'2016-06-03 03:56:42',	'Looking to buy a selmer 500 series baritone sax for my son.  What price range should I look for in Australian $ or US $ and I\'ll convert. He\'s played a Yamaha student sax for 3 years. Is the selmer a good option to buy?\r\nThanks',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 4.4.2; en-au; SAMSUNG SM-G900I Build/KOT49H) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/1.6 Chrome/28.0.1500.94 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(183057,	3630,	'Isai Sanchez',	'sanchezisai0108@gmail.com',	'',	'209.65.145.46',	'2016-06-03 11:05:49',	'2016-06-03 18:05:49',	'Hi, I recently became acquainted with a Buescher True Tone alto sax that i believe needs new pads and springs plus thorough cleaning it is also loosing its paint and lacquer, but if that\'s no harm its fine any suggestions on who i can turn to for this job and maybe how much the price could be ? I\'m From West Texas. Thank You.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/50.0.2661.102 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(183173,	4854,	'J. Dennis',	'j.dennisarceo@gmail.com',	'https://www.jdennisarceo.com',	'112.205.135.1',	'2016-06-05 11:19:12',	'2016-06-05 18:19:12',	'It was actually surprising not to see Jennifer Price on the list. She, as not too many people know, was actually the brians behind Guardalla mouthpieces. The very famous and well imitated sound of Michael Brecker\'s was produced using a Guardalla piece. She now has her own line of mouthpieces called Vigilante.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 9_3_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Mobile/13F69 [FBAN/FBIOS;FBAV/56.0.0.58.135;FBBV/30582859;FBRV/0;FBDV/iPhone7,2;FBMD/iPhone;FBSN/iPhone OS;FBSV/9.3.2;FBSS/2;FBCR/Globe;FBID/phone;FBLC/en_US',	'',	0,	0),
(183180,	4854,	'Zachary M Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'107.201.109.91',	'2016-06-05 12:59:49',	'2016-06-05 19:59:49',	'Hello J Dennis,\r\n\r\nThanks for the update. This is a working list and there have been many more mouthpiece re-facers hitting the scene that do deserve credit as well. I have heard great things about Jennifer\'s work but have not had the chance to try one of her mouthpieces yet.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/50.0.2661.102 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(183184,	1098,	'Louis Gerrits',	'louisgerrits@gmail.com',	'https://www.michaelbreckerliverecordings.com',	'82.95.184.243',	'2016-06-05 14:26:35',	'2016-06-05 21:26:35',	'Thanks again Doron for doing the interview! Things have changed again 5 years later. The website is still there, but the Facebook page is more alive then ever. https://www.facebook.com/groups/michael.brecker/\r\n\r\nHope all is well.\r\n\r\nLouis',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_5) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/50.0.2661.102 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(183198,	1098,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'70.113.101.140',	'2016-06-05 20:13:25',	'2016-06-06 03:13:25',	'Hey Louis! Yeah, I\'ve noticed the amount of activity on the FB page, amazing work you\'ve done there. I\'ll add the link to the post. \r\n\r\nBTW, I still think you should make a documentary on Brecker, it would truly be an amazing story to share. :)\r\n\r\nI hope you\'re doing great otherwise,\r\n\r\nD',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/51.0.2704.79 Safari/537.36',	'',	183184,	1),
(183203,	4854,	'Lalo Rojas',	'lalorojassax@gmail.com',	'',	'190.53.69.187',	'2016-06-05 22:37:54',	'2016-06-06 04:37:54',	'These are some more names to add to this great list...\r\n\r\nFred Lamberson\r\n\r\nJohannes Gerber\r\n\r\nJoe Giardullo\r\n\r\nJohn Thomas',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 9_3_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Mobile/13E238 [FBAN/MessengerForiOS;FBAV/73.0.0.33.71;FBBV/31011105;FBRV/0;FBDV/iPhone8,2;FBMD/iPhone;FBSN/iPhone OS;FBSV/9.3.1;FBSS/3;FBCR/TIGOHND;FBID/phon',	'',	0,	0),
