(194499,	1895,	'Byron',	'bathoma1@att.net',	'',	'70.197.7.221',	'2016-10-10 13:36:53',	'2016-10-10 20:36:53',	'I am trying to play my altissimo g I currently use a number 3 Alexander especial tenor would a 3-1/2 work better',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 4.4.4; XT1080 Build/SU6-7.7) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/37.0.2062.117 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(194652,	3630,	'Jade',	'tigersrule.neal9@gmail.com',	'',	'199.212.86.133',	'2016-10-12 08:45:15',	'2016-10-12 15:45:15',	'I\'ve been playing Alto Sax in my high school\'s band for a few weeks now. The one I\'m using sounded fine until I cleaned it, and now it squeaks every other note I produce. I didn\'t tighten any screws, or did anything wierd, I just cleaned it because it needed to be. I also recently started using Rico reeds at 2 Strength',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 4.4.2; SCH-R890 Build/KOT49H) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/53.0.2785.124 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(195145,	196,	'Luke Yancey',	'lukasyancee@gmail.com',	'https://www.devoesmusic.net/default.aspx',	'107.150.75.134',	'2016-10-18 05:43:28',	'2016-10-18 12:43:28',	'I didn\'t know that saxophones could range up to $4,000! I thought it would maybe cost $700 at most. Maybe I am better off renting one instead. Thank you for the average prices!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/53.0.2785.143 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(195194,	5781,	'Andy Geiger',	'ageiger@olypen.com',	'',	'71.35.97.233',	'2016-10-18 19:36:44',	'2016-10-19 02:36:44',	'I have a Cory Bros. Tone Tablet. I am delighted with the improved projection, warmth, and response I am experiencing. Well worth the modest investment!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 10_0_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/602.1.50 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14A456 Safari/602.1',	'',	0,	0),
(195199,	2502,	'Angelo',	'alopez380@msn.com',	'',	'63.152.117.82',	'2016-10-18 20:07:51',	'2016-10-19 03:07:51',	'I have an old Selmer C* but it has oxidated and has teeth marks on the bill. I would like to get it to you to see if it can be put back into shape. \'\'Tks For your help.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 10_0_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/600.1.4 (KHTML, like Gecko) GSA/19.0.133715217 Mobile/14A456 Safari/600.1.4',	'',	0,	0),
(195334,	5713,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.147.121',	'2016-10-20 09:55:17',	'2016-10-20 16:55:17',	'My Cannonball tenor has a metal thumb hook mainly because the horn is kind of a retro horn. Has a big bell, subtones great etc, etc and really projects and has a sound. However my Selmer Mk VI 214,xxx has a lastic thumb hook. It really projects too, has  a nice subtone and really has a sound too but different and has a standard bell. Does the thumb hook make a difference, I don\'t know? Sax Alley also sells a metal thumb hook that Tim says really boost your sound. The old horns had metal thumb hooks mostly because plastic was not in wide use in the 1930\'s or 40\'s. I say, if it works for you use it. However I try not not to be obsessed about this stuff. Heck I play pro and teach and I still use Rico reeds, a FL metal Link mpc w/a Selemer lig and it works great for me. To quote Michael Brecker when he gave a wrkshp at my Navy Band. \"If it works for you, use it and don\'t go nuts about it.\" geez Brecker was using LaVoz med tenor reeds and a Selmer lig in 2003.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:48.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/48.0',	'',	0,	0),
(195373,	3827,	'Nathan',	'Nathanararatwatson@hotmail.com',	'',	'108.196.161.120',	'2016-10-20 18:48:36',	'2016-10-21 01:48:36',	'I am very interested in the Navarro mouthpieces. But with all of the different lines and different cutaways it\'s hard to make a decision without being able to try them. I live in the Atlanta area. Do you know of any place near me that has a selection of such mouthpieces that I could try?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 10_0_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/602.1.50 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14A456 Safari/602.1',	'',	0,	0),
(195581,	2809,	'Mario Curtis',	'mario.curtis@hotmail.co.uk',	'',	'86.154.169.252',	'2016-10-23 02:15:18',	'2016-10-23 09:15:18',	'I may have missed this in the replies - does the saxophone sound affect the players own hearing over time? Many electric guitar players and rock singers wear earpieces to lessen the potential damage to hearing. Any thoughts? Also as a relative newcomer to the sax I can\'t actually gauge the volume to expect when I play.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; SAMSUNG SM-T800 Build/MMB29K) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) SamsungBrowser/4.0 Chrome/44.0.2403.133 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(195671,	3933,	'richard ross',	'richardsaxross@yahoo.com',	'https://richardsaxross.com',	'108.74.175.49',	'2016-10-24 06:12:18',	'2016-10-24 13:12:18',	'great jazz sound on both!, But the Amma sounds more refined, fatter and darker, better in tune and as if it\'s easier to control and articulate',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_10_5) AppleWebKit/600.8.9 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/8.0.8 Safari/600.8.9',	'',	0,	0),
