(198607,	337,	'Chris',	'bebopdesign@comcast.net',	'',	'50.129.122.80',	'2016-11-28 19:52:32',	'2016-11-29 03:52:32',	'Selmer USA models were made in Elkhart Indiana until i believe they transitioned from the AS100 series to the AS110. not sure exactly on the timing of that though. I have an AS100...it was the pro USA model for Selmer, I consider it a high end intermediate or an entry pro.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/54.0.2840.99 Safari/537.36',	'',	2737,	0),
(199242,	4575,	'J.Q.',	'jequer@gmail.com',	'',	'200.152.99.93',	'2016-12-05 13:27:58',	'2016-12-05 21:27:58',	'Hi, I\'m playing for a year... I\'m having a hard time finding music sheets with more than the \"Head\"; I know I am supposed to learn the head and then create my own stuff, but it is too soon for that I am afraid... Then I listen how big players do it, I see how they take the head which last 30 seconds and make it into a 10 mins solo! It is very slow for my try to figure out the notes the play\r\n\r\nSo,,,, can you recomend me a website where to find it? I.E. Music sheet transcription from Charlie Parker playin now is time, full transcription, not just the head!\r\n\r\nThank u all in advance!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/54.0.2840.99 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(199515,	3863,	'ash',	'ashleylauren445@gmail.com',	'',	'50.29.104.202',	'2016-12-08 15:09:08',	'2016-12-08 23:09:08',	'what is the paper called that goes your lower lip. _____film, is the name of one but i cant seem to find it.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_6) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/54.0.2840.98 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(199601,	1596,	'Shennaya',	'shennykretschmer@gmail.com',	'',	'162.157.78.252',	'2016-12-09 13:03:48',	'2016-12-09 21:03:48',	'This is mind blowing!! I had no idea about playing with your lip out! I\'ve been a musician for 11 years ( im 18) and have been paying tenor sax for 3 now. I\'ve only ever known tucking in your bottom lip to play! I\'m defiantly going to try this! This is amazing!!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 10_1_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/602.2.14 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14B100 Safari/602.1',	'',	0,	0),
(199697,	2161,	'VortexLimited',	'kyboi64@gmail.com',	'',	'107.77.87.34',	'2016-12-10 11:17:07',	'2016-12-10 19:17:07',	'I play on tenor sax and I\'ve had a 3.5 rico reserve last for 14 months. When it finally wore out(tonally) I had to buy a vandoren until I could find another box of reserves and that thing broke in 3 days. I learn that vandorens are crap, and now only play on Rico Royal or Reserves.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 5.0.2; LG-V410 Build/LRX22G) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/53.0.2785.124 Safari/537.36',	'',	1324,	0),
(200025,	3630,	'Garnett Johnson',	'goats04@yahoo.ca',	'',	'201.160.135.75',	'2016-12-14 06:35:14',	'2016-12-14 14:35:14',	'Hi Matt  My octave does not work when I press my left ring finger ?Got any suggestions ?It seems to me it envoles the upper parts.Thanks,and belated Congradulations .',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 9_3_5 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.0 Mobile/13G36 Safari/601.1',	'',	0,	0),
(200208,	2809,	'Christina',	'christina02@gmail.com',	'',	'104.254.252.50',	'2016-12-16 15:49:10',	'2016-12-16 23:49:10',	'My upstairs neighbor is a professional saxophone player.  I absolutely cannot stand the sound of the saxophone anymore.  He practices scales or whatever over and over and over and hours at a time and it drives me crazy.  Duh Nuh Nuh Nuh Nuuuuuhhhhhh... Duh Nuh Nuh Nuh Nuuuuuhhhhhh... Duh Nuh Nuh Nuh Nuuuuuhhhhhh... Duh Nuh Nuh Nuh Nuuuuuhhhhhh... Duh Nuh Nuh Nuh Nuuuuuhhhhhh... Duh Nuh Nuh Nuh Nuuuuuhhhhhh... Duh Nuh Nuh Nuh Nuuuuuhhhhhh... I want to break the sax over his head.  Now over the years, we\'ve both tried to rectify this situation.  He got a whisper box, but it was still too loud.  He further padded the box, but the sound still resonates.  He\'s done the best he can and I get that, but it\'s still not good enough.  I can deal with normal sounds - music, tv, stomping around - but no one should be subjected to this nor be expected to tolerate it.  So my advice to all you in this comment section - If you are buying a condo or renting an apartment, get one on the first floor so you don\'t torture your downstairs neighbor.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0',	'',	0,	0),
(200232,	337,	'Jaye Libeccio',	'Firebladejay@aol.com',	'',	'86.162.1.233',	'2016-12-17 00:30:21',	'2016-12-17 08:30:21',	'My father who passed away in 1987 used to regularly play his selmer tenor sax at Ronnie Scott\'s, (personal friend of dad..rip) .\r\nRonnie played it a few times, and so did some other faces on the jazz scene, proof (getz) .\r\nThe sax shows serial number 17001.\r\nRequires couple of pads, couple of springs sticky \r\nAm going to sell this as I don\'t play it, my children don\'t have interest, nor my grandkids .\r\nWhat would be the value of this sax?.\r\nI intend to give money to Huntingdon s disease association as my dad died of this condition in 1987 aged 59.\r\n\r\nHe owned that sax for at least 20 years prior to passing away.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 4.4.3; KFTHWI Build/KTU84M) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Silk/54.3.1 like Chrome/54.0.2840.85 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(200561,	3827,	'Steven Redd',	'ssredd@bellsouth.net',	'',	'99.113.144.215',	'2016-12-20 08:04:46',	'2016-12-20 16:04:46',	'Just another voice to remind people to *NOT* deal with Steve Goodson of New Orleans.  He is a complete piece of garbage who stole a Selmer Mark VII from me that I left with him in the late 90s on an agreement for consignment sale.  I still have the original paperwork written in his own hand that he subsequently lied about and claimed that it wasn\'t anything he recognized.\r\n\r\nSteve Goodson is a liar and a thief.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/55.0.2883.87 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(200592,	1974,	'Steve Sax',	'sax2481@gmail.com',	'https://www.saxsupport.com.au',	'103.39.84.27',	'2016-12-20 17:43:09',	'2016-12-21 01:43:09',	'Hi check out the SaXSupport web site, the support enables correct posture.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 9_3_5 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.0 Mobile/13G36 Safari/601.1',	'',	0,	0),
(200777,	5732,	'Matthew',	'robynandmatt@hotmail.com',	'https://SaxophoneTShirts.com',	'165.225.98.89',	'2016-12-22 20:29:51',	'2016-12-23 04:29:51',	'Hi Simon,\r\nThanks for the sax recording tips.  Personally, I find that if I place my mic approx 2 feet away and pointing towards the main middle fingering section of (ie left hand little pinky finger and right hand pointer finger) the sax.  Maybe it\'s my room, or my mic, or both, but this gives me the best compromise on high vs low frequencies and balance.\r\nThanks again,\r\nMatthew\r\n(Melbourne, Australia)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; rv:45.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/45.0',	'',	0,	0),
(201607,	694,	'Geo',	'saxiphonium@yahoo.com',	'',	'68.170.181.181',	'2016-12-31 11:48:27',	'2016-12-31 19:48:27',	'Eve,\r\n\r\nI don\'t think it is a good idea to run your mouthpiece through a dishwasher. The detergents are very strong and the temps get pretty high. Both of which MAY, operative term here, cause damage to your mouthpiece',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.3; WOW64; rv:50.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/50.0',	'',	0,	0),
(201608,	337,	'alan',	'smoothscales@gmail.com',	'',	'45.56.43.179',	'2016-12-31 12:47:29',	'2016-12-31 20:47:29',	'Jaye, I am interested in the horn.  Could you send me an email of pictures?  smoothscales@gmail.com',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_10_5) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/54.0.2840.98 Safari/537.36',	'',	200232,	0),
(202156,	5173,	'Malcolm K Williams, Jr.',	'kwsaxman9@gmail.com',	'',	'208.119.81.90',	'2017-01-07 09:45:05',	'2017-01-07 15:45:05',	'I have played the sax for 44 years.  I like Selmer Paris Saxophones the best.\r\nI play on a Lost Wax alto mourthpiece and a Beechler Tenor Mpouthpi3ece with 1 and 1/2 Plasticover reeds. I have a Sopranino and a C Soprano sax as well, but are not played as much. I once performed 7 nights a week, but now mostly just play in churches and at a Christian Rehab that I have worked at for the last 14 years.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; rv:22.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/22.0',	'',	0,	0),
(202425,	337,	'tony',	'ninocapra@ymail.com',	'',	'174.88.22.192',	'2017-01-10 21:50:39',	'2017-01-11 05:50:39',	'i would like to see pictures or even skype I am interested in the horn. My condolences for your dad ,much too young ! I\'m in Toronto Ontario, Canada',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_12_2) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/55.0.2883.95 Safari/537.36',	'',	200232,	0),
(202446,	3899,	'AG',	'alaingueben@gmail.com',	'',	'91.177.149.37',	'2017-01-11 03:02:10',	'2017-01-11 11:02:10',	'Tip #12: sell it and buy a trumpet...',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	0,	0),
(202760,	337,	'Smitty',	'Europoljuice@gmail.com',	'',	'71.3.101.141',	'2017-01-15 16:34:24',	'2017-01-16 00:34:24',	'I just picked up a Alto AS-100 and I can\'t seem to find any info on the Ser, #.  It does say USA on the Bell. Any idea where I can find out any other info. Here is the #829121.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/55.0.2883.87 Safari/537.36',	'',	198607,	0),
(202892,	4854,	'Joseph Delossantos',	'jdelossantos9six@gmail.com',	'',	'158.222.175.206',	'2017-01-17 17:02:42',	'2017-01-18 01:02:42',	'Add Matt Marantz to the list!! He refaced my jody jazz HR 7M and the tone on it feels great!!!!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/55.0.2883.87 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(203022,	4755,	'George',	'bpmusic@snet.net',	'',	'72.10.100.2',	'2017-01-20 06:37:08',	'2017-01-20 14:37:08',	'Hi, I am not a sax player, so I am a little confused about the bis key. You said: \"You use the same finger you use to finger the B (your index finger, or what would actually be referred to as LH1 in most fingering charts, since it’s the top finger of the left hand).\" I tried this and I can\'t get a Bb unless I press down the B key with the index finger AND the bis key with the LH2  (Could you clear this up?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/55.0.2883.87 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(203086,	3881,	'Troy W',	'Willtech61@gmail.com',	'',	'50.53.111.96',	'2017-01-21 18:21:26',	'2017-01-22 02:21:26',	'I\'ve mostly played Bari in all the big bands I have been fortunate to work with. It is a tricky part at times. One moment, you have a nice ensemble sound with your four brothers. Next you are the fifth bone and then other times you are with the string bass or whatever. Dynamics, intonation and volume are key. In one group, the lead alto said to play out more. The 2nd tenor however, helped me kind of keep it in line. I wanted to be a good neighbor, so it all worked out well!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 10_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/602.3.12 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14C92 Safari/602.1',	'',	0,	0),
(203162,	3630,	'Tristin',	'dammy0075@yahoo.com',	'',	'107.167.99.234',	'2017-01-23 16:34:15',	'2017-01-24 00:34:15',	'pls what kind of paint is used to spray a saxophone???',	0,	'1',	'Opera/9.80 (Android; Opera Mini/7.0.31782/37.9311; U; en) Presto/2.12.423 Version/12.16',	'',	0,	0),
(203337,	3630,	'Trevor',	'Midiguana@aol.com',	'https://Www.midnightiguana.com',	'107.77.94.116',	'2017-01-26 13:20:45',	'2017-01-26 21:20:45',	'Hi Joe. Never have a saxophone relaquered ( replated) it ruins the sound and value and even if you can locate someone still willing to do it it will cost an arm and leg. Saxes look cool with a mixed used patina . Never relaquer !!!\r\n????????',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 9_3_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.0 Mobile/13F69 Safari/601.1',	'',	8674,	0),
(203338,	3630,	'Trevor',	'Midiguana@aol.com',	'https://Www.midnightiguana.com',	'107.77.90.57',	'2017-01-26 13:28:40',	'2017-01-26 21:28:40',	'Hi Jade ,\r\nHow did you clean it ? A sax should be swabbed out EVERY time after you finish playing so moisture doesn\'t ruin your pads . \r\nI worked at a music store for many years and people would come in all the time that had put a woodwind instrument into the bath tub because it had gotten a bit smelly. That ruined All the pads and a complete pad replacement was usually necessary . Hopefully you didn\'t give you sax a bath ????',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 9_3_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.0 Mobile/13F69 Safari/601.1',	'',	194652,	0),
(203339,	3630,	'Trevor',	'Midiguana@aol.com',	'https://Www.midnightiguana.com',	'107.77.90.57',	'2017-01-26 13:31:26',	'2017-01-26 21:31:26',	'Not anything you can do yourself so Pleeeeease don\'t spray paint your sax !!!!!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 9_3_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.0 Mobile/13F69 Safari/601.1',	'',	203162,	0),
(203452,	5892,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.147.121',	'2017-01-28 20:03:02',	'2017-01-29 04:03:02',	'I heard Semaus play at the Saxophone Symposium several years ago. He played great.However at that point he said he was using a 1940\'s HR Otto Link Reso mpc. I wonder why the switch, he sounded great, just as good in the video above. He was using the Selmer Super Balanced Action from the late 40\'s or early 50\'s.He was also using the Roberto RW Reeds, as was Chris Potter the following year. However Chris said he switched back and forth between RW reeds and Rico Jazz Select Reeds. ANyway just wondering about the mpc. Ted Klum\'s mpc\'s are EXPENSIVE!!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:48.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/48.0',	'',	0,	0),
(203497,	5892,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zach@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'',	'107.201.109.91',	'2017-01-29 13:09:16',	'2017-01-29 21:09:16',	'Hello Larry,\r\n\r\nSeamus has also liked his reso chamber link but Ted\'s mouthpieces work for him. I really like Ted\'s work and am looking to check out the same mouthpiece Seamus is playing but in a 7 tip opening to see how it compares to my hard rubber slant link. Hoping to find a back-up to my link. Ted\'s mouthpieces are on the higher end of the price spectrum but if one of Ted\'s mouthpieces works extremely well for you, then you in theory would never have to purchase a new mouthpiece ever again unless the piece was damaged, lost, or stolen.  I would definitely check out one of Ted\'s mouthpieces if you are in the market for a back-up or replacement. Ted does great work.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/55.0.2883.87 Safari/537.36',	'',	203452,	0),
(203512,	4344,	'Steve Sax',	'sax2481@gmail.com',	'https://www.saxsupport.com.au',	'67.1.184.182',	'2017-01-29 21:01:09',	'2017-01-30 05:01:09',	'Hi\r\n\r\nI have been playing Bari for a number of years and getting more and more back pain, especially after a long gig.\r\n\r\nSo rather than try and reinvent the sling I went for a method that supports the sax by transferring the weigh directly to the ground.\r\n\r\nThe SaxSupport is a simple, easy to assemble, inexpensive solution to this problem.\r\n\r\nFor more information please refer to www.saxsupport.com.au or email me direct sax2481@gmail.com',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 9_3_5 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.0 Mobile/13G36 Safari/601.1',	'',	0,	0),
(203622,	1031,	'tik',	'ccie0007@hotmail.com',	'',	'109.157.27.141',	'2017-01-31 12:48:39',	'2017-01-31 20:48:39',	'Hello Mate,\r\n                     In exercise 3 we have to play middle F and with Bb key we have hit middle F right? i got this bit.Again hit middle F with middle F key but after that play middle F with low b key or Bb key?sorry i am learning.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.3; WOW64; rv:51.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/51.0',	'',	0,	0),
(203623,	1031,	'tik',	'ccie0007@hotmail.com',	'',	'109.157.27.141',	'2017-01-31 12:56:12',	'2017-01-31 20:56:12',	'I got it now bymyself.cheers anyway.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.3; WOW64; rv:51.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/51.0',	'',	0,	0),
(203628,	3630,	'Tristin',	'dammy0075@yahoo.com',	'',	'107.167.113.6',	'2017-01-31 16:20:20',	'2017-02-01 00:20:20',	'thanks Trevor............ I don\'t wanna spray it myself, I just wanna have an inkling on the kind of paint used in spraying ití ½í¸£í ½í¸£í ½í¸£',	0,	'1',	'Opera/9.80 (Android; Opera Mini/7.0.31782/37.9339; U; en) Presto/2.12.423 Version/12.16',	'',	0,	0),
(203761,	5892,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.147.121',	'2017-02-02 17:58:10',	'2017-02-03 01:58:10',	'Zach: Not really in the market for it and could not afford a Ted Klum mpc anyway. For backup I have a current HR Link that was adjusted by John Reilly of Hollywood, CA. I also have a HR CE Winds B stock HR \"The Sig\" that plays well. It is a Link knockoff. My Main mpc is a metal FL Otto Link 8* from the mid-1960\'s that I bought used from a retired Army Band guy for $50.00 bucks. The best $50.00 dollars I every spent. I bought it around \'90 or \'91 before E bay and the net were there. I feel that Ebay is responsible for the inflated prices of Links, Mk VI\'s etc. I met a guy at the Sax Symposium at GMU a few yrs back. He had a metal 8* just like mine by he spent $500.00 for it. He was shocked when I told him what I spent. Because you review for this site I assume that you get a good break on a lot of products. From your articles I gather that a lot of guys send you samples of their products.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:48.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/48.0',	'',	0,	0),
(203768,	5892,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zach@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'',	'107.201.109.91',	'2017-02-02 19:15:29',	'2017-02-03 03:15:29',	'Hello Larry,\r\n\r\nUnderstood. I do receive quite a bit of products to test play but mostly send them back unless if I want to purchase an item I pay the current price or a bit less depending on the condition of the mouthpiece sent (new, slightly used, or test). I have stuck with the same vintage HR link for quite some time but am always looking for a back-up or simply a good mouthpiece.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/55.0.2883.87 Safari/537.36',	'',	203761,	0),
(203822,	5892,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.147.121',	'2017-02-03 14:24:35',	'2017-02-03 22:24:35',	'Zach: The search is eternal. I believe that once you find a good mpc and horn that you should just stick w/it and practice. Zoot stuck w/the same mpc forever. Dexter the same for the most part. The only reason he switched horns and mpcs is because his Conn 10M and Dukoff Hollywood were stolen in Paris and not made any more at the time of the thief. So he went w/a Selmer Mk VI and an Metal Otto Link around a 8 or 8*. Then he just stuck w/it. His friends Sonny Stitt and Johnny Griffin were playing the same basic setup. Although for a while I believe Johnny played a King Super 20.\r\n\r\nI believe and tell students this, buy the best horn you can afford, the same for mpcs. Now if they are just so-so or junkers then yeah they will have to upgrade down the line.\r\n\r\nThe thing 1 would like to know is why so many guys switched from the Selmer Super Balanced Action to the Mark VI? Was the VI so much better? All the SBA\'s I\'ve played play so much better in the lower register than the VI. Maybe the intonation on the VI is better. All I know s that all the studio guys play VI\'s as well as most of the jazz guys. Getz and others made the switch. The 1 guy who did not switch was Ben Webster even though Selmer was going to give him a MK VI. I think Ben may have graciously accepted the present but still played the SBA. I heard he gave his VI to Dexter after Dexter\'s Conn10M was stolen. Okay enough stories.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:48.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/48.0',	'',	0,	0),
(203922,	196,	'David Nichols',	'Dnnjax1@yahoo.com',	'',	'73.208.98.63',	'2017-02-05 09:32:09',	'2017-02-05 17:32:09',	'Doran, \r\nI am an adult thinking of learning to play the sax.  I just received my sisters tenor sax.  We bought it for her when we lived in Japan in the early 80\'s.  She went on to play in the USC Trojan Marching Band.    I had a local shop repad/cork it.  They said it was in very good playing condition despite the exterior scratches.\r\n\r\nIt is a Yamaha YTS-32 with a purple stenciled logo. \r\nCan you tell me anything about this horn?\r\n\r\nMany thanks,\r\nDavid',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; SM-G920P Build/MMB29K) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/56.0.2924.87 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(204070,	3899,	'Constance',	'Avery@assurancefamily.com',	'',	'208.54.80.223',	'2017-02-07 04:19:54',	'2017-02-07 12:19:54',	'Well, learning multiple instruments would help one get better on all instruments so learning the trumpet too wouldn\'t be too bad. But I definitely wouldn\'t sell a saxophone to pay for a trumpet. (There are many other ways to conserve money! ;))',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 10_2_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/602.4.6 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14D27 Safari/602.1',	'',	202446,	0),
(204153,	1895,	'Paul',	'paulthomas0003@gmail.com',	'',	'137.97.206.183',	'2017-02-07 20:04:36',	'2017-02-08 04:04:36',	'suggest food habits tht affect throat or that open up throat...iam a worship leader and while singing i cant take up high pitch and my sound is going while singing..',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 4.4.4; SM-E700H Build/KTU84P) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/40.0.2214.109 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(204398,	5811,	'Mike',	'mtkin@btinternet.com',	'',	'77.234.43.153',	'2017-02-10 08:43:02',	'2017-02-10 16:43:02',	'Tough exercise, particularly reading the flat keys',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 10_2_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/602.4.6 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14D27 Safari/602.1',	'',	0,	0),
(204790,	5335,	'Podgora Sea',	'borratko@gmail.com',	'',	'212.92.205.241',	'2017-02-15 00:46:59',	'2017-02-15 06:46:59',	'I played the trumpet, and my daughter played a flute. I always loved sax, and as my neighbour played a clarinet - he always loved to play a saxophone, in the time of sunset :) that was like in the movie!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.3) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/56.0.2924.87 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(204933,	3863,	'Khanika Sharma',	'khanikasharma357@gmail.com',	'https://khanika.in',	'103.253.153.82',	'2017-02-18 01:27:44',	'2017-02-18 09:27:44',	'Thanks for sharing such an informative article. I really feel very good to come on your post.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; rv:47.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/47.0',	'',	0,	0),
(205074,	4267,	'agboola omotayo sax',	'omotayorsax@gmail.com',	'',	'141.0.14.210',	'2017-02-22 11:48:37',	'2017-02-22 17:48:37',	'Thank you for your sharing',	0,	'1',	'Opera/9.80 (BlackBerry; Opera Mini/8.0.35659/57.135; U; en) Presto/2.12.423 Version/12.16',	'',	0,	0),
(205288,	3881,	'Mickey Capuano',	'mickeycapuano@suddenlink.net',	'',	'47.215.108.231',	'2017-02-23 22:27:05',	'2017-02-24 06:27:05',	'Artie shaw\'s band is all you say and I agree but Glenn millers orchestra topped the charts featuring the reed section. He had a clarinet play over four saxophones, usually the clarinet and lead tenor played melody. Willie Swartz and Tex beneke were great and Hal McIntyre had lead alto that put this bands sound on top of the charts during the height of this wonderful era.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 10_2_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/602.4.6 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14D27 Safari/602.1',	'',	0,	0),
(205303,	3486,	'mart winston',	'plooky6479@gmail.com',	'https://plooky6479@gmail.com',	'66.87.73.27',	'2017-02-24 08:17:42',	'2017-02-24 16:17:42',	'Trying to hard Cover book and dvd\'s',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 5.1.1; SAMSUNG SM-J320P Build/LMY47X) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) SamsungBrowser/3.5 Chrome/38.0.2125.102 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(205334,	1831,	'Maddy',	'maddycascarini@gmail.com',	'',	'82.13.223.115',	'2017-02-25 01:52:51',	'2017-02-25 09:52:51',	'Help me! I have just started playing and my bottom lip hurts SO much , is there any other way of blowing that does not include biting my bottom lip? Also my saxophone keeps squeaking and I don\'t know why ! Please help!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 9_3_5 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/601.1.46 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.0 Mobile/13G36 Safari/601.1',	'',	0,	0),
(205484,	2809,	'J.J',	'Fhuu32gj@yahoo.com',	'',	'108.194.45.118',	'2017-03-01 20:24:49',	'2017-03-02 04:24:49',	'I\'ve been playing in a band for 15 years and recently decided to learn to play the alto sax (first wind instrument). I\'m surprised at how loud it is! Sometimes I practice in the back seat of my truck. I\'m seriously considering the esax mute because walking back and forth to my truck is getting old. If I can keep the noise down, I\'d be practicing several times a day  in small bursts.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; SAMSUNG-SM-J320A Build/MMB29K) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) SamsungBrowser/4.0 Chrome/44.0.2403.133 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(205626,	1797,	'olotu ifeoluwa enoch',	'olotuifeoluwa2016@gmail.com',	'',	'141.0.14.83',	'2017-03-06 14:52:17',	'2017-03-06 22:52:17',	'good',	0,	'1',	'Opera/9.80 (Android; Opera Mini/21.0.2254/58.167; U; en) Presto/2.12.423 Version/12.16',	'',	0,	0),
(205720,	1831,	'Richard',	'twocircles13@gmail.com',	'',	'75.143.89.108',	'2017-03-10 08:36:40',	'2017-03-10 16:36:40',	'Those unfamiliar with the teachings of Joe Allard might search the Internet, where there are notes from his students and a series of videos on YouTube available. While his quote to breathe is dead-on, he also had instructions and exercises to re-learn to breathe correctly and in a relaxing way, which most of us, after about the age of 6, have forgotten how to do.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_12_4) AppleWebKit/603.1.30 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.1 Safari/603.1.30',	'',	0,	0),
(205722,	1876,	'HARRY HOWELL',	'harjazz@manx.net',	'',	'87.254.80.44',	'2017-03-10 11:58:04',	'2017-03-10 19:58:04',	'If i am blessed, going to see and meet Dave and Richie Beirach in London Oct\'17.....speaking with both, incredible human beings who live like i do to hear Jazz.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/49.0.2623.112 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(205994,	538,	'Dan E. Doran',	'Hastingsdoran@att.net',	'',	'108.230.69.250',	'2017-03-20 10:31:08',	'2017-03-20 16:31:08',	'Wasn\'t Glen Frye\'s \' \"(Are You Gonna Stay with) The One You Love\" from the 80\'s?. Lot\'s of sax on that one.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/51.0.2704.79 Safari/537.36 Edge/14.14393',	'',	0,	0),
(206242,	1434,	'Tony',	'tonytat42@gmail.com',	'https://tonelovette.wordpress.com',	'98.124.91.241',	'2017-03-30 23:23:03',	'2017-03-31 06:23:03',	'That\'s simple advice. I was in the Navy for 20 year, playing with their various big bands, small jazz ensembles, rock bands and other crap. They just about beat music out of me, so much so, I didn\'t want to play anymore. The last time I played with the navy, or anywhere else was 2007. \r\n\r\nNow I\'ve just picked up a new horn and practicing again. While in the navy I never had to work very hard to get gigs outside my day job (which was music). Everyone knew who we were usually. I feel it will be a challenge now getting my name and face out there. But I\'m not ready yet anyway. Thanks for the guidance. I\'ve never had to work at it before. Should be interesting.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_10_5) AppleWebKit/603.1.30 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.1 Safari/603.1.30',	'',	0,	0),
(206560,	3190,	'Nae',	'nae.rose.kelly@gmail.com',	'',	'101.176.161.206',	'2017-04-11 17:28:29',	'2017-04-12 00:28:29',	'Yeah I\'ve only been playing for a short time but when I finish my breath and reed always smell really bad. I can\'t wash it because my saxophone teacher keeps getting up me when I take it out of the mouthpiece because \'every time you put it in you run the risk of splintering it\' (a different problem I used to have)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 10_2_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/602.4.6 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14D27 Safari/602.1',	'',	0,	0),
(206696,	337,	'SaxManTrevor',	'SaxManTrevor64@aol.com',	'https://MidnightIguana.com',	'97.81.83.121',	'2017-04-18 10:04:24',	'2017-04-18 17:04:24',	'Oh noooo never relaquer a sax especially a mark VI it drops the value way down \r\nMost professionals don\'t care about looks it\'s all about the sound and the relaquer can damage the sound',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 10_2_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/602.4.6 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14D27 Safari/602.1',	'',	8593,	0),
(206697,	337,	'SaxManTrevor',	'SaxManTrevor64@aol.com',	'https://MidnightIguana.com',	'97.81.83.121',	'2017-04-18 10:12:02',	'2017-04-18 17:12:02',	'There are great values in vintage saxes. And many can be had at teriffic  bargains. \r\nFor the price of a new pad job and set up you can have a pro sax for the cost of a modern student instrument . My recommendation is a CG Conn I\'ve played combs for years and live their warm full sound. Also the early Pan Americans are Made by Conn from left over CG Conn stock and can be had for next to nothing as they were marketed as student instruments but in reality were made from professional parts so they are amazing',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 10_2_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/602.4.6 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14D27 Safari/602.1',	'',	196900,	0),
(206722,	2161,	'Jeremy Holst',	'jeremyholst20@mittymonarch.com',	'',	'172.10.238.6',	'2017-04-19 03:22:18',	'2017-04-19 10:22:18',	'The tip of the reed is fragile! What you must do is put the opposite side in and avoid touching the thin side aka the tip! Also, curve your bottom lip around your teeth and have the mouthpiece about half an inch in your mouth. Never touch the tip and avoid hitting it on things, so put on the cap whenever you can.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 10_3_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/603.1.30 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14E304 Safari/602.1',	'',	187280,	0),
(206723,	2161,	'Jeremy Holst',	'jeremyholst20@mittymonarch.com',	'',	'172.10.238.6',	'2017-04-19 03:24:11',	'2017-04-19 10:24:11',	'What is the grain? I\'ve searched for reed anatomies on the internet and saw nothing called the grain. Also what exactly does 2.5 and etc. measure in the reed?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 10_3_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/603.1.30 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14E304 Safari/602.1',	'',	0,	0),
(206740,	3881,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.147.121',	'2017-04-19 19:29:58',	'2017-04-20 02:29:58',	'Bresdin: Bonjour come\' talle\' vous? Tres bien? Thank you for your comments. To everyone, I am retired from a Navy Band in the USA. I have played every chair in the section. My favorite chairs were bari (although it does get heavy), 2nd alto (lots of really good notes of the chord. Plenty of # 11ths\' b 9th\'setc, etc) and any tenor chair especially if I get to solo. Actually in a really good band all the saxes get to solo. I do like playing lead alto but I\'m very partial to Art Pepper\'s sound and he usually played 2nd alto and soloed w/Kenton and others. I really dig his combo stuff.\r\n\r\nBy and large I actually prefer to play small group stuff over big band stuff. I really like the freedom and the chance to expand my palette.  A 3 or 4 piece rhthym section and me on tenor is it. Some of my favorite sax players are Stan Getz, Zoot, Dexter, Lester, Bird, Art Pepper, Bill Perkins, Ben Webster, Scott Hamilton, Harry Allen, Dick Oatts among others.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:48.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/48.0',	'',	0,	0),
(206760,	4043,	'Joe Higham',	'joehigham@hotmail.com',	'',	'91.178.109.143',	'2017-04-21 03:12:31',	'2017-04-21 10:12:31',	'Just a quick update, the book is actually $13.99. Maybe it\'s got something to do with the $/€. Anyhow, thought it worth mentioning, and updating.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.8; rv:43.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/43.0 SeaMonkey/2.40',	'',	0,	0),
(206763,	4928,	'Joe Higham',	'joehigham@hotmail.com',	'',	'91.178.109.143',	'2017-04-21 04:51:19',	'2017-04-21 11:51:19',	'looks very interesting (the way you organise the ideas/scale). I\'m highly tempted to have a look at your book(s)! Thanks for the article.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.8; rv:43.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/43.0 SeaMonkey/2.40',	'',	0,	0),
(206767,	4043,	'Zach Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'107.201.109.91',	'2017-04-21 10:14:17',	'2017-04-21 17:14:17',	'Hello Joe,\r\n\r\nAppreciate the update. I updated the price point. I recall at the time it was $9.99 but believe the price went up. Regardless, it\'s worth the $13.99. Let me know if you have any questions.\r\n\r\nZach',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/57.0.2987.133 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	15),
(206860,	2933,	'Jaime Chavez',	'Bro99gh@gmail.com',	'',	'205.213.171.4',	'2017-04-24 11:49:35',	'2017-04-24 18:49:35',	'Dear Zach,\r\n\r\nWhat would you recommend for a Selmer Mrk Vi tenor? I recently got one but the case it came with is too big for it, and I\'ve already had to pay for repairs on it.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; CrOS x86_64 9202.64.0) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/57.0.2987.146 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(206861,	6145,	'Joseph C. Sitompul',	'abang.chris@gmail.com',	'',	'112.215.238.3',	'2017-07-25 18:03:20',	'2017-07-26 01:03:20',	'You gave me better and deeper understanding, not just about saxophone, but also about music.\r\nThanks a lot, randy!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 5.0.2; ASUS_Z00ED Build/LRX22G) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/59.0.3071.125 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(206862,	6145,	'Randy Hinter',	'Randy@randyhunterjazz.com',	'http://www.beginningsax.com',	'71.199.157.162',	'2017-07-26 18:48:39',	'2017-07-27 00:48:39',	'Thanks Joseph! That\'s such a great compliment. I\'m very honored! Randy',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 10_3_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/603.2.4 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0 Mobile/14F89 Safari/602.1',	'',	0,	0),
(206866,	6243,	'Jay Rodriguez',	'jayrodri@gmail.com',	'https://www.jayrodriguez.com',	'66.87.31.42',	'2017-10-23 07:46:15',	'2017-10-23 14:46:15',	'Excellent resource for all musicians . !',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 10_3_3 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/603.3.8 (KHTML, like Gecko) Mobile/14G60 [FBAN/FBIOS;FBAV/146.0.0.73.91;FBBV/75938921;FBDV/iPhone9,1;FBMD/iPhone;FBSN/iOS;FBSV/10.3.3;FBSS/2;FBCR/Sprint;FBID/phone;FBLC/en_US;FBOP/5;FBR',	'',	0,	0),
(206879,	6272,	'Larry Weintraub',	'lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.174.58',	'2017-11-27 08:36:04',	'2017-11-27 16:36:04',	'Under my bio it should say Keely Smith not Kelly Smith. She was married to Louie Prima. They did a Vegas act together before they divorced. She was also a friend of Frank Sinatra\'s and recorded a tribute CD to him a year or two after Frank passed.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:48.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/48.0',	'',	0,	0),
(206880,	6272,	'Larry Weintraub',	'lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.174.58',	'2017-11-28 15:39:07',	'2017-11-28 23:39:07',	'If you want to check me out go to your search bar and type in:\r\n\r\nLarry Weintraub with the TCC Faculty Jazz Combo\r\n\r\n     This was from a faculty recital at TCC in Norfolk, VA in March 2015. I played \"Don\'t Get Around....,\" \"Polka Dots &amp; Moon Beams,\" and \"Autumn Leaves.\"\r\n\r\nThe type in: Larry Weintraub playing Yesterdays          This was from April, 2013 when I was working on my Masters at ODU. The big band is the ODU Jazz Ensemble.\r\n\r\nI hope you enjoy the videos. If anyone needs a tenor player send me an e-mail at Lweintraub1@cox.net    the same if you want to talk about the Military Bands or anything else. Btw - I also play clarinet and alto sax.\r\n\r\nTake care,\r\n\r\nLarry W',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:48.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/48.0',	'',	0,	0),
(206881,	6278,	'eric king',	'ericmichelleking@yahoo.com',	'',	'172.56.6.224',	'2017-12-29 15:43:37',	'2017-12-29 23:43:37',	'love it',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 7.0; SM-G950U Build/NRD90M; wv) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4.0 Chrome/63.0.3239.111 Mobile Safari/537.36 [FB_IAB/FB4A;FBAV/153.0.0.54.88;]',	'',	0,	0),
(206885,	6305,	'Mark Brown',	'msaxbrown@earthlink.net',	'',	'71.175.226.217',	'2018-01-01 07:22:08',	'2018-01-01 13:22:08',	'Hi Larry, Thank you for sharing your recollections of a day with Michael  and your own history and  sax wisdom.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 11_2_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/604.4.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/11.0 Mobile/15C153 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(206886,	6305,	'Aga Smies',	'aesmies@yahoo.ca',	'',	'156.57.212.71',	'2018-01-01 09:07:58',	'2018-01-01 17:07:58',	'That is a very enjoyable and inspirational article all band players should read. The comments about listening and being prepared hit close to home.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/63.0.3239.84 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(206887,	6305,	'Donna Schwartz',	'donna@donnaschwartzmusic.com',	'https://DonnaSchwartzMusic.com',	'47.51.53.74',	'2018-01-01 09:53:23',	'2018-01-01 17:53:23',	'Nice article, Larry! Thanks for sharing your experience with everyone.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_9_5) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/63.0.3239.84 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(206888,	6305,	'Steve S.',	'SSub50@aol.com',	'',	'206.53.87.60',	'2018-01-01 11:16:07',	'2018-01-01 19:16:07',	'Thanks so very much for taking the time to relate this great bit of military music history AND a bit of Michael Brecker history as well !!\r\nIt is also nice to have your personal Bio included as I am always interested in how people come to their music lives ..... and how they handle the reality of the economics involved....... Best wishes for a great year to you and yours !',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_2) AppleWebKit/604.4.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/11.0.2 Safari/604.4.7',	'',	0,	0),
(206889,	6305,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'71.121.229.136',	'2018-01-01 11:21:40',	'2018-01-01 19:21:40',	'Mark: Hi, I\'m glad you liked the article. Michael was very humble and inspiring. My own music history is not typical in that I did not learn how to play in the public schools. I took private lessons from a local Union Pro. \r\nWhen Sinatra came to town he was in the band, the same when Ella, Tony Bennett or others came my teacher Al Sigismondi was always in the band.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	206885,	0),
(206890,	6305,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'71.121.229.136',	'2018-01-01 11:23:39',	'2018-01-01 19:23:39',	'Aga: Thank you I really appreciate your comments. I agree, listening to the music and being prepared are very important.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	206886,	0),
(206891,	6305,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'71.121.229.136',	'2018-01-01 11:25:12',	'2018-01-01 19:25:12',	'Donna: Thank you very much. I\'m glad you enjoyed the article.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	206887,	0),
(206892,	6305,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'71.121.229.136',	'2018-01-01 11:28:12',	'2018-01-01 19:28:12',	'Steve: Thank you. Michael Brecker\'s history and his path was very interesting. As I mentioned before  was really inspired by him and how humble he was. I hope you have a Happy New Year as well.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	0,	0),
(206893,	6305,	'Mark Rybiski',	'mrybiski@gmail.com',	'',	'107.221.20.166',	'2018-01-01 12:51:58',	'2018-01-01 20:51:58',	'Thanks for sharing Larry.    Astonished at your personal bio/journey too...wow.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64; rv:57.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/57.0',	'',	0,	0),
(206894,	6305,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'71.121.229.136',	'2018-01-01 21:07:03',	'2018-01-02 05:07:03',	'Mark: Thanks for liking my article. Me, I\'m no one special, not like Michael that is for sure. Don\'t get me wrong I enjoyed many aspects of being a military musician, especially the travel. I met some very interesting and nice people. However none of us in military music are of the caliber of player that Michael was. If we were we wouldn\'t be in a military band. We\'d be in NYC or L.A. setting the world on fire.\r\n\r\nMe I\'m a local player now plus I teach as mentioned in my bio. There are a few guys from the Navy Jazz Commodores and the Army Jazz Ambassadors who are really, really great players. Check out Jim Hayward on tenor sax, Luis Hernandez also on tenor. Then there is Marty Nau on alto and Scott Silbert on tenor. From the Army check out Tom Williams on trpt. All of these guys except Luis are out of the service. They are all in the Greater Wash DC area except Jim who is in Michigan.\r\n\r\nWell thanks again and have a Happy New Year Mark.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	206893,	0),
(206895,	6305,	'Joe Sullivan',	'Sullivan_1@comcast.net',	'',	'50.234.133.198',	'2018-01-02 08:00:50',	'2018-01-02 16:00:50',	'Larry,\r\nThanks very much for sharing. It was great to hear your story. Have a great year.\r\nJoe Sullivan',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 8_4 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/600.1.4 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/8.0 Mobile/12H143 Safari/600.1.4',	'',	0,	0),
(206896,	6305,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'71.121.229.136',	'2018-01-02 10:34:12',	'2018-01-02 18:34:12',	'Joe: Thank you. You have a Great Year as well. Are you the same Joe Sullivan I knew in the Baltimore area back in the 70\'s - 80\'s? If so you played alto?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	206895,	0),
(206897,	6305,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'71.121.229.136',	'2018-01-02 11:24:35',	'2018-01-02 19:24:35',	'One thing that Michael did say about Improv that I left out by accident. He said \"that it may take 6 months to year for a pattern or idea that he is practicing to show up in performance.\" So do not feel bad folks if you think that you are moving to slowly. It takes time to really internalize musical ideas through the keys and have them come out in your solos, especially the harder stuff.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	0,	0),
(206898,	6305,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'71.121.229.136',	'2018-01-02 19:52:49',	'2018-01-03 01:52:49',	'Typo corrections:\r\n\r\nLast paragraph under Michaels \"Final Words To US.\"  Yes I did play the A section of \"Body and Soul\" for him. The correction is he stopped me before the 1st bridge which is in E Major on the tenor not E minor. Also my tenor sax mpc is a metal Otto Link 8* (star) not a plain 8. \r\n\r\nI\'ve got to get better at proof reading. Oh well just 2 slight errors in 3,142 words.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	0,	0),
(206901,	5452,	'Jacobs Jean-Marie',	'jeanmarie.jacobs@vdab.be',	'',	'84.192.11.133',	'2018-01-03 17:10:10',	'2018-01-03 23:10:10',	'Well, I first tried using a small screwdriver as \'my device\' and  recorded all my saxes with and without screwdriver . The difference was obvious on both 5alto s and 3tenors, be it more on the alto\'s. I found myself practising and recording with this screwdriver  in front of me all the time...Looks so  silly. So I ordered this device knowing it has to work. It looks like a natural part of my saxophone now. Surprisingly It \'s actually a little less efficient than the screwdriver. Still...You clearly hear  more evenness of tone,somewhat warmer and fuller highs,rounder lows. My expensive Keilwerth sounds even more expensive now. That and the sax reflector are really usefull devices. Glad I bought both of them . Jm\r\n\r\n,',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 7.0; HUAWEI VNS-L31 Build/HUAWEIVNS-L31) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/63.0.3239.111 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(206908,	6305,	'Nicolas Buff',	'Nicolas.buff@yahoo.com',	'https://Facebook.com',	'101.173.64.17',	'2018-01-04 15:41:04',	'2018-01-04 21:41:04',	'Thanks for sharing this amazing experience with your and Michael B’s insights. Particularly the points about service musician culture which I can relate to my own army music experience here in Australia. Best wishes!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 11_2_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/604.4.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/11.0 Mobile/15C153 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(206909,	6305,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'71.121.229.136',	'2018-01-04 19:32:34',	'2018-01-05 01:32:34',	'Nicolas You\'re an Aussie eh. Your welcome for the article, I\'m glad you liked it. I guess military bands and music are the same all over mate. When I 1st joined the USN there were some Aussie guys going through the School of Music at Little Creek, VA in Va Bch. They were nice guys. \r\n\r\nAre you still; in an Aussie Army Band? Are you doing the full career? How is promotion for you guys? For us it wasn\'t that good at all. \r\n\r\nNow I know that you don\'t have a pet kangaroo but if you happen to see one in the Outback give it a pat for me. I like kangaroo\'s or as you lads say the bloody Roo\'s.\r\n\r\nPlease check out my other article about Touring Overseas and some SHORT Navy Band Stories. Do you guys do any touring overseas at all? Does your band play in any military Tattoos? I\'ve been in 14 bloody Tattoos and as far as I\'m concerned that is 13 to many. We did do the Big International Tattoo in Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada. The Tattoo was way to long and overblown. However I did meet some very nice people from Canada and Estonia. Well ya got to take the good w/the bad. Best Wishes to you and have a Happy New Year Down Under Mate. I assume you play saxophone too.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	206908,	0),
(206910,	3161,	'Douglass Jones',	'douglass.jones31@gmail.com',	'https://www.facebook.com',	'58.111.106.86',	'2018-01-04 20:25:18',	'2018-01-05 02:25:18',	'I leaned a great leason years ago. Diversity is the key ! Call it what you like but I call it improvisation !',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/63.0.3239.84 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(206912,	6323,	'Kathy Marshall',	'Kaco61@att.net',	'',	'12.105.36.114',	'2018-01-08 09:53:05',	'2018-01-08 15:53:05',	'I signed up previously but I don\'t think I ever received the FREE sax tips booklet + 3-part audio master class series with Bob Sheppard, Tim Price &amp; Ricky Sweum.  Can I still receive this?  Thank you.   Kathy Marshall',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/63.0.3239.84 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
