(207669,	6521,	'Larry Weintraub',	'lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.174.58',	'2018-04-07 15:25:02',	'2018-04-07 21:25:02',	'Find a good teacher either at a local college or music store and practice, practice, practice.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.6; rv:48.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/48.0',	'',	207659,	0),
(207674,	5824,	'Ron Adkins',	'ronadkins7@gmail.com',	'',	'172.58.137.53',	'2018-04-08 09:05:07',	'2018-04-08 15:05:07',	'Hey Bruce I first heard you playing with Roy Hargrove \"mister magic\", I\'m instantly a fan !! You are so AWESOME !! I\'M an athlete but I love JAZZ !! I wish you continued success !!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 7.0; LG-TP450 Build/NRD90U) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/58.0.3029.83 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(208237,	1937,	'dahszil dahszil',	'dahszil@gmail.com',	'',	'24.165.131.216',	'2018-04-28 22:16:53',	'2018-04-29 04:16:53',	'Over the decades I have really been getting tired of the raspy growl sax technique .  I have rediscovered Stan Getz , Charlie Parker(who could play every type of technique . a genius of music and composition in general) and a few others from the past and I am happy .  However I can understand younger people digging the raspy growl sax .  I know i was when as a young teen hearing Junior Walker, et al .',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/65.0.3325.181 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(208385,	6521,	'Dino Saliba',	'Rasaliba55@gmail.com',	'',	'23.119.232.103',	'2018-05-02 13:17:28',	'2018-05-02 19:17:28',	'Good information in both articles Larry.  It will be very useful to those seeking performance opportunities.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 7.0; XT1585 Build/NCK25.118-10.5; wv) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4.0 Chrome/66.0.3359.126 Mobile Safari/537.36 [FB_IAB/Orca-Android;FBAV/164.0.0.24.95;]',	'',	0,	0),
(208389,	6521,	'Larry W',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.151.43',	'2018-05-02 14:33:49',	'2018-05-02 20:33:49',	'Dino: Thanks, that is why I wrote it. Fyi - Dino is another sax player I know from the Navy Band in Orlando, FL.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_10_5) AppleWebKit/602.3.12 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.0.2 Safari/602.3.12',	'',	208385,	0),
(208461,	1937,	'paul roberts',	'paulsroberts2005@yahoo.com',	'http://yahoo.com',	'67.143.208.170',	'2018-05-04 09:48:53',	'2018-05-04 15:48:53',	'I would like to learn how to growl on my alto sax and what technique it will take to make happen for me.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/66.0.3359.139 Safari/537.36',	'',	208237,	0),
(208549,	6010,	'Julie A Baca',	'julieannbaca@gmail.com',	'',	'201.207.190.134',	'2018-05-06 11:43:51',	'2018-05-06 17:43:51',	'I have a 64 Buffet SDA, I am looking for a mouthpiece to use on this sax. I like the review of the Soltice, and I am drawn to the west coast sound. But... I also like playing Bossa Nova, and soulful ballads. So, am tending to go for the custom Meyer. \r\nWhat\'s your take on which mouthpiece would be the best fit for my vintage sax?\r\nHope to get a reply, so thank you in advance.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; SM-T710 Build/MMB29K) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/66.0.3359.126 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(208550,	6010,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'107.201.109.91',	'2018-05-06 12:02:52',	'2018-05-06 18:02:52',	'Hello Julie,\r\n\r\nYou need to try both to figure out which one will work best for you. I personally prefer the Custom Meyer over the Solstice but they both play well and you could achieve the same result. I\'d recommend reaching out to Phil and I know he is happy to help.\r\n\r\nBest,\r\n\r\nZach',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/66.0.3359.139 Safari/537.36',	'',	208549,	0),
(208636,	5534,	'larry rauson',	'larryrauson@gmail.com',	'',	'173.70.255.239',	'2018-05-07 22:46:06',	'2018-05-08 04:46:06',	'I use V21 3.0 occasionally on Theo Wanne Westcoast Mofo 110. Its a metal high baffled tenor piece. I enjoy the darker, powerful tone as opposed to the brightness of Java Green. Very excellent reed.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; LG-K550 Build/MXB48T) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/62.0.3202.84 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(208801,	5485,	'Jonix',	'jonboutellier@yahoo.fr',	'',	'77.136.16.33',	'2018-05-11 08:48:36',	'2018-05-11 14:48:36',	'Thanks for this article.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_2) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/66.0.3359.139 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(208811,	4921,	'Kenny',	'kennyfernandes2000@yahoo.com',	'',	'72.238.158.31',	'2018-05-11 14:03:40',	'2018-05-11 20:03:40',	'Another great ballad for the Saxophone  is \"The End of a Love Affair\" by the Stan Kenton Orchestra.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; ZTE-Z956 Build/MMB29M; wv) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4.0 Chrome/45.0.2454.95 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(208886,	2161,	'Jason G.',	'jgreensax@gmail.com',	'',	'107.77.209.137',	'2018-05-12 21:50:39',	'2018-05-13 03:50:39',	'No serious players buy one reed at a time.  You can’t compare them this way because the other 9 Vandorens in the box could have been amazing and you could have gotten lucky by choosing one of the good Rico’s.  Do yourself a favor:  buy AT LEAST a box at a time and compare them. You’ll find a box of any brand probably has a few great ones, a lot of good ones (if you have the right strength for your mouthpiece) and a few that barely play until you adjust them. You can save a lot of money learning how to adjust reeds. They are usually not “ready to go” right out of the box. Tom Ridenour has some good videos on adjusting reeds. There is also no way a single reed would work well for 14 months unless you hardly ever play. Good luck.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 11_2_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/604.4.7 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/11.0 Mobile/15C153 Safari/604.1',	'',	199697,	0),
(208977,	6608,	'Napo Camassa',	'napocamassa@yahoo.co.uk',	'',	'2.96.45.3',	'2018-05-15 04:03:54',	'2018-05-15 10:03:54',	'Dear David,Thanks for having me.Just a short message...Can you give the best tips andmakes, about attached mikes to the bell,reeds ,metal/rubber/ebony mouthpieces,effects,stands and stuff,for my soprano sax ? Many Thanks Napo Camassa/Zenlo from London UK',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_9_5) AppleWebKit/601.7.8 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/9.1.3 Safari/537.86.7',	'',	0,	0),
(208997,	6608,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'70.113.101.140',	'2018-05-15 12:04:26',	'2018-05-15 18:04:26',	'Hello there Napo, Doron, the interviewer here. I am not sure that Dave is monitoring the comments here, but I just added your question to the list for the next interview. Thanks for listening!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/66.0.3359.139 Safari/537.36',	'',	208977,	1),
(209637,	3974,	'Bill Easley',	'WilliamEasley@aol.com',	'http://BillEasley.Net',	'98.26.53.150',	'2018-05-25 17:52:11',	'2018-05-25 23:52:11',	'I keep a few ready to play reads in the Ziploc bag with a damp sponge . Use a file to fine tune the rough spots on front and back.  This week I am trying something sugested by Mark Vinci.   He stores rieeds soaking in white vinegar in the refrigerator.  I am only trying it because I think he’s brilliant .   This Reed stuff is kind a new to me since I’ve only been playing for 60 some  Years.  Proud and happy to be a Vandoren endorcer.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 11_3 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/11.0 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(209678,	3974,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'70.113.101.140',	'2018-05-26 16:15:52',	'2018-05-26 22:15:52',	'Hello Bill, an honor to have you commenting here! Interesting method - hopefully the reeds don\'t smell too bad after soaking in that stuff, but I\'d be curious to give it a try. Thanks for sharing that!\r\n\r\nPS. Although I have not been bestowed the title of \"endorser\", I\'ve used Vandoren\'s myself nearly my entire playing career, they\'re among the least-bad reeds I\'ve ever played. :)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/66.0.3359.181 Safari/537.36',	'',	209637,	1),
(209867,	4224,	'Alexander',	'fakemail@bell.net',	'',	'142.112.136.124',	'2018-05-30 14:51:41',	'2018-05-30 20:51:41',	'Reichert Studies are really good. (Flutist here and I heard the saxophone has the same fingering for almost all notes.) The most  challenging for me is the Gb major in study no2. (Shows on the picture but with six flats...) Finally, I got over it making no mistakes (takes time LOL) and now I am just increasing the speed slowly and gradually.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/49.0.2623.112 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(209868,	4224,	'Alexander',	'fakemail@bell.net',	'',	'142.112.136.124',	'2018-05-30 15:03:32',	'2018-05-30 21:03:32',	'Oh yeah, and one more thing. Reichert studies are written for more intermediate and advanced players. I remember, as an intermediate player I had so much trouble already in study no1 already in Bb major and below. LOL. But slowly and gradually the study are helping acquiring the technique and to be friends with all the keys in major (+) and minor (-) scales and arpeggios and its different variations.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 5.1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/49.0.2623.112 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(210245,	5640,	'Nathan Peabody',	'nathan.j.peabody@gmail.com',	'',	'166.182.81.183',	'2018-06-08 10:25:51',	'2018-06-08 16:25:51',	'Steve - the “2” incorporates some small updates added by Theo as a result of customer feedback.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 11_4 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/11.0 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(210265,	6682,	'Ted Reynolds',	'Danetre.Ted@gmail.com',	'',	'172.88.42.236',	'2018-06-08 17:19:34',	'2018-06-08 23:19:34',	'Incredible in its simplicity, sitting on my porch just singing through the rhythms, just bought the book.\r\nTHANK YOU#',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 7.0; VS987 Build/NRD90U) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/66.0.3359.158 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(210271,	6682,	'DN Rhythm',	'studiod179@att.net',	'http://DNrhythm.com',	'99.16.143.136',	'2018-06-08 21:26:33',	'2018-06-09 03:26:33',	'I\'m always glad to share with the music community. I always suggest using the Bebopish words, licks and phrases  in the book before, in the middle and at the end of other things you like to play, adding to your vocabulary. The book helps to \"Sing Da Bebop\" in a fun and easy way. Have fun! \r\n \"Easy Easy Bebop\"',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64; rv:60.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/60.0',	'',	0,	0),
(210339,	1937,	'Deb Morcom',	'Saxielady@gmail.com',	'',	'58.172.148.150',	'2018-06-11 08:55:07',	'2018-06-11 14:55:07',	'Hi\r\nI\'m in the middle of rehearsaling a solo piece with concert band Saxophobia based on Rudy Weidorf 1920s piece.  I have a low G to flutter tongue on.  I have just read your info on flutter tonguing and will give it a go asap.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; SM-G900I Build/MMB29M) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/67.0.3396.81 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(210340,	1937,	'Deb Morcom',	'Saxielady@gmail.com',	'',	'58.172.148.150',	'2018-06-11 09:02:13',	'2018-06-11 15:02:13',	'Growling I find easy to do. \r\nRelax your throat and use the back of the throat to make a grrr sound adjust your embouchure slightly let the air through normally you should be able to produce the growl sound.  High G helps it come out better.  Beginners do it well too. \r\nThere is a great book and CD out by Hal Leonard to learn all these special effects.  Can\'t think of its name.  Blue cover.  I\'m sure there are some youtube clips out too.  Good luck.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; SM-G900I Build/MMB29M) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/67.0.3396.81 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	208461,	0),
(210346,	1937,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'70.113.101.140',	'2018-06-11 12:13:00',	'2018-06-11 18:13:00',	'Awesome, feel free to leave another comment with an update on how the flutter tonguing goes at the concert!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/66.0.3359.181 Safari/537.36',	'',	210339,	1),
(210428,	4648,	'Woodrow Carter',	'woodrowcarter4@gmail.com',	'',	'173.53.67.203',	'2018-06-13 12:15:23',	'2018-06-13 18:15:23',	'Wow can l get the corse and how much does it cost?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 11_3 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/604.1.34 (KHTML, like Gecko) GSA/51.0.198805899 Mobile/15E216 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(210429,	4648,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'70.113.101.140',	'2018-06-13 12:28:01',	'2018-06-13 18:28:01',	'Hello Woodrow, sorry if the link in the article wasn\'t very obvious, but you can find it at https://www.jazzlessonswithgiants.com and it\'s $49 for the complete package, but there are cheaper packages if you just want the audio or the ebook by themselves. \r\n\r\nPlease reach out at https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local/contact if you have any other questions, Thanks!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_4) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/66.0.3359.181 Safari/537.36',	'',	210428,	1),
(210652,	5461,	'Lanny Aplanalp',	'lannya@earthlink.net',	'',	'71.93.221.113',	'2018-06-20 12:29:56',	'2018-06-20 18:29:56',	'I was on an important gig yesterday when a reed suddenly went dead. Fortunately I had a reed in my reedjuvinate to use immediately. Thanks!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 11_4 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/604.1.34 (KHTML, like Gecko) GSA/51.0.198805899 Mobile/15F79 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(210710,	4799,	'Smitty',	'Greatsax4u@gmail.com',	'',	'69.136.25.68',	'2018-06-22 08:33:50',	'2018-06-22 14:33:50',	'I was told by my fellow musician\'s that play guitar that the song they were playing was in A minor. So I play a Alto Sax and I was trying to find that transposed Key that I would explain what key I needed to be in. I got  lost!!! lol  Any suggestions??  Shoot me an email if you have the answer..I could use it. :)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/67.0.3396.87 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(210711,	4799,	'Joe Q.',	'jwosnick@gmail.com',	'',	'199.212.27.189',	'2018-06-22 08:42:29',	'2018-06-22 14:42:29',	'For key transposition, you go down by a minor third (three semitones). Concert A minor becomes played F# minor on the alto.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/67.0.3396.87 Safari/537.36',	'',	210710,	0),
(211157,	5824,	'Bruce Williams',	'Brucewilliamsjazz@gmail.com',	'',	'173.70.194.180',	'2018-07-07 20:56:48',	'2018-07-08 02:56:48',	'Thank you Ron! BW',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 11_4 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/11.0 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(211348,	3827,	'Profleighton',	'ivy@inch.com',	'',	'174.220.23.224',	'2018-07-15 20:12:19',	'2018-07-16 02:12:19',	'4 Words\r\n\r\nThe Boston Sax Shop\r\nReally....you gotta check it out if you ever go to Boston!\r\n\r\nhttps://www.bostonsaxshop.com/staps/',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; CrOS x86_64 10575.58.0) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/67.0.3396.99 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(211473,	5824,	'Tim',	'ttthatcher@msn.com',	'',	'68.62.53.209',	'2018-07-20 15:49:09',	'2018-07-20 21:49:09',	'Very kind of your to share your skills...thanks Bruce and every good wish.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_4) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/11.1 Safari/605.1.15',	'',	211157,	0),
(211499,	1254,	'Sher',	'sherkeel@yahoo.com',	'',	'206.169.44.206',	'2018-07-22 10:16:19',	'2018-07-22 16:16:19',	'Saxophone lung is real...caused from mold. It can cause Broncithitis, asthma symptoms...clean your instrument daily, brush your teeth before use...see a doctor for persistent lung problems with playing instrument.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	0,	0),
(211635,	6754,	'Sebastian',	'Sebas.gomezd@gmail.com',	'',	'190.177.45.12',	'2018-07-28 07:49:40',	'2018-07-28 13:49:40',	'Hi, \r\nI would like obtain your product.\r\nDo you send to argentina country?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 11_4_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Mobile/15G77 Instagram 55.0.0.8.78 (iPhone8,4; iOS 11_4_1; es_AR; es-AR; scale=2.00; gamut=normal; 640x1136)',	'',	0,	0),
(211680,	2876,	'Catherine Shirey',	'csshirey@yahoo.com',	'',	'174.194.23.2',	'2018-07-30 09:23:23',	'2018-07-30 15:23:23',	'I have a conn 12m and it will not play middle b any recomdations.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 7.0; VS835 Build/NRD90U) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/66.0.3359.126 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(211746,	6810,	'Don Wilburn',	'dwilbu02@aol.com',	'',	'99.62.146.4',	'2018-08-02 15:38:13',	'2018-08-02 21:38:13',	'Great tuff.  As a beginner, this provides some basic simple exercises that will help ear training.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_10_5) AppleWebKit/603.3.8 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/10.1.2 Safari/603.3.8',	'',	0,	0),
