(213780,	6939,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweinraub1@cox.net',	'',	'68.107.158.241',	'2018-10-25 13:36:01',	'2018-10-25 19:36:01',	'Thank you Paul. Hope everyone is well.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.10; rv:60.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/60.0',	'',	213777,	0),
(213781,	6833,	'Mark Morley-Fletcher',	'mark@playinthezone.com',	'https://playinthezone.com/',	'80.189.112.50',	'2018-10-25 14:56:50',	'2018-10-25 20:56:50',	'Glad you liked it, Gene. Yes, it\'s amazing what you can learn from playing live that just doesn\'t come up in the practice room. And great attitude about consistently getting a little bit out of your comfort zone - that\'s how you grow!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64; rv:63.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/63.0',	'',	213755,	0),
(213905,	4071,	'Younggee',	'ygnho1789@naver.com',	'',	'203.244.212.28',	'2018-11-01 00:10:28',	'2018-11-01 06:10:28',	'younmentioned \"https://Lebaylemouthpieces.com/lrlrii.cfm\" is not open.\r\nI order a soprano metal mouthpiece 1 year ago. but still it is not arrived. If Mr. Fred Lebayle is not crazy or an impostor, It must be arrived at my home. I paid the money but mouthpiece is not arrived. What shall I do?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	0,	0),
(213906,	4071,	'Zach Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'107.201.109.91',	'2018-11-01 01:20:20',	'2018-11-01 07:20:20',	'Hey Younggee,\r\n\r\nI am sorry to hear that. I have heard a lot has changed with Fred over the past few years. I have not spoken with him in quite some time. Hoping you paid via credit card because you should be able to dispute the charge since you never received the product.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/69.0.3497.100 Safari/537.36',	'',	213905,	15),
(213995,	6945,	'Damien Mc Donnell',	'damodrummer@gmail.com',	'http://Com.',	'80.233.43.123',	'2018-11-05 15:42:31',	'2018-11-05 21:42:31',	'Are there any reviews of the Otto Link Rocky Giglio tenor mouthpiece?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 7.0; SM-G925F Build/NRD90M; wv) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4.0 Chrome/70.0.3538.80 Mobile Safari/537.36 [FB_IAB/FB4A;FBAV/196.0.0.41.95;]',	'',	0,	0),
(214009,	605,	'A. Robinson',	'N_INHURSAG@yahoo.com',	'http://yahoo.com',	'65.88.88.153',	'2018-11-06 12:45:58',	'2018-11-06 18:45:58',	'How did \"john Coltrane\" practice when he first started playing an instrument.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/63.0.3239.132 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(214016,	6945,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'157.130.212.6',	'2018-11-06 18:31:24',	'2018-11-07 00:31:24',	'Hey Damien,\r\n\r\nI found some further information on the RG Otto Link mouthpiece on Theo Wanne\'s website. In addition from what I have read about these mouthpieces, they are much closer to a Berg Larsen than a traditional Otto Link mouthpiece. I do not know many people who play them but their are a few YouTube video\'s with various people play testing them.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_6) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/70.0.3538.77 Safari/537.36',	'',	213995,	0),
(214123,	4921,	'sharon spring',	'eosdaystar@aol.com',	'',	'104.180.27.53',	'2018-11-11 13:17:02',	'2018-11-11 19:17:02',	'Please correct your article. Ram Rameriz   wrote Lover Man NOT George Gershwin',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	0,	0),
(214145,	5793,	'Justin',	'Jdickson19@live.com',	'',	'192.52.109.161',	'2018-11-12 07:47:10',	'2018-11-12 13:47:10',	'Zach,\r\n\r\nThanks for the review. Were you able to try out an A7S+ by chance? If so, how did you feel it stacks up to the A7 you currently have?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 12_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/12.0 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(214196,	270,	'Ronny Lang',	'ronbarbel@aol.com',	'',	'68.123.155.225',	'2018-11-13 12:23:30',	'2018-11-13 18:23:30',	'Never live. always with John Barry in a recording studio. he watched the picture and fitted the music to screen soundtrack...',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/70.0.3538.102 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(214198,	270,	'Ronny lang',	'ronbarbel@aol.com',	'',	'68.123.155.225',	'2018-11-13 12:42:15',	'2018-11-13 18:42:15',	'as far as doubling is concerned , as a studio session player it was required. Some times with only a few woodwind on a session, i would be playing  3 4 or 5 combinations. maybe  Alto sax, flute, clar .and piccolo. At one time i owned about 15 different instruments. mostly smaller orks. on T V shows. The large groups for John Williams used 10 or 12 woods . Not many doublers ...',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/70.0.3538.102 Safari/537.36',	'',	214196,	0),
(214282,	5469,	'Terry Schmidt',	'Terryls714@gmail.com',	'',	'173.16.78.137',	'2018-11-17 18:20:34',	'2018-11-18 00:20:34',	'Ordered a box. All 5 had tips that resembled a spoon. They were cupped. All 5. That in itself made them unplayable but in addition to that, the brand ‘stamp’ that was embedded in the table of each reed had so much residual material sticking up from the edges that it was impossible for any of the reeds to made a solid, flat contact surface to the mouthpiece. After confirming that these were unplayable, I stopped after 2. Now, I eventually got one of them to make a vibration by blowing as hard as possible but it wasn’t a tone, just a noise.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 12_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/604.1.34 (KHTML, like Gecko) GSA/62.1.220348572 Mobile/16B92 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(214285,	5469,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'113.37.160.250',	'2018-11-17 19:18:30',	'2018-11-18 01:18:30',	'Hello Terry,\r\n\r\nI would reach out to Bravo Reeds if you believe there was a defect with the product and I know they would be happy to further assist. I have not run into the issue you are describing so unfortunately I am not able to assist further.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_6) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/70.0.3538.77 Safari/537.36',	'',	214282,	0),
(214321,	5469,	'Terry Schmidt',	'terryls714@gmail.com',	'',	'173.16.78.137',	'2018-11-19 11:28:59',	'2018-11-19 17:28:59',	'Hello Zach, \r\nThank you for your info. I just returned them. Not a big deal. I had a very similar issue when I ordered a Forestone reed. Seems everything was in common: black material, spooned tip. I\'ve used synths for years. 2 brands that seem to be consistent and full bodied. Fibereed and Fibracell. The Fibracell has more cane characteristics; harmonics, buzz, low to high range. The Fibereed is SUPER easy to play but gets a little unpredictable when you start getting in to the harmonic range. There is also a noticeable difference in the models. Hemp is a little brighter than the regular material. I hope this info helps someone. My setup on Tenor is a MK VI using a Bill Evans 1AO and still experimenting with ligatures. regular Selmer metal and a Silverstein.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/70.0.3538.102 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(214330,	5469,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'113.37.160.250',	'2018-11-19 17:32:32',	'2018-11-19 23:32:32',	'Hello Terry,\r\n\r\nI have a few Forestone reeds and have not run into that issue. I know Forestone is happy to assist if you believe their is an issue with a reed. For a ligature, I would also try the ishimori metal ligature as well as Marc Jean Ligature if you are not satisfied with the Selmer metal or Silverstein ligature.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_6) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/70.0.3538.77 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(214347,	1254,	'Jane Doe',	'user@email.com',	'',	'68.53.217.249',	'2018-11-20 07:40:33',	'2018-11-20 13:40:33',	'Clean your mouthpiece out after you play. Make sure to take the reed off and put it away every time you put your sax away and to alternate and change reeds every so often.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; CrOS x86_64 10718.88.2) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/68.0.3440.118 Safari/537.36',	'',	152256,	0),
(214354,	5469,	'Charley W',	'chas5131@gmail.com',	'',	'104.156.210.130',	'2018-11-20 12:36:28',	'2018-11-20 18:36:28',	'I agree.\r\nPlastics have BPA among other things I don\'t want in my body.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/70.0.3538.102 Safari/537.36',	'',	191022,	0),
(214792,	2933,	'Wendy Scher',	'baridrummer@gmail.com',	'',	'71.105.62.244',	'2018-12-06 19:23:57',	'2018-12-07 01:23:57',	'So am I correct in that there is no heavy duty flight case available for a vintage Bb bari?  I requested a quote from Manning, though I imagine it will be far out of my league.  The 32 pounds of the horn in my Pro Tec is pretty damn painful on the back (really, a wood frame in 2018?), and isn\'t protective enough for, say, plane travel.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 8.1.0; BBB100-1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/70.0.3538.80 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(215050,	2161,	'Argendonax',	'marketing.argendonax@gmail.com',	'https://www.argendonax.com',	'122.173.94.202',	'2018-12-20 18:37:42',	'2018-12-21 00:37:42',	'Its an insightful article for both beginners and experts. Reeds and the instrument are highly dependent on each. To generate a good tone that meet the orchestral standards, one should be very cautious about the quality of the reeds and his instrument. French Cut Reeds (https://www.argendonax.com/product/oboe-pro-reeds) are the most popular reeds and therefore, french artists have gained a very high reputation and popularity. The top quality reeds will have a hard sound but they are best for the orchestral setting.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/69.0.3497.100 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
