(217546,	7061,	'Olujimi Tafataona',	'olujimitafataona@yahoo.com',	'http://www.inthetraditionjazz.net',	'64.94.35.33',	'2019-03-21 20:39:43',	'2019-03-22 02:39:43',	'I wholeheartedly agree with everything in this article.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 7.1.1; Z982 Build/NMF26V; wv) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4.0 Chrome/73.0.3683.75 Mobile Safari/537.36 [FB_IAB/FB4A;FBAV/212.0.0.28.110;]',	'',	0,	0),
(217622,	7047,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'http://www.bandmix.com/larry1261702',	'68.107.158.241',	'2019-03-25 21:33:56',	'2019-03-26 03:33:56',	'Doron: Nice interview w/Susan Brecker. Michael was a true inspiration to me when he came to the Atlantic Fleet Band in Sept. 2003. He was very humble but he laid everything on the line when he listened to our groups. \r\n\r\nWell you ca go bac to read my article on this site f you have questions. Please direct Susan Brecker to my article. i hope she will like it.\r\n\r\nTake care ,\r\n\r\nLarry W',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10.10; rv:60.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/60.0',	'',	0,	0),
(217942,	2576,	'Martin',	'Mrtnferris@gmail.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local/is-it-worth-buying-a-pro-model-saxophone-part-i/',	'68.61.17.158',	'2019-04-01 17:54:45',	'2019-04-01 23:54:45',	'I have an H. Couf Professional Alto Sax, by Julius Kielworth, that I bought from a friend for $500 in  the late 1980’s .  It was previously owned by my Sax teacher.  I also still have my student model Yamaha YAS-23 Alto Sax from 1980.  I have to say that the Yamaha is an excellent sad after all these years of playing it.  It’s easier to play and had a more comfortable thumb rest.  And the original mouthpiece that came with it still produces a sound equal to my newer Yamaha 4C mouthpiece.   Anyone looking for a good student model should check out the Yamaha YAS-23  Alto...',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 12_1_4 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) FxiOS/15.1b14275 Mobile/16D57 Safari/605.1.15',	'',	0,	0),
(217967,	6243,	'Eddy Bourjolly',	'Ebourjolly@aol.com',	'',	'108.46.148.64',	'2019-04-02 10:45:06',	'2019-04-02 16:45:06',	'As a guitarist I use Coltrane solos as a means of staying in shape technically and harmonically.  I am currently learning the original countdown solo and was not aware of the alternate take. Wow!!!   sounds even crazier. What a treat! Thanks for sharing.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 11_3 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/11.0 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(217968,	7061,	'Jamie Dech',	'tamethesax@gmail.com',	'http://www.tamethesax.com',	'209.171.88.122',	'2019-04-02 11:07:10',	'2019-04-02 17:07:10',	'Agreed. After all, aren\'t even scales and arpeggios, in a sense, \"licks\" as we learn them as patterns and practice them to get proficient with them? We just do it with scales and arpeggios to the point they\'ve become a part of us. Nothing wrong with this approach that I can tell.\r\n\r\nGood article, for sure',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_6) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/12.0.3 Safari/605.1.15',	'',	0,	0),
(217969,	7066,	'Jamie Dech',	'tamethesax@gmail.com',	'http://www.tamethesax.com',	'209.171.88.122',	'2019-04-02 11:12:10',	'2019-04-02 17:12:10',	'..... maaaaybe. But in a sense, aren\'t even scales and arpeggios \"licks\" in that they are progressions through sets of notes that we work to become familiar enough with that they become second-nature, and we own them to the point we can use them in truly unique and musical ways. Perhaps if you think of licks as different forms and types of scales, you two are closer than you think about the need to not merely memorize licks but practice them (as Jamey Aebersold would say) with different articulations and timings until you FEEL them and then they become a part of your style. Just a thought.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_13_6) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/12.0.3 Safari/605.1.15',	'',	0,	0),
(218111,	7061,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'http://www.bandmix.com/larry1261702',	'100.16.128.204',	'2019-04-07 15:30:11',	'2019-04-07 21:30:11',	'Great article. I read the opposing article and I agree w/you. I really l like the comparing jazz improve to a language approach. However you must LISTEN to the language in order to play it.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; WOW64; Trident/7.0; rv:11.0) like Gecko',	'',	0,	0),
(218863,	4406,	'Yaakov Levy',	'yaakov7@hotmail.com',	'',	'107.198.137.220',	'2019-04-27 17:36:42',	'2019-04-27 23:36:42',	'Thanks for the list, but please, you left out a crucial addition: Mr. George Adams who played tenor with Mingus, McCoy Tyner and pianist Don Pullen.  Adams (1940-92) played one of the most incredible solos ever heard on tenor sax. Please listen on Youtube to McCoy Tyner album \"The Greeting\" and the song is \"Fly With The Wind\" on that recording.  George Adams plays what no one since (or before) has done: He plays with incredible passion and creativity, using multiphonics and various textures through the changes.  It is rare to hear a musician play freely and texturally over chord changes...and to so utilizing all the root traditions of the music: spirituals, blues, lyricism etc.\r\n  I saw Mr. Adams play on this song in 1977 at UCLA\'s Royce Hall and it was unforgettable. I was able to see him again and meet him in  Spring of 1988 when the Adams-Pullen Quartet (with Cameron Brown, bass; Dannie Richmond, drums) played at Catalina\'s Bar &amp; Grill in Los Angeles.\r\n   As a professional musician myself on woodwinds, I have never heard anyone play like George Adams. His approach is not only unique but innovative.  His creativity, energy, imagination and musical/technical concepts are completely his own. I am hoping by his inclusion on such lists as yours, he will receive the recognition he so richly deserves. He is survived by his son Quami who lives in the Los Angeles area.\r\n  G-d bless Mr. George Adams for his amazing contribution to music!  See also \"Song Everlasting\" (Adams-Pullen) and Mingus \"Changes\".',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Win64; x64; rv:66.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/66.0',	'',	0,	0),
(218864,	4406,	'Yaakov Levy',	'yaakov7@hotmail.com',	'',	'107.198.137.220',	'2019-04-27 17:43:31',	'2019-04-27 23:43:31',	'Here is the incredible George Adams solo referred to in my comment above.\r\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yQ0XRegNEJ4\r\n\r\nI also agree that Pharaoh Sanders must be included on this list along with David Murray, a remarkable innovator whose bass clarinet work is unmatched since Dolphy.  Also, I would hope you\'d include Albert Ayler.  Did you know he used to practice Charlie Parker solos backward and forward? He had a complete mastery of the horn. His innovations musicially along with his spiritual devotion must be more widely known. John Coltrane himself was an admirer of Ayler\'s work and went to hear him in NY. You can hear on Coltrane\'s last recordings a much heavier, devotion filled vibrato that may have come from listening to Albert Ayler.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Win64; x64; rv:66.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/66.0',	'',	0,	0),
(218865,	4406,	'Yaakov Levy',	'yaakov7@hotmail.com',	'',	'107.198.137.220',	'2019-04-27 17:46:11',	'2019-04-27 23:46:11',	'I also highly recommend that you include Archie Shepp.  His work over many years is quite notable.  He did two duet recordings with pianist Horace Parlan \"Goin\' Home\" (spirituals) and \"Trouble in Mind\" (Blues).  He also did  \"Looking at Bird\" a duet with bassist NHO Pederson. His mastery of the idiom, warmth, sincerity and depth along with a very distinguishable sound make him a necessary addition to this list.  This along with his compositions: \"The Cry of My People\", \"Steam\" etc.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Win64; x64; rv:66.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/66.0',	'',	0,	0),
(218866,	4406,	'Yaakov Levy',	'yaakov7@hotmail.com',	'',	'107.198.137.220',	'2019-04-27 18:04:32',	'2019-04-28 00:04:32',	'Please also listen to Hank Mobley\'s tenor solo on Lee Morgan\'s Ceora. It is a gem:\r\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5V3PXsHqw7M\r\n\r\nAlso, listen to his solos with Miles on Old Folks and I Thought About You. Everything about this work is masterful, brilliant, poignant and beautiful.  Thank you, and G-d bless Hank Mobley!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Win64; x64; rv:66.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/66.0',	'',	0,	0),
(218932,	3899,	'Marquett Smith',	'Marquett@aol.com',	'http://Marquett@aol.com',	'73.171.111.45',	'2019-04-29 13:15:06',	'2019-04-29 19:15:06',	'Relatively new to playing the saxophone, I find myself stuck in sounding practiced and non-expressive.\r\n\r\nYour article will give me new things to practice and expand my learning toolkit.  Thank you for the gifts.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPad; CPU OS 12_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/12.1 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(219193,	2809,	'Kevin Greig',	'mrkevingreig@gmail.com',	'',	'94.197.121.250',	'2019-05-09 07:07:27',	'2019-05-09 12:07:27',	'I have a problem with the noise I was ok on nightshirt as I was on my own but now I\'m on days and can\'t play it . Can\'t play at home either .',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 7.0; EVA-L09) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/74.0.3729.136 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(219559,	5452,	'TenorMoxie',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'47.208.11.42',	'2019-05-25 15:09:14',	'2019-05-25 20:09:14',	' Standard pattern here as in other comment threads.  Doers find something interesting and useful.  Non-doers masturbate their egos with negativity.',	0,	'1',	'',	'comment',	0,	0),
(219560,	5452,	'TenorMoxie',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'47.208.11.42',	'2019-05-25 15:10:46',	'2019-05-25 20:10:46',	' That\'s good to know, since I\'m a cheap bastard who likes a little ugly chic with his instrument enhancements.',	0,	'1',	'',	'comment',	206901,	0),
(219561,	5672,	'TenorMoxie',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'47.208.11.42',	'2019-05-25 16:09:07',	'2019-05-25 21:09:07',	' FWIW, Trane played a SBA, not a VI.  His sound was uncharacteristically out-front for that instrument.  It might be easier to achieve that quality on an 82Z than with a Selmer.  Just goes to show how different equipment can lead towards the same destination for different players.',	0,	'1',	'',	'comment',	192074,	0),
(219562,	5672,	'TenorMoxie',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'47.208.11.42',	'2019-05-25 16:11:52',	'2019-05-25 21:11:52',	' That Doron is such a mischievous lad.....',	0,	'1',	'',	'comment',	192074,	0),
(219563,	5672,	'Thirdeye',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'47.208.11.42',	'2019-05-25 16:20:18',	'2019-05-25 21:20:18',	' I play a 10M but if I were in the market for an instrument with that same sound quality today I would be looking seriously at the Cannonball big bell, Keilwerth SX90R, and the Theo Wanne Mantra.  There might be some lesser-known Taiwanese horns in that same category.  I love my 10M, but that doesn\'t blind me to certain advantages of more up-to-date horns.',	0,	'1',	'',	'comment',	190212,	0),
(219609,	4854,	'Crispin Cioe',	'crispin@crispinmusic.com',	'http://www.crispinmusic.com',	'68.197.79.114',	'2019-05-31 20:14:23',	'2019-06-01 01:14:23',	'Norbert Stachel is brilliant, as a player and working on pieces.  He worked on my main tenor and alto mouthpieces (both vintage Guardala), as well as on a couple of other backup tenor pieces, and made them all infinitely more playable and enjoyable.  I would recommend Norbert to anyone.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_14_5) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/74.0.3729.169 Safari/537.36',	'',	12214,	0),
(219964,	6865,	'TenorMoxie',	'geophone@hotmail.com',	'',	'47.208.11.42',	'2019-06-18 22:02:16',	'2019-06-19 03:02:16',	'The most basic question is whether to use a stand at all.  Using a stand, albeit one of those tubular steel high center-of-gravity cheapies with the foam rubber bell cradle, anywhere outside the home always made me nervous.  I started to sniff around for a good lightweight, compact, secure stand while my interim solution was to detach the neck and put the instrument in its case with the lid ajar.  Then it struck me that no stand would offer the protection of the case, where it <i>can\'t</i> fall.  Maybe doublers needing all their instruments in a quick-draw position benefit from a stand, but I don\'t.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/74.0.3729.169 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(219977,	4071,	'Sean',	'Sean010@yahoo.com',	'http://None',	'41.13.64.60',	'2019-06-19 15:16:49',	'2019-06-19 20:16:49',	'I bought and paid for a Lebayle alto mouthpiece in 2015 which I am still waiting for. Go and look at Sax on The Web Forum and see how many people Fred Lebayle has ripped off. You are advertising products of him. Please do your homework when supporting a person. Do not buy Lebayle’s stuff not even from ebay or anywhere',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 12_3_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/12.1.1 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(219981,	4071,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//',	'70.113.101.140',	'2019-06-19 17:41:01',	'2019-06-19 22:41:01',	'Youngee and Sean, it looks like many people have experienced what you\'ve experienced, and I am so sorry to hear it! To reflect the situation, I have updated this article with a warning at the beginning of the article that Lebayle is not a company that anyone should be doing business with at the moment. Thanks for bringing it to my attention.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_14_5) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/74.0.3729.169 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	1),
(220181,	6110,	'LUIS SANTAMARIA',	'ritmoyalma@hotmail.com',	'',	'189.202.227.196',	'2019-06-28 10:38:40',	'2019-06-28 15:38:40',	'MUCHAS GRACIAS POR TUS COMENTARIOS SOBRE LOS EQUIPOS YA ESO NOS AYUDA A TOMAR UNA DECISIÓN YA QUE AVECES NO TENEMOS LA OPORTUNIDAD DE PODER PROBAR TODOS LOS EQUIPOS O ACCESORIOS QUE NOS INTERESAN Y POR ELLO TOMAMOS MALAS DECISIONES Y Y GASTAMOS DE MÁS, ACABO DE ADQUIRIR UNA JODY JAZZ SUPER JET 7 AVER QUE PASA.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 6.1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/75.0.3770.100 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(220415,	7172,	'Mark Sepinuck',	'connsaxman@comcast.net',	'http://www.10mfan.com',	'71.196.86.71',	'2019-07-08 15:04:08',	'2019-07-08 20:04:08',	'Zach,\r\nI just wanted to thank you for the beautiful review of the two mouthpieces I sent you. \r\nI am very appreciative of ALL  of your efforts and the time you spent to get to know the pieces and put up your review. It was beautifully done, and I am very glad you had a chance to try these out. . \r\n\r\nAll the best, \r\nMark Sepinuck\r\n\r\n10MFAN Mouthpieces',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 12_3_1 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/12.1.1 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(220755,	4107,	'Ruston',	'rustonreynolds@gmail.com',	'http://Windsmithmusic.com',	'174.224.19.245',	'2019-07-31 12:28:41',	'2019-07-31 17:28:41',	'I’m getting about 3-4 hours out of their Black Bamboo and Hinoki reeds before they start curling towards the tip. Loved the tone, but can justify spending 5x’s the cost for a reed that lasts a fraction of the time a cane reed does. I’ve written the company about my experience and that of several other players I know. No response yet. Google tells me this experience is common. Too bad. Now if they were $2-3 each, I’d play on one a couple of times, toss it and feel good about it.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 12_2 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/12.1 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1',	'',	0,	0),
(220867,	3827,	'Dror Ben Gur',	'drorbengur@gmail.com',	'http://www.saxinst.com',	'109.67.21.1',	'2019-08-04 00:56:37',	'2019-08-04 05:56:37',	'Are there any shops in Poland?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_11_6) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/75.0.3770.100 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(221168,	337,	'mauricio lagunes melchor',	'mauriciolagunesm@outlook.com',	'',	'200.68.142.10',	'2019-08-14 11:25:48',	'2019-08-14 16:25:48',	'What about tenor sax selmer ts 500',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; SM-J700M) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/73.0.3683.90 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(221358,	3337,	'Rich',	'richard.greenberg@gmail.com',	'',	'73.157.111.59',	'2019-08-21 19:29:37',	'2019-08-22 00:29:37',	'Hi all. Thought I would throw something in here. I have been playing the sax (tenor, alto, flute, clarinet) for about 50 years (including a lot of club-date and live \"professional gigs\" .I retired recently from my day gig and have quite a bit of time on my hands. I have been practicing quite a bit - a good thing -  but in my own way, which I have found to be quite pleasant - and keeps me practicing. I only (for the most part) practice with play along stuff. I concentrate on the basics (intonation, tone, articulation, evenness) while playing along. I try to attempt phrases (including harmonic movements between changes) that challenge my technique, and if I do not succeed, will play the phrase over and over a few times- and catch up to the play along afterwards. I have found that I have fun playing and practicing in this manner and having fun is what keeps me practicing.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; CrOS armv7l 12239.67.0) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/76.0.3809.102 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(221390,	6945,	'Matthew Fontana',	'mfclarinet1928@gmail.com',	'',	'99.203.119.43',	'2019-08-22 21:31:54',	'2019-08-23 02:31:54',	'What size ishimori ligature did you use for the Theo wanne?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 12_3 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) CriOS/76.0.3809.81 Mobile/15E148 Safari/605.1',	'',	0,	0),
(221392,	6945,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'99.155.39.225',	'2019-08-22 22:04:17',	'2019-08-23 03:04:17',	'Hey Matt,\r\n\r\nMy Ishimori Lig size was the one that would fit a V16 or Standard Hard Rubber Otto Link Mouthpiece. \r\n\r\nhttps://www.woodsysmusic.com/products/wood-stone-ishimori-woodwind-ligature?variant=830843486233\r\n\r\nHas a few options',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/76.0.3809.100 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(221405,	6945,	'Matthew Fontana',	'mfclarinet1928@gmail.com',	'',	'67.80.34.202',	'2019-08-23 11:36:43',	'2019-08-23 16:36:43',	'Hello Zachary,\r\n\r\nThank you so much for your response. I just received my new Theo Wanne Slant 2 and really love it. I use the ishimori ligature on my clarinet and have loved it so I want to pick one up for the Slant. This review was super helpful.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 12_4 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) CriOS/76.0.3809.81 Mobile/15E148 Safari/605.1',	'',	221392,	0),
(221406,	6945,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'99.155.39.225',	'2019-08-23 12:35:46',	'2019-08-23 17:35:46',	'Hello Matt,\r\n\r\nGlad to hear! I like the sterling silver ishimori ligature but it comes all down to personal preference and what works for your setup.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_14_6) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/76.0.3809.100 Safari/537.36',	'',	221405,	0),
(221564,	2809,	'Levent',	'leventcirit@gmail.com',	'',	'46.104.50.97',	'2019-08-29 01:07:32',	'2019-08-29 06:07:32',	'Hi there,\r\nGreat writing for us to give idea about what to do.\r\nI\'m a newbie who\'s interested in learning sax but haven\'t bought a sax yet. I live at a flat, at the entrance floor. I also have opportunity to go down stairs to the basement but as basement is an empty floor, i think it will make much more echoe there.\r\nWhat do you think about playing at basement while it\'s me sitting at this first floor? Will it be still noisiy to disturb other neighbors?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 6.0.1; SAMSUNG SM-N910C) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) SamsungBrowser/10.1 Chrome/71.0.3578.99 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(221607,	5907,	'Ian Vantull.',	'yakiyn@mail.com',	'',	'108.236.219.168',	'2019-08-30 13:50:29',	'2019-08-30 18:50:29',	'I appreciate your sharing. It opened up some doors, affording me a different perspective and approach. I made a quantum leap instantly, esp. since I am not one to be in denial, making me a fast learner. Understanding makes a critical difference. You, being empathetic, simplify the abstract, making you a great teacher.  Thanks so much. Keep up the great work.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/64.0.3282.140 Safari/537.36 Edge/17.17134',	'',	0,	0),
(221821,	2161,	'Jasmine The Sax Lover',	'jasminevera1706@gmail.com',	'',	'65.130.180.202',	'2019-09-06 22:39:36',	'2019-09-07 03:39:36',	'I really, really want a synthetic reed for my alto sax. However, I am constantly hearing that despite their durance, they don\'t sound as well as a cane reed. I\'m only in 8th grade, so getting that tone perfect is important for me. But my cane reeds are always breaking. It becomes incredibly annoying and stressful at times. Also, my cane reeds never want to stay damp, so a synthetic would be nice for that too. What advice does anyone have for me? (Please take into consideration my youth and what you feel is most important for it.)',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (X11; CrOS x86_64 12239.92.1) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/76.0.3809.136 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(221841,	7235,	'Gyedu-Blay Ambolley',	'ambolleyb@hotmail.com',	'http://gyedublayambolley.com',	'154.160.20.116',	'2019-09-07 15:10:59',	'2019-09-07 20:10:59',	'Nice one',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 9; SM-G965F) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/75.0.3770.143 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(221918,	4071,	'micheal murray',	'michealmurray52@gmail.com',	'',	'86.43.126.46',	'2019-09-09 19:05:41',	'2019-09-10 00:05:41',	'Hi there! Just wanted to let you know that I cant access the audio clips for some reason!',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 7.0; SM-A510F) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/76.0.3809.132 Mobile Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(222017,	1937,	'John Laughter',	'JSAXL@aol.com',	'https://www.facebook.com/john.laughter',	'68.1.133.162',	'2019-09-12 21:13:50',	'2019-09-13 02:13:50',	'If you are having a difficult time getting the tongue to produce the effect, try using just the mouthpiece/reed for several minutes. Then attach the neck and m/p and practice on it for several minutes then attach the sax. Same for the growl. Coordinating the airstream and tongue for the flutter and airstream and humming for the growl can (for some players) be easier by starting with just the mouthpiece/reed. Just a suggestion.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/76.0.3809.132 Safari/537.36',	'',	0,	0),
(222031,	1937,	'John Laughter',	'JSAXL@aol.com',	'https://www.facebook.com/john.laughter',	'68.1.133.162',	'2019-09-13 06:09:41',	'2019-09-13 11:09:41',	'Maybe \"Rock &amp; Roll Saxophone\r\nBook/CD Pack-2nd edition\"?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/76.0.3809.132 Safari/537.36',	'',	210340,	0),
(222137,	4854,	'Memory of Music',	'pencho.minchev@abv.bg',	'',	'213.226.17.10',	'2019-09-18 01:58:10',	'2019-09-18 06:58:10',	'Hello everybody ! How about a good refacers i Europe. Do you know any ?!?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 5.0.1; GT-I9505 Build/LRX22C; wv) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/4.0 Chrome/69.0.3497.100 Mobile Safari/537.36 [FB_IAB/FB4A;FBAV/233.0.0.36.117;]',	'',	0,	0),
(222228,	2161,	'David',	'daviddiamond@comcast.net',	'',	'69.248.206.239',	'2019-09-22 16:48:20',	'2019-09-22 21:48:20',	'mrG, I noticed your comment about using a synthetic for your xaphoon.  I switched to a Légère for my Erik-the-Flutemaker Tenor All Terrain Sax for the same reason - convenience.  It plays easier and more consistently, and is always ready.  But it is at the expense of warmth.   The Tenor All Terrain Sax has a non-replaceable, glued-in, Rico alto mouthpiece with a 1.5 tenor reed.  Have you experimented with different  cane reeds for your xaphoon?  Which ones produce the warmest, most woody sound?  Is yours an ABS or a wood xaphoon?\r\n\r\nRegards.\r\nDavid D.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/76.0.3809.132 Safari/537.36 OPR/63.0.3368.94',	'',	750,	0),
(222233,	2161,	'David',	'daviddiamond@comcast.net',	'',	'69.248.206.239',	'2019-09-22 19:48:38',	'2019-09-23 00:48:38',	'Now that I think about, even though I cannot swap out the mouth piece, I can try a different ligature on my Rico mouthpiece.  The one that is there now is a two-screw, brass ligature.  Perhaps a soft ligature would make the tone more mellow.\r\n\r\nAny opinions?\r\n\r\nDavid',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/76.0.3809.132 Safari/537.36 OPR/63.0.3368.94',	'',	222228,	0),
(222235,	2161,	'David',	'daviddiamond@comcast.net',	'',	'69.248.206.239',	'2019-09-22 21:15:01',	'2019-09-23 02:15:01',	'Thanks for the Reed Vitalizer product tip.  If this makes it easier to use reeds without having to wet them first, I may go back to cane.  I like the convenience, playability and accuracy of synthetic, but I prefer the tone of cane.',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/76.0.3809.132 Safari/537.36 OPR/63.0.3368.94',	'',	815,	0),
(222236,	2161,	'David',	'daviddiamond@comcast.net',	'',	'69.248.206.239',	'2019-09-22 21:20:00',	'2019-09-23 02:20:00',	'Do you still wet and condition new reeds first, or do you place them right from their original packaging into the Reed Vitalizer case?',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/76.0.3809.132 Safari/537.36 OPR/63.0.3368.94',	'',	222235,	0),
(222275,	1,	'Eric',	'puppeteeric@gmail.com',	'http://www.puppeteeric.com',	'108.48.47.241',	'2019-09-25 23:26:33',	'2019-09-26 04:26:33',	'Hello from Maryland, Doron, \r\nA friend gifted me a saxophone today and I have never heard of the maker. What information do you have on \"Centurion\" saxophones and how does one tell whether they stack up to modern pro horns? It has a high F-sharp key, a heavy and solid stack, as well as a \"pro-feel\" to the spring action. \r\n\r\nThank you,',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_14_6) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 (KHTML, like Gecko) Version/13.0.1 Safari/605.1.15',	'',	0,	0),
