(228805,	3603,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'99.155.39.225',	'2020-05-25 16:03:08',	'2020-05-25 21:03:08',	'Hey William,\r\n\r\nI\'ve included a link to the D\'Addario reed comparison chart. On alexander\'s website, they state to compare the reed strength of there reeds to a vandoren traditional blue box. My thought would be if a D\'Addario Select Jazz 3s is similar to a Vandoren blue box 2.5 then I would buy the Alexander NY 2.5 reed strength. I will say of all the Alexander reed types, the Superial was my favorite. If you were concerned about the reed being to soft then I recommend always going up a half step and using a reedgeek or light sand paper (reedgeek is better) to remove some cane so the reed is less hard.\r\n\r\nhttps://www.daddario.com/globalassets/learn-more-content/woodwinds/dw_reed_strength_comparison_chart_saxophone.pdf\r\n\r\nHope this helps\r\n\r\nZach',	0,	'1',	'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/83.0.4103.61 Safari/537.36',	'',	228801,	0),
