(229451,	7821,	'LUIS SANTAMARIA',	'ritmoyalma@hotmail.com',	'',	'189.202.227.196',	'2019-06-28 10:38:40',	'2019-06-28 15:38:40',	'MUCHAS GRACIAS POR TUS COMENTARIOS SOBRE LOS EQUIPOS YA ESO NOS AYUDA A TOMAR UNA DECISIÓN YA QUE AVECES NO TENEMOS LA OPORTUNIDAD DE PODER PROBAR TODOS LOS EQUIPOS O ACCESORIOS QUE NOS INTERESAN Y POR ELLO TOMAMOS MALAS DECISIONES Y Y GASTAMOS DE MÁS, ACABO DE ADQUIRIR UNA JODY JAZZ SUPER JET 7 AVER QUE PASA.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229452,	7822,	'Earl Belcher',	'earlslb@aol.com',	'http://www.earltiptopbelcher.com',	'207.38.186.52',	'2019-01-18 12:54:07',	'2019-01-18 18:54:07',	'I\'m looking for an Brilhart Ligature screw with the black plastic on it, does anyone sell them or know someone that does ?',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229453,	7823,	'Jay Rodriguez',	'jayrodri@gmail.com',	'https://www.jayrodriguez.com',	'66.87.31.42',	'2017-10-23 07:46:15',	'2017-10-23 14:46:15',	'Excellent resource for all musicians . !',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229454,	7823,	'Eddy Bourjolly',	'Ebourjolly@aol.com',	'',	'108.46.148.64',	'2019-04-02 10:45:06',	'2019-04-02 16:45:06',	'As a guitarist I use Coltrane solos as a means of staying in shape technically and harmonically.  I am currently learning the original countdown solo and was not aware of the alternate take. Wow!!!   sounds even crazier. What a treat! Thanks for sharing.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229455,	7823,	'Sam',	'vegasammy@hotmail.com',	'',	'128.230.72.106',	'2020-03-15 16:25:20',	'2020-03-15 21:25:20',	'OMG that was fun!',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229456,	7824,	'Kathy Marshall',	'Kaco61@att.net',	'',	'12.105.36.114',	'2018-01-08 09:53:05',	'2018-01-08 15:53:05',	'I signed up previously but I don\'t think I ever received the FREE sax tips booklet + 3-part audio master class series with Bob Sheppard, Tim Price &amp; Ricky Sweum.  Can I still receive this?  Thank you.   Kathy Marshall',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229457,	7824,	'Kevin',	'kev.gould@comcast.net',	'',	'98.217.202.70',	'2018-01-08 12:31:56',	'2018-01-08 18:31:56',	'I did not receive the FREE sax tips booklet. Is there a download site?',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229458,	7824,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://www.bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com//',	'70.113.101.140',	'2018-01-08 13:05:26',	'2018-01-08 19:05:26',	'Hey Kathy and Kevin, apologies if you didn\'t get the booklet, let me take a look and get back to you asap.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	1),
(229459,	7824,	'Doron Orenstein',	'doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com',	'https://www.bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com//',	'70.113.101.140',	'2018-01-08 13:11:47',	'2018-01-08 19:11:47',	'Hello again Kathy and Kevin, I just tried subscribing myself and upon confirming my email address, I got an email back with the subject line, \"Best Saxophone Website Ever List: Subscription Confirmed\". This email contains a link that reads, \"click here to get your FREE saxophone tips booklet\".\nCan you please confirm whether or not you received an email with this subject line?',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	1),
(229460,	7825,	'Tony Lopez',	'Lopez4081@sbcglobal.net',	'',	'172.56.40.114',	'2018-01-23 10:00:56',	'2018-01-23 16:00:56',	'Thanks so much for the insight. I hear melodies in my head but just cannot seem to transfer that to my axe.As an exercise I sing a short two measure riff and try to play it back using my axe.Seems to be working. I also try that same riff in different keys.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229461,	7825,	'Jon Gordon',	'JONGORDONMUSIC1@GMAIL.COM',	'https://jongordonmusic.com',	'24.78.93.190',	'2018-01-24 17:49:12',	'2018-01-24 23:49:12',	'Hey Tony, that sounds like a good way to do it. Get small pieces of things you\'re hearing on the horn. Take them through the keys. See how and where you can apply them in the context of basic harmony, ii, v, I\'s and tunes. But also try to get them at the piano and see if they can be the start of a composition. Sometimes for me it will just be an interval, like a 2nd, that will inspire a piece or an idea to develop when improvising. A lot of great pieces and improvisations start with a small idea, and the artistry in it isn\'t the idea itself so much as what you do with it...',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229462,	7826,	'John Plichta',	'jfp502@gmail.com',	'',	'24.127.83.214',	'2018-02-19 19:12:46',	'2018-02-20 01:12:46',	'I\'m a newbe, all those sharps and flats drive me up the wall.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229463,	7826,	'Adrian Hopper',	'hoppers@freeuk.com',	'',	'143.159.71.118',	'2018-02-20 04:18:00',	'2018-02-20 10:18:00',	'Think in \'steps\' like the old session guys do - then a sharp or flat is just one step away from it\'s nearest whole note,don\'t forget that they\'re named differently whether ascending or descending.\nRegards, Another Newbie(ish)',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229464,	7826,	'Larry Weintraub',	'lweintraub1@cox.net',	'',	'70.160.174.58',	'2018-02-20 18:10:00',	'2018-02-21 00:10:00',	'Bob: I am a tenor sax player too but I play some piano. I had to get past the piano test in college and just expanded it from there.\nI like to have musical conversations w/my drummer, it\'s a lot of fun. A few things I actually dislike. A) a bass player who does not know his role in the ensemble, playing lots of altered notes that are not called for in the tune, you know a guy who is playing # 11ths but never plays the root or 5th while the head and solos are happening. On his solo go ahead, knock yourself out. Also a bass player who plays to busy during the head of the tune. Here we are playing a simple blues and the bass player is running all over the place. B) a piano player that doesn\'t voice chords well and just plays to vanilla. C) a drummer who just plays time and doesn\'t setup the various sections of a tune. D) anyone who is not listening and just going on auto-pilot.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229465,	7828,	'Ted Reynolds',	'Danetre.Ted@gmail.com',	'',	'172.88.42.236',	'2018-06-08 17:19:34',	'2018-06-08 23:19:34',	'Incredible in its simplicity, sitting on my porch just singing through the rhythms, just bought the book.\nTHANK YOU#',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229466,	7828,	'DN Rhythm',	'studiod179@att.net',	'http://DNrhythm.com',	'99.16.143.136',	'2018-06-08 21:26:33',	'2018-06-09 03:26:33',	'I\'m always glad to share with the music community. I always suggest using the Bebopish words, licks and phrases  in the book before, in the middle and at the end of other things you like to play, adding to your vocabulary. The book helps to \"Sing Da Bebop\" in a fun and easy way. Have fun!\n \"Easy Easy Bebop\"',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229467,	7829,	'Eileen Stirling',	'eileenstirling@ymail.com',	'',	'194.207.133.208',	'2018-10-17 10:12:35',	'2018-10-17 16:12:35',	'You are an inspiration Matthew, a fantastic musician and teacher! Thank you for sharing your valuable tips and for your encouraging words of wisdom. You are a brilliant saxophonist and an equally brilliant educator. You give so much to so many and always with  enduring patience, understanding and wit...... Thank you!',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229468,	7830,	'Paul Colombo',	'paulguitarcolombo@gmail.com',	'',	'24.246.230.34',	'2018-10-25 12:31:17',	'2018-10-25 18:31:17',	'Great advice written by a pro musician!',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229469,	7830,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweinraub1@cox.net',	'',	'68.107.158.241',	'2018-10-25 13:36:01',	'2018-10-25 19:36:01',	'Thank you Paul. Hope everyone is well.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	229468,	0),
(229470,	7832,	'Jay Metcalf',	'jay@bettersax.com',	'https://bettersax.com',	'5.51.36.90',	'2019-03-21 12:37:28',	'2019-03-21 18:37:28',	'Amen to that...',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229471,	7832,	'Jim Bator',	'jmsbtr@gmail.com',	'',	'174.103.86.195',	'2019-03-21 19:11:37',	'2019-03-22 01:11:37',	'Great article ....',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229472,	7832,	'Olujimi Tafataona',	'olujimitafataona@yahoo.com',	'http://www.inthetraditionjazz.net',	'64.94.35.33',	'2019-03-21 20:39:43',	'2019-03-22 02:39:43',	'I wholeheartedly agree with everything in this article.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229473,	7832,	'Jamie Dech',	'tamethesax@gmail.com',	'http://www.tamethesax.com',	'209.171.88.122',	'2019-04-02 11:07:10',	'2019-04-02 17:07:10',	'Agreed. After all, aren\'t even scales and arpeggios, in a sense, \"licks\" as we learn them as patterns and practice them to get proficient with them? We just do it with scales and arpeggios to the point they\'ve become a part of us. Nothing wrong with this approach that I can tell.\nGood article, for sure',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229474,	7832,	'Larry Weintraub',	'Lweintraub1@cox.net',	'http://www.bandmix.com/larry1261702',	'100.16.128.204',	'2019-04-07 15:30:11',	'2019-04-07 21:30:11',	'Great article. I read the opposing article and I agree w/you. I really l like the comparing jazz improve to a language approach. However you must LISTEN to the language in order to play it.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229475,	7833,	'Jamie Dech',	'tamethesax@gmail.com',	'http://www.tamethesax.com',	'209.171.88.122',	'2019-04-02 11:12:10',	'2019-04-02 17:12:10',	'..... maaaaybe. But in a sense, aren\'t even scales and arpeggios \"licks\" in that they are progressions through sets of notes that we work to become familiar enough with that they become second-nature, and we own them to the point we can use them in truly unique and musical ways. Perhaps if you think of licks as different forms and types of scales, you two are closer than you think about the need to not merely memorize licks but practice them (as Jamey Aebersold would say) with different articulations and timings until you FEEL them and then they become a part of your style. Just a thought.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229476,	7833,	'9 Pieces of Advice for Young Saxophonists &raquo; Best. Saxophone. Website. Ever.',	'',	'https://www.bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com/9-pieces-of-advice-for-young-saxophonists/',	'35.193.149.198',	'2020-04-04 10:37:05',	'2020-04-04 15:37:05',	'[&#8230;] only as good as you play. Your grades don’t matter, the licks and solos you learned don’t matter, what you know (or think you know) doesn’t matter. The only [&#8230;]',	0,	'1',	'',	'pingback',	0,	0),
(229477,	7834,	'Mark Sepinuck',	'connsaxman@comcast.net',	'http://www.10mfan.com',	'71.196.86.71',	'2019-07-08 15:04:08',	'2019-07-08 20:04:08',	'Zach,\nI just wanted to thank you for the beautiful review of the two mouthpieces I sent you.\nI am very appreciative of ALL  of your efforts and the time you spent to get to know the pieces and put up your review. It was beautifully done, and I am very glad you had a chance to try these out. .\nAll the best,\nMark Sepinuck\n10MFAN Mouthpieces',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229478,	7836,	'George Godliveth',	'godlivethg@gmail.com',	'http://www.facebook.com/george.godliveth',	'107.167.109.90',	'2019-10-07 07:11:10',	'2019-10-07 12:11:10',	'Thank alot. I really appreciate.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229479,	7839,	'Ryan',	'Rbarber7@hotmail.com',	'',	'152.78.0.201',	'2019-11-09 03:02:18',	'2019-11-09 09:02:18',	'As much as I love to experiment with equipment and the differences they make, I think I draw the line at ligature finish.  That\'s not to say there is absolutely no difference, but in my mind it\'s so insignificant that it\'s not worth considering.  Although I did enjoy trying the MO a while back and it has a good balance of Reed support whilst not damping the sound very much.  One of my favourites.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229480,	7839,	'Zachary Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'99.155.39.225',	'2019-11-09 17:51:13',	'2019-11-09 23:51:13',	'Hey Ryan,\nIt\'s very subjective. I think finish or material can be a difference but the to what extent its difficult to say and is very much a personal preference but I do see your point and agree that the M|O is a good overall ligature.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229481,	7839,	'Juan',	'juan@gmail.com',	'',	'27.106.116.125',	'2019-12-24 02:30:22',	'2019-12-24 08:30:22',	'Hello Zach, don\'t you think it would be appropiate to also test two MO with same finish against each other? to conclude if these differences aren\'t just because its a different piece rather than finish.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229482,	7839,	'Zach Sollitto',	'zsollitto@bellsouth.net',	'',	'99.156.125.176',	'2019-12-24 10:02:50',	'2019-12-24 16:02:50',	'Hello Juan,\nI hoping to potentially do so at NAMM 2020 this year. The Pink Gold finish M|O model is not as easy to get as the other models which is why I only tried one.',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	229481,	1),
(229483,	7841,	'Jeff',	'Bassinson@gmail.com',	'http://MoJazz.net',	'174.234.135.39',	'2020-02-24 11:16:40',	'2020-02-24 17:16:40',	'Nice Missouri photo.  Who shot it?',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0),
(229484,	7841,	'Tim',	'Yourbuildertim@gmail.com',	'',	'107.77.234.47',	'2020-03-31 22:18:26',	'2020-04-01 03:18:26',	'I’m unqualified to even comment &gt;&gt; I grew up seeing the navy blues band every weekend in DC(incredible), Count Basie etc... those sax players SHREDDED!!! .. sure they got quiet and moody too.. you are next Generation!!! Absolutely mind blowing to see live!!🤦‍♂️🙌',	0,	'1',	'',	'',	0,	0);
INSERT INTO `wp_ccut_contact_form_7` (`cf7_unit_id`, `title`, `form`, `mail`, `mail_2`, `messages`, `additional_settings`) VALUES
(1,	'Contact form 1',	'<p><strong>Your Name (required)</strong><br />\r\n    [text* your-name] </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Your Email (required)</strong><br />\r\n    [email* your-email] </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Subject</strong><br />\r\n    [text your-subject] </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Your Message</strong><br />\r\n    [textarea your-message] </p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"contact_form_submit\">[submit \"Send\"]</p>',	'a:7:{s:7:\"subject\";s:49:\"From bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com: [your-subject]\";s:6:\"sender\";s:26:\"[your-name] <[your-email]>\";s:4:\"body\";s:210:\"From: [your-name] <[your-email]>\r\nSubject: [your-subject]\r\n\r\nMessage Body:\r\n[your-message]\r\n\r\n--\r\nThis mail is sent via contact form on Best. Saxophone. Website. Ever. https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local/\";s:9:\"recipient\";s:20:\"buffallo66@gmail.com\";s:18:\"additional_headers\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"attachments\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"use_html\";s:0:\"\";}',	'a:8:{s:6:\"active\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"subject\";s:14:\"[your-subject]\";s:6:\"sender\";s:26:\"[your-name] <[your-email]>\";s:4:\"body\";s:149:\"Message body:\r\n[your-message]\r\n\r\n--\r\nThis mail is sent via contact form on Best. Saxophone. Website. Ever. https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local/\";s:9:\"recipient\";s:12:\"[your-email]\";s:18:\"additional_headers\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"attachments\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"use_html\";s:0:\"\";}',	'a:13:{s:12:\"mail_sent_ok\";s:43:\"Your message was sent successfully. Thanks.\";s:12:\"mail_sent_ng\";s:84:\"Failed to send your message. Please try later or contact administrator by other way.\";s:17:\"akismet_says_spam\";s:84:\"Failed to send your message. Please try later or contact administrator by other way.\";s:16:\"validation_error\";s:74:\"Validation errors occurred. Please confirm the fields and submit it again.\";s:12:\"accept_terms\";s:35:\"Please accept the terms to proceed.\";s:13:\"invalid_email\";s:28:\"Email address seems invalid.\";s:16:\"invalid_required\";s:31:\"Please fill the required field.\";s:17:\"captcha_not_match\";s:31:\"Your entered code is incorrect.\";s:23:\"quiz_answer_not_correct\";s:27:\"Your answer is not correct.\";s:13:\"upload_failed\";s:22:\"Failed to upload file.\";s:24:\"upload_file_type_invalid\";s:30:\"This file type is not allowed.\";s:21:\"upload_file_too_large\";s:23:\"This file is too large.\";s:23:\"upload_failed_php_error\";s:38:\"Failed to upload file. Error occurred.\";}',	''),
(2,	'Reed Review Submission Form',	'<p><strong>Your Full Name *</strong> <br />\r\n    [text* your-name] </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Your Email *</strong> <br />\r\n    [email* your-email] </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Reed Being Reviewed *</strong> (brand of reed, ie: \"Vandoren Java\" or \"LaVoz\")<br />\r\n    [text* reed-brand] </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Your Review of This Reed *</strong><br />\r\n    [textarea* your-review] </p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Your Rating for Sound Quality of Reed *</strong> (Do you like how you sound on these reeds?)<br />\r\n   [select* sound-quality include_blank \"5 (I love the way I sound on these reeds)\" \"4\" \"3\" \"2\" \"1 (I hate the way I sound on these reeds)\"]</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Your Rating for Consistency of Quality *</strong> (Are the reeds in a single box of similar quality, or are some of them much worse than others?)<br />\r\n    [select* reed-consistency include_blank \"5 (highest level of consistency)\" \"4\" \"3\" \"2\" \"1 (lowest level of consistency)\"]</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Your Rating for Responsiveness of Reed *</strong> (How did these reeds feel when playing? Did articulation on these reeds seem unfocused? Did the sound become constricted when playing loudly – even when you were using the correct strength?)<br />\r\n    [select* reed-responsiveness include_blank \"5 (This reed is extremely responsive)\" \"4\" \"3\" \"2\" \"1 (This reed is not responsive at all)\"]</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Would you like to have your name publicly listed on the site as the reviewer for this reed?</strong><br />\r\n [radio radio-192 \"Yes\" \"No\"]</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>If you\'d like to have your name displayed, would you also like your name to be linked to a particular website? If so, please enter the URL for the website you\'d like to link to here:</strong><br />\r\n [text website-link]\r\n</p> \r\n\r\n\r\n<p>[submit \"Send\"]</p>',	'a:7:{s:7:\"subject\";s:36:\"Saxophone Reed Review ([reed-brand])\";s:6:\"sender\";s:26:\"[your-name] <[your-email]>\";s:4:\"body\";s:457:\"From: [your-name] \r\n\r\nEmail Address: [your-email]\r\n\r\nBrand of Reed: [reed-brand]\r\n\r\nReed Review:\r\n[your-review]\r\n\r\nSound Quality: [sound-quality]\r\n\r\nConsistency of Reed Quality: [reed-consistency]\r\n\r\nReed Responsiveness: [reed-responsiveness]\r\n\r\nDisplay name of reviewer: [radio-192]\r\n\r\nWebsite to link reviewer name to: [website-link]\r\n\r\n\r\n--\r\nThis mail is sent via contact form on Best. Saxophone. Website. Ever. https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local/\";s:9:\"recipient\";s:34:\"doron@bestsaxophonewebsiteever.com\";s:18:\"additional_headers\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"attachments\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"use_html\";s:0:\"\";}',	'a:8:{s:6:\"active\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"subject\";s:14:\"[your-subject]\";s:6:\"sender\";s:26:\"[your-name] <[your-email]>\";s:4:\"body\";s:149:\"Message body:\r\n[your-message]\r\n\r\n--\r\nThis mail is sent via contact form on Best. Saxophone. Website. Ever. https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local/\";s:9:\"recipient\";s:12:\"[your-email]\";s:18:\"additional_headers\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"attachments\";s:0:\"\";s:8:\"use_html\";s:0:\"\";}',	'a:13:{s:12:\"mail_sent_ok\";s:43:\"Your message was sent successfully. Thanks.\";s:12:\"mail_sent_ng\";s:84:\"Failed to send your message. Please try later or contact administrator by other way.\";s:17:\"akismet_says_spam\";s:84:\"Failed to send your message. Please try later or contact administrator by other way.\";s:16:\"validation_error\";s:74:\"Validation errors occurred. Please confirm the fields and submit it again.\";s:12:\"accept_terms\";s:35:\"Please accept the terms to proceed.\";s:13:\"invalid_email\";s:28:\"Email address seems invalid.\";s:16:\"invalid_required\";s:31:\"Please fill the required field.\";s:17:\"captcha_not_match\";s:31:\"Your entered code is incorrect.\";s:23:\"quiz_answer_not_correct\";s:27:\"Your answer is not correct.\";s:13:\"upload_failed\";s:22:\"Failed to upload file.\";s:24:\"upload_file_type_invalid\";s:30:\"This file typ