(2650,	756,	'Notes',	'PART 1: What are overtones\r\n\r\n- effects of equipment on overtones\r\n\r\nPART 2: why should you practice them\r\n\r\n- joe viola\r\n\r\nPART 3: Basic overtone exercises\r\n\r\n- ask Pete Thomas if I can use his (https://tamingthesaxophone.com/saxophone-harmonics-overtones.html)\r\n- write my own\r\n- proper equipment for dark and bright sounds\r\n\r\novertones don\'t really improve you tone(long tones are for that), but it enables you to have more control. They will help you to eventally have enough control that you will be able to get the altissimo notes with ease and in tune. It is really good if you use a tuner when doing over tones to try and get it in tune. Well at least that\'s what I think.\r\n\r\nHelps you to make intervallic jumps\r\n\r\n(see Joe allard PDF for more reasons)'),
