(3883,	1665,	'Notes',	'Fender Rumble 15 Amplifier\r\n\r\n<h2>M-Audio Oxygen25 25 Key MIDI Controller</h2>\r\nThis is a nice little keyboard controller that also makes a bunch of cool sounds. If you need some nice sounds to add to your music or film project, this little keyboard will do the trick. I use this with Sony ACID Music (Cost: $80) or Sony Vegas, and this small keyboard has a ton of sound options. For you Mac lovers out there, this works great with Garage Band as well! It has at least 4 octaves and essentially is a plug-and-play device. Not too steep of a learning curve either. Cost is approximately $129.\r\n\r\n<strong>For more information on the M-Audio Oxygen25 25 Key MIDI Controller, <a href=\"https://click.linksynergy.com/fs-bin/click?id=HRLLNJha7rU&amp;subid=&amp;offerid=163557.1&amp;type=10&amp;tmpid=4359&amp;RD_PARM1=http%253A%252F%252Fwww.samash.com%252Fp%252FM-Audio_Oxygen25%25252025%252520Key%252520MIDI%252520Controller_-49954014\">CLICK HERE</a>. </strong>\r\n\r\nThis is a nice and inexpensive amp that puts out enough sound to support a live saxophone (and that sax can get to be pretty loud as your neighbors will most likely be able to tell you). I use a microphone and a laptop while plugging in my  MP3 player so I can play along with recorded music. Or I can run a line out from my computer and send music from other sources into the amp. It has a nice equalizer which produces a decent sound. You can also hook up headphones and additional speakers (using adapters from Radio Shack or any other other electronics store) so you can hear yourself play while also being able to hear your \"virtual backup band.\" The cost for the Fender Rumble 15 is approximately $99.'),
