(2011,	1,	'2011-04-11 06:00:35',	'2011-04-11 13:00:35',	'<img class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-2013\" title=\"how-to-bend-notes-on-the-saxophone\" src=\"https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//wp-content/uploads/how-to-bend-notes-on-the-saxophone1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"628\" height=\"239\" />One of the most human-sounding instruments on the planet, the <strong>saxophone requires subtlety and finesse in order to truly sing</strong>. During those early days on the horn, we\'re doing a lot more barking, squeaking, and squaking than singing.\r\n\r\nAlthough we should all aspire to be <em>eternal students</em>, <strong>we don\'t necessarily have to <em>sound</em> like students.</strong>\r\n\r\nOne of the trademarks of a student-sounding saxophonist is the way they bend, or scoop their notes.<strong> The student bends their notes very drastically and abruptly</strong> - a practice that I refer to as the <em>\"Marching Band Scoop.\"</em>\r\n\r\nIn this video, I demonstrate the \"Marching Band Scoop\" while also describing and demonstrating what I consider to be the more polished and professional approach to this essential skill.\r\n\r\nNow when it comes to video, I, myself most certainly come off as a <em>student</em>, so hopefully you can look past the awkwardness and pick up a quick tip to <strong>take your playing from sounding \"<em>schmo\" - </em>to sounding <em>pro.</em> </strong>\r\n\r\n<object width=\"480\" height=\"390\"><param name=\"movie\" value=\"https://www.youtube.com/v/rsw7r8MwWms?fs=1&amp;hl=en_US\"></param><param name=\"allowFullScreen\" value=\"true\"></param><param name=\"allowscriptaccess\" value=\"always\"></param><embed src=\"https://www.youtube.com/v/rsw7r8MwWms?fs=1&amp;hl=en_US\" type=\"application/x-shockwave-flash\" allowscriptaccess=\"always\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" width=\"480\" height=\"390\"></embed></object>',	'Bend Notes Without Sounding Like a Student',	'',	'draft',	'open',	'open',	'',	'bend-notes-without-sounding-like-a-student',	'',	'',	'2016-05-22 20:55:53',	'2016-05-23 03:55:53',	'',	0,	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//?p=2011',	0,	'post',	'',	1,	0),
