(4716,	1,	'2013-10-17 22:44:04',	'0000-00-00 00:00:00',	'Hello Shelley,\n<div></div>\n<div>I agree that bebop is not the end-all-be-all of music, especially now that it\'s over 60 years after the advent of that style- it\'s definitely time to move on! But it\'s also my own opinion, that if you really want to create jazz music of any depth, that you must have the ability to navigate with relative ease and agility over standard jazz chord progressions. You don\'t need to know the exact bebop vocabulary of Charlie Parker and Dizzy Gillespie, per se, but if you can\'t clearly outline the chord changes in your solos, I think you are missing the boat and will have a challenge creating beautiful compelling improvised melodies that will affect people the way that modern folks like David Sanborn and Kirk Whalum do, both of them being great straight-ahead players too. Bebop gives you the foundation that you need in order to be a great jazz musician.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>So yes, bebop doesn\'t need to be the end goal, but as far as I see it, bebop must not be overlooked in one\'s development in becoming a well-rounded jazz musician. Once you can do the bebop stuff, that you have a wide canvas from which to pull simpler catchy melodies. I mean, who\'s catchier than Herbie Hancock, and he\'s one of the greatest straight ahead piano players ever to live?</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>Otherwise, great work on the video, I like the way you went into that last chord and what you played over it, very cool.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>All the best</div>\n<div>\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\n<div><b><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> </span></b></div>\n<b><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Doron Orenstein</span></b><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">\n</span><b><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><i>Best. Saxophone. Website. Ever.</i></span></b>\n<div><b><span style=\"color: #333399;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><a href=\"https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.<wbr />BestSaxophoneWebsiteEver.com</a></span></span></b></div>\n<div><span style=\"color: #333399;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><a href=\"https://www.jazzlessonswithgiants.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.<wbr />JazzLessonsWithGiants.com</a>\n<a href=\"https://www.bulletproofsaxophoneplaying.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.<wbr />BulletproofSaxophonePlaying.<wbr />com</a></span></span></div>\n<div>\n<div><b><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><a href=\"tel:323.252.3122\" target=\"_blank\">323.252.3122</a></span></b></div>\n<div><b><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"> </span></b></div>\n</div>\n<div><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/bestsaxophonewebsiteever\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//wp-content/uploads/facebook.png\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://plus.google.com/b/102506078269530327855/102506078269530327855/posts\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//wp-content/uploads/googleplus.png\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://www.twitter.com/bestsaxophonewe\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//wp-content/uploads/twitter.png\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/bestsaxophonewe\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//wp-content/uploads/youtube.png\" /></a>  <a href=\"https://www.myspace.com/bestsaxophonewebsiteever\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//wp-content/uploads/myspace1.png\" /></a></span></span>&nbsp;\n\n</div>\n<div><b><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Newsletter</span></b><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">: </span><a href=\"https://eepurl.com/bcvb-/\" target=\"_blank\">https://eepurl.com/<wbr />bcvb-/</a></div>\n<div><span style=\"font-family: georgia, serif;\"><b> </b></span></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div>\n<div id=\":2w8\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" data-tooltip=\"Hide expanded content\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/images/cleardot.gif\" /></div>\n</div>\n<div>\n<div></div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>On Tue, Oct 1, 2013 at 1:52 PM, Donna Shelley &lt;<a href=\"mailto:genr8torx@comcast.net\" target=\"_blank\">genr8torx@comcast.net</a>&gt; wrote:\n<blockquote>From: Donna Shelley &lt;<a href=\"mailto:genr8torx@comcast.net\" target=\"_blank\">genr8torx@comcast.net</a>&gt;\nSubject: bebop/melodies etc\n\nMessage Body:\nYour site is great! But I do have one concern that has bugged me over the years.  That is: that everyone lionizes the bebop player above all else.  All the exercises and techniques I\'ve seen make the player zip thru the music with fantastic speed and agility  and everyone goes...ahhhh he\'s great.  Honestly I have found those exercises not useful in making my music.  I am a writer who when I compose a sax part I have the \"head\" like everyone else, but when I go into the \"jam\" I create new and delicious bits of melody...not just spitting out the endless \"exercises\" that make every bop sax player sound like every other bop sax player.   I have lines that people can walk out the door humming.  I\'ve never heard people humming the bip/bop/dip/dop kind of stuff.  What happened to memorable melodic music?  It\'s hard to create endless melodies that are interesting....it\'s not hard to memorize exercises.  Yet no one seems to care about making \"great music\".  I don\'t get it.  If you listen to one of my pieces (Mojito) you will see what I am saying.  Tell me if I\'m wrong or if I\'m going down the wrong path.\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qjEufd4Bjvo\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?<wbr />v=qjEufd4Bjvo</a></blockquote>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>',	'Do I need to know bebop',	'',	'draft',	'open',	'open',	'',	'',	'',	'',	'2013-10-17 22:44:04',	'2013-10-18 05:44:04',	'',	0,	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local//?p=4716',	0,	'post',	'',	0,	0),
