(6333,	1,	'2018-01-05 10:00:52',	'2018-01-05 16:00:52',	'Making large intervallic jumps is not something that comes naturally to most of us sax players, yet, being able to get around the horn fluently gives our playing a new dimension of polish and power. In this article, Jon De Lucia offers some challenging but fun exercises that will push you in ways that you would never be pushed by exercises and etudes written expressly for the saxophone. Sheet music is included.',	'Using Intervallic Studies from Bach’s Toccata and Fugue for Technique and Flexibility',	'',	'publish',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'making-large-intervallic-jumps-is-not-something-that-comes-naturally-to-most-of-us-sax-players-yet-being-able-to-get-around-the-horn-fluently-gives-our-playing-a-new-dimension-of-polish-and',	'',	'',	'2018-01-08 13:00:12',	'2018-01-08 19:00:12',	'',	0,	'https://bestsaxophonewebsiteevercom.local/nxs_qp/making-large-intervallic-jumps-is-not-something-that-comes-naturally-to-most-of-us-sax-players-yet-being-able-to-get-around-the-horn-fluently-gives-our-playing-a-new-dimension-of-polish-and/',	0,	'nxs_qp',	'',	0,	0),
