(326,	17,	'first_name',	'Bill'),
(327,	17,	'last_name',	'Plake'),
(328,	17,	'nickname',	'billplake'),
(329,	17,	'description',	'Having played professionally for the past 35 years, Bill Plake is a saxophonist, flutist and composer, and an Alexander Technique teacher certified by the American Society for the Alexander Technique (AmSAT). He\'s performed with musicians such as Vinny Golia, Charlie Haden, Nels and Alex Cline, and and Kim Richmond to name just a few.  Bill is on the faculty of the American Musical and Dramatic Academy in Los Angeles, teaching the Alexander Technique to actors, singers and dancers. He also teaches the Alexander Technique as a guest lecturer and adjunct at California Institute of the Arts, and Pomona College.  More on bill at BillPlakeMusic.org.'),
