(727,	36,	'nickname',	'warrenkeller'),
(728,	36,	'first_name',	'Warren'),
(729,	36,	'last_name',	'Keller'),
(730,	36,	'description',	'Warren began his musical journey as a classical clarinetist, transitioning to tenor, alto, bari sax, and flute in his teens. Flirting lightly with jazz over the years, he played and sang rock, funk, and blues professionally for twenty five years on the Jersey Shore, and in New York City and Nashville. He\'s had the privilege of playing with members of the following acts: David Bowie, Billy Idol, Flo &amp; Eddie, The Sweet, Blondie, and Los Straitjackets, and also with Larry Herbstritt, and Steve Addabbo. After a long hiatus, he recommitted himself to jazz tenor and flute in 2015.'),
